helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145136				0	sk	Converts a string comparison or numeric comparison to a Boolean expression, or converts a single numeric expression to a Boolean expression.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153345				0	sk	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149514				0	sk	CBool (Expression1 {= | <> | < | > | <= | >=} Expression2) or CBool (Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156152				0	sk	Return value:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419				0	sk	Bool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147530				0	sk	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156344				0	sk	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any string or numeric expressions that you want to compare. If the expressions match, the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function returns \<emph\>True\</emph\>, otherwise \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149655				0	sk	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that you want to convert. If the expression equals 0, \<emph\>False\</emph\> is returned, otherwise \<emph\>True\</emph\> is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	sk	The following example uses the \<emph\>CBool\</emph\> function to evaluate the value that is returned by the \<emph\>Instr\</emph\> function. The function checks if the word "and" is found in the sentence that was entered by the user.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156212				0	sk	Príklad:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3147288				0	sk	Sub ExampleCBool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sk	Dim sText As String				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132				0	sk	sText = InputBox("Please enter a short sentence:")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	sk	REM Proof if the word »and« appears in the sentence.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3146984				0	sk	REM Instead of the command line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sk	REM If Instr(Input, "and")<>0 Then...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	sk	REM the CBool function is applied as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3155413				0	sk	If CBool(Instr(sText, "and")) Then				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152940				0	sk	MsgBox "The word »and« appears in the sentence you entered!"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	sk	EndIf				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03100100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152886				0	sk	End Sub				20200411 15:09:53
