helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3155341				0	sk	Enables an object to be addressed at run-time as a string parameter through the object name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	sk	For example, the following command:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3148473				0	sk	MyObj.Prop1.Command = 5				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	sk	corresponds to the command block:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153896				0	sk	Dim ObjVar as Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154760				0	sk	Dim ObjProp as Object				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	sk	ObjName As String = "MyObj"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154939				0	sk	ObjVar = FindObject( ObjName As String )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3150793				0	sk	PropName As String = "Prop1"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3154141				0	sk	ObjProp = FindPropertyObject( ObjVar, PropName As String )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	sk	ObjProp.Command = 5				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	sk	This allows names to be dynamically created at run-time. For example:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03103800.xhp	0	help	par_id3153104				0	sk	"TextEdit1" to TextEdit5" in a loop to create five control names.				20200411 15:09:53
