helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03010103.xhp\" name=\"Print Statement [Runtime]\"\>Print Statement [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	sk	Outputs the specified strings or numeric expressions to a dialog or to a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145785				0	sk	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153188	4			0	sk	Print [#FileName,] Expression1[{;|,} [Spc(Number As Integer);] [Tab(pos As Integer);] [Expression2[...]] 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147348				0	sk	Parameter:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id2508621				0	sk	\<emph\>FileName:\</emph\> Any numeric expression that contains the file number that was set by the Open statement for the respective file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3163712				0	sk	\<emph\>Expression\</emph\>: Any numeric or string expression to be printed. Multiple expressions can be separated by a semicolon. If separated by a comma, the expressions are indented to the next tab stop. The tab stops cannot be adjusted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153092				0	sk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>: Number of spaces to be inserted by the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	sk	\<emph\>Pos\</emph\>: Spaces are inserted until the specified position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sk	If a semicolon or comma appears after the last expression to be printed, $[officename] Basic stores the text in an internal buffer and continues program execution without printing. When another Print statement without a semicolon or comma at the end is encountered, all text to be printed is printed at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	sk	Positive numeric expressions are printed with a leading space. Negative expressions are printed with a leading minus sign. If a certain range is exceeded for floating-point values, the respective numeric expression is printed in exponential notation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	sk	If the expression to be printed exceeds a certain length, the display will automatically wrap to the next line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03010103.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	sk	You can insert the Tab function, enclosed by semicolons, between arguments to indent the output to a specific position, or you can use the \<emph\>Spc\</emph\> function to insert a specified number of spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
