helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156344				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03060200.xhp\" name=\"Eqv Operator [Runtime]\"\>Eqv Operator [Runtime]\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	sk	Calculates the logical equivalence of two expressions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154367				0	sk	Syntax:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154910				0	sk	Result = Expression1 Eqv Expression2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151043				0	sk	Parameters:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	sk	\<emph\>Result:\</emph\> Any numeric variable that contains the result of the comparison.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3150448				0	sk	\<emph\>Expression1, Expression2:\</emph\> Any expressions that you want to compare.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562				0	sk	When testing for equivalence between Boolean expressions, the result is \<emph\>True\</emph\> if both expressions are either \<emph\>True\</emph\> or \<emph\>False\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03060200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sk	In a bit-wise comparison, the Eqv operator only sets the corresponding bit in the result if a bit is set in both expressions, or in neither expression.				20200411 15:09:53
