helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	sk	This section describes how to assign Basic programs to program events.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	sk	You can automatically execute a macro when a specified software event occurs by assigning the desired macro to the event. The following table provides an overview of program events and at what point an assigned macro is executed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	sk	Udalosť				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	sk	An assigned macro is executed...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	sk	Program Start				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\01040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	sk	... after a $[officename] application is started.				20200411 15:09:53
