helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148668				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>margins; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; setting with the mouse\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; indents, margins and columns\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148668				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/13020000.xhp\" name=\"Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\"\>Setting Indents, Margins, and Columns\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155364				0	sk	You can define the indents and margins for the current paragraph, or for all selected paragraphs, using the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3152594				0	sk	If you split the page into columns, or the cursor is placed in a multiple-column text frame, you can change the column width and the column spacing by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154398				0	sk	When an object, an image, or a draw object is selected, you will see the borders of the object in the ruler. You can change the borders by dragging them on the ruler with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146130				0	sk	If the cursor is placed in a table cell, you can change the indents for the contents of the cell by dragging them with the mouse on the ruler. You can change the boundary lines of the table on the ruler or by dragging the actual boundary line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156136				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3153750\" src=\"res/helpimg/linleft.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.2291inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3153750\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	sk	These icons mark the left indent for the first line of the current paragraph (top triangle) and the left indent for the other lines of the paragraph (bottom triangle).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150774				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3145071\" src=\"res/helpimg/linright.png\" width=\"0.3646inch\" height=\"0.2602inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145071\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sk	This icon on the right of the ruler marks the right indent of the current paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\13020000.xhp	0	help	par_id3146949				0	sk	\<emph\>Task\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
