helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Výber				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151299				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/18010000.xhp\" name=\"Selection\"\>Selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3148520				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:SelectObject\"\>Allows you to select objects in the current document.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149511				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3159194\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_drawselect.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3159194\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3147571				0	sk	Výber				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	sk	To select an object, click the object with the arrow. To select more than one object, drag a selection frame around the objects. To add an object to a selection, press Shift, and then click the object. \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>The objects selected together can then be defined as a \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05290000.xhp\" name=\"group\"\>group\</link\>, turning them into a single group object.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can edit individual elements of a group. You can also delete elements from a group with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Shift\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+click.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\18010000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166460				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CHART\"\>\</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"MATH\"\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>You can select single objects from a group by double-clicking, if you first disable the \<emph\>Double-click to edit Text\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Option\</emph\> Bar.\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850				0	sk	Special Tips for Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539				0	sk	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372				0	sk	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	sk	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616				0	sk	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	sk	Vložiť stĺpec				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552				0	sk	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827				0	sk	Nahradiť za				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267				0	sk	Zmazať stĺpec				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275				0	sk	Stĺpec				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	sk	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539				0	sk	Skryť stĺpce				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771				0	sk	Zobraziť stĺpce				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	sk	Viac				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561				0	sk	Všetko				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349				0	sk	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416				0	sk	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062				0	sk	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510				0	sk	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758				0	sk	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657				0	sk	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	sk	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	sk	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	sk	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	sk	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Standard Filter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12090100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151097				0	sk	Standard Filter				20200411 15:09:53
