helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	sk	Not all printers can print a paper up to its edges. Most of them leave an unprinted margin.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182				0	sk	$[officename] offers a semi-automatic feature that enables you to print as close to the paper's edge as is possible.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	sk	Make sure that your printer has been setup under \<emph\>File - Printer Settings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	sk	Make sure that the \<emph\>Web Layout\</emph\> in the \<emph\>View\</emph\> menu is not selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147653				0	sk	Select the \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\> command, and go to the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	sk	Under \<emph\>Margins\</emph\> you can define the maximum or minimum possible value for the page margins (left, right, top, and bottom). Click into the respective control, then press the Page Up or Page Down key. The preview displays a dashed line around the printable range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\pageformat_max.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
