helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491971				0	sk	One example of differences between Calc and Excel is the handling of boolean values. Enter TRUE to cells A1 and A2. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491973				0	sk	In Calc, the formula =A1+A2 returns the value 2, and the formula =SUM(A1;A2) returns 2. 				20200411 15:09:53
