helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	sk	You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_tabledefine.xhp\"\>Table Design\</link\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10778				0	sk	Creating a New Table View				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077C				0	sk	Some database types support table views. A table view is a query that is stored with the database. For most database operations, a view can be used as you would use a table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10782				0	sk	Open the database file where you want to create the new table view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	sk	In the left pane of the database window, click the \<emph\>Tables\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
