helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	bm_id4724570				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>databases;registering (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>registering;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>deleting;databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>databases;deleting (Base)\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;registered databases (Base)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105A3				0	sk	\<variable id=\"data_register\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/data_register.xhp\"\>Registering and Deleting a Database\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C1				0	sk	Data from any \<link href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/dabadoc.xhp\"\>database file\</link\> can be registered to %PRODUCTNAME. To register means to tell %PRODUCTNAME where the data is located, how it is organized, how to get that data, and more. Once the database is registered, you can use the menu command \<emph\>View - Data source\</emph\> to access the data records from your text documents and spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C8				0	sk	To register an existing database file:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CF				0	sk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105E1				0	sk	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\> and select the database file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	sk	To remove a registered database from %PRODUCTNAME				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10707				0	sk	Choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01160200.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Base - Databases\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN10719				0	sk	Select the database file and click \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F3				0	sk	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/explorer/database/main.xhp#base\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\data_register.xhp	0	help	par_idN105FB				0	sk	\<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/database_main.xhp#database_main\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting Hyperlinks				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150789				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>hypertextové odkazy; vkladanie\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>odkazy; vkladanie\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vkladanie; hypertextové odkazy\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789				0	sk	\<variable id=\"hyperlink_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/hyperlink_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149095				0	sk	You can insert hyperlinks in two ways: as text or as a button. In both cases, the visible text can be different from the URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153527	7			0	sk	Display the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> by choosing \<emph\>View - Toolbars - Hyperlink Bar\</emph\>. Type the visible text in the left field and the full URL in the right field, including http:// or file://.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811	8			0	sk	Place the text cursor in the document at the point where you want to insert the hyperlink. Click the\<emph\> Hyperlink\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\>. The hyperlink is inserted as text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	sk	If you want to insert the hyperlink as a button, click and hold the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>As Button\</emph\> from the sub-menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150275				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3149763\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_hyperlinkdialog.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149763\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3151385	30			0	sk	To use the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/09070000.xhp\" name=\"Hyperlink dialog\"\>Hyperlink dialog\</link\> instead of the \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>\<emph\>Bar\</emph\> to define the hyperlink, click the icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	23			0	sk	To jump to a specific line in a text document, first enter a bookmark at that position (\<emph\>Insert - Bookmark\</emph\>). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076D				0	sk	To jump to a cell in a spreadsheet, first enter a name for the cell (\<emph\>Insert - Names - Define\</emph\>).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144432				0	sk	In the \<emph\>URL\</emph\> combo box, enter only the short form of the URL when jumping within the same document: If the bookmark is called \<emph\>Target\</emph\>, enter \<emph\>Target\</emph\>. To jump to another document, enter the complete URL.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3152887				0	sk	Hyperlinks can also be inserted by drag-and-drop from the Navigator. Hyperlinks can refer to references, headings, graphics, tables, objects, directories or bookmarks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\hyperlink_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	sk	If you wish to insert in a text a hyperlink that refers to Table 1, drag the entry Table 1 from the Navigator and drop it in the text. To do this, the \<emph\>Insert as Hyperlink\</emph\> drag mode must be selected in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153394				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; copying between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; draw objects between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;draw objects from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153394				0	sk	\<variable id=\"copy_drawfunctions\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/copy_drawfunctions.xhp\" name=\"Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\"\>Copying Drawing Objects Into Other Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	28			0	sk	In $[officename] it is possible to copy drawing objects between text, spreadsheets and presentation documents. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	sk	Select the drawing object or objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426				0	sk	Copy the drawing object to the clipboard, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996				0	sk	Switch to the other document and place the cursor where the drawing object is to be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3149234				0	sk	Insert the drawing object, for example, by using \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147573				0	sk	Inserting into a text document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276				0	sk	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current paragraph. You can change the anchor by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>OLE-Object\</emph\> toolbar or the \<emph\>Frame\</emph\> toolbar. This opens a popup menu where you can select the anchor type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145609				0	sk	Inserting into a spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\copy_drawfunctions.xhp	0	help	par_id3151210	30			0	sk	An inserted drawing object is anchored to the current cell. You can change the anchor between cell and page by selecting the object and clicking the \<emph\>Change Anchor\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149456\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_toggleanchortype.png\" width=\"5.64mm\" height=\"5.64mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149456\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Configuring $[officename]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152801				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>configuring; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customizing; $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152801				0	sk	\<variable id=\"configure_overview\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/configure_overview.xhp\" name=\"Configuring $[officename]\"\>Configuring $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345				0	sk	You can customize your $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155421				0	sk	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Customize\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Customize\</emph\> dialog to change toolbars, menus and other user interface items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3145071				0	sk	You are free to change the items on the menu bar. You can delete items, add new ones, copy items from one menu to another, rename them, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	sk	The toolbars may be freely configured.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443				0	sk	You can change the shortcut keys.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3153345				0	sk	You can change default settings of $[officename] to suit your needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	optid3155421				0	sk	Use \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/010000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\>\</link\> to open the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> dialog to change a variety of settings you will use in $[officename] modules. Items presented in the \<emph\>Tools - Options\</emph\> menu will change depending on the module you are using.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3145071				0	sk	In \<link href=\"text/shared/guide/language_select.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Language Settings\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find options for your default language and currency setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3149811				0	sk	In \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040000.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - $[officename] Writer - Basic Fonts\</emph\>\</link\>, you will find default font settings. Change these to suit your preferences. Fonts can easily be changed on per document basis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3150443				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010900.xhp\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Options - Print\</emph\>\</link\> contains a number of print customizations that may be useful for your particular needs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	par_id3155388				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06140000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Customize\"\>Tools - Customize\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\configure_overview.xhp	0	help	opt3155388				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01000000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Options\"\>Tools - Options\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150502				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>ImageMap; editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editors; ImageMap editor\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>images; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pictures; ImageMap\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hotspots;adding to images\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>URL;in pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10631				0	sk	\<variable id=\"imagemap\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/imagemap.xhp\"\>Adding Clickable Hotspots to Images\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1064F				0	sk	An ImageMap allows you to attach URLs to specific areas, called hotspots, on a picture in your document. An image map is a group of one or more hotspots.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066C				0	sk	You can draw three types of hotspots: rectangles, ellipses, and polygons. When you click a hotspot, the URL is opened in the browser window or frame that you specify. You can also specify the text that appears when your mouse rests on the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10677				0	sk	To add a clickable hotspot to an image				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067E				0	sk	Position the cursor where you want the ImageMap in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>, select and insert a bitmap picture.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068A				0	sk	With the picture selected, choose \<emph\>Edit - ImageMap\</emph\>. You see the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02220000.xhp\"\>ImageMap Editor\</link\>, which displays the picture at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A0				0	sk	Use the icons in the ImageMap Editor to draw a hotspot shape, for example a rectangle, over the image at the background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	sk	You can see an extended help text on the functions of each icon when you enable Extended Help in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AB				0	sk	Enter the "Address" URL that will be shown in a Web browser when the user clicks the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	sk	Optionally, enter the "Text" that will be shown as a tip when the user points the mouse to the hotspot.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B3				0	sk	Click the Apply button to apply your changes, and close the ImageMap Editor.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106B7				0	sk	Save the document in the %PRODUCTNAME or HTML format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\imagemap.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BA				0	sk	You may save the ImageMap as a file and upload that file to a Web server, for example.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Turning Extended Tips On and Off				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156414				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>Help; extended tips on/off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>extended tips in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tips;extended tips in Help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tooltips;extended tips\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>activating;extended help tips\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156414				0	sk	\<variable id=\"active_help_on_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/active_help_on_off.xhp\" name=\"Turning Extended Tips On and Off\"\>Turning Extended Tips On and Off\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	sk	\<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\> provide a brief description of the function of a particular icon, text box or menu command when you rest your cursor on that item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155339				0	sk	To turn Extended Tips on and off:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - General\</emph\>, and check \<emph\>Extended tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3149398				0	sk	A check mark indicates that the extended tips are activated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149811				0	sk	To turn Extended Tips on temporarily:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153541				0	sk	Press the shortcut keys Shift+F1 to activate extended tips once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\active_help_on_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825				0	sk	A question mark appears beside the mouse pointer. You can move this \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> over all controls, icons and menu commands to obtain a description of the command. The \<emph\>Help Mouse Pointer\</emph\> is disabled the next time you click the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting and Editing Buttons				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149798				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>command buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>controls;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keys;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>buttons;adding push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>press buttons, see push buttons\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>push buttons;adding to documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149798				0	sk	\<variable id=\"formfields\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/formfields.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Buttons\"\>Adding a Command Button to a Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	sk	You can use the Form Controls toolbar to add checkboxes, buttons, tables showing data records, and other controls to a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077F				0	sk	To Add a Button to a Document 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154751				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>View - Toolbars - Form Controls\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145345				0	sk	On the Form Controls toolbar, click the \<emph\>Push Button\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A4				0	sk	The mouse pointer changes to a cross-hair.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3159233				0	sk	In the document, drag to draw the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B2				0	sk	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Control\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CD				0	sk	Specify the properties of the button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154923				0	sk	To change the button label, click the \<emph\>General\</emph\> tab, and edit the text in the \<emph\>Label\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147303	12			0	sk	To attach a macro to the button, click the \<emph\>Events\</emph\> tab, and click the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button beside the button action that you want to run the macro. In the \<emph\>Assign Macro\</emph\> dialog, locate the macro that you want to use, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10814				0	sk	Close the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147350				0	sk	(Optional) Specify the properties of the form that the button belongs to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\formfields.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	sk	Right-click the button and choose \<emph\>Form\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
