helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149234				0	sk	Restrict Files to Display				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3150985				0	sk	To restrict the display of files in the \<emph\>Open\</emph\> dialog to a certain type select the corresponding \<emph\>File type\</emph\> from the list. Select \<emph\>All Files (*.*)\</emph\> to display all files.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id4651326				0	sk	Cursor Position				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id5509201				0	sk	In general, all documents open with the cursor at the start of the document. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id6594744				0	sk	One exception appears when the author of a Writer text document saves and reopens a document: The cursor will be at the same position where it has been when the document was saved. This only works when the name of the author was entered in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME - User Data\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	par_id3422650				0	sk	Press Shift+F5 to set the cursor to the last saved position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\doc_open.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148453				0	sk	Opening an Empty Document				20200411 15:09:53
