helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Specifies the display options for guides.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057B				0	sk	Display Guides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN1057F				0	sk	Displays or hides guides that you can use to align objects on a page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN10582				0	sk	Snap to Guides				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN10586				0	sk	Automatically aligns objects to vertical and horizontal guides. To override this feature, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>when you drag an object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN105C6				0	sk	Vodiace čiary na popredie				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\guides.xhp	0	help	par_idN105CA				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Displays the guides in front of the objects on the slide or page.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	HTML import and export				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154380				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>importing; HTML with META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; to HTML\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML; importing META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; META tags in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>META tags\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tags; META tags\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154380				0	sk	HTML import and export				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	sk	When you export a file to an HTML document, the description and the user-defined file properties are included as META \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#tags\" name=\"tags\"\>tags\</link\> between the HEAD tags of the exported document. META tags are not displayed in a Web browser, and are used to include information, such as keywords for search engines on your Web page. To set the properties of the current document, choose \<emph\>File - Properties\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Description\</emph\> or \<emph\>User Defined\</emph\> tabs, and then type the information you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3148552				0	sk	The following file properties are converted to META tags when you export a file as an HTML document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154935				0	sk	File Property				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056				0	sk	<TITLE>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3153778				0	sk	Predmet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3147228				0	sk	<META NAME="CLASSIFICATION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3154908				0	sk	Kľúčové slová				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3156422				0	sk	<META NAME="KEYWORDS" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	sk	Popis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3125863				0	sk	<META NAME="DESCRIPTION" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159149				0	sk	Info fields 1...4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3157892				0	sk	<META NAME="Info field name" CONTENT="Field Content">				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855	22			0	sk	When you import an HTML containing these META tags, the contents of the tags are added to the corresponding $[officename] file property box. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id0926200812164481				0	sk	Keywords must be separated by commas. A keyword can contain white space characters or semicolons.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163822				0	sk	Import Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155307				0	sk	When you import an HTML document, following META tags are automatically converted to $[officename] fields: <META HTTP-EQUIV="REFRESH"...> and <META NAME="..." ...> , where NAME equals to AUTHOR, CREATED, CHANGED, CHANGEDBY, DESCRIPTION, KEYWORDS or CLASSIFICATION.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3146146				0	sk	Scripts, comments, and META tags that are positioned directly before a TABLE tag are inserted in the first cell of the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3155366				0	sk	Scripts and META tags in the header of an HTML document are imported and anchored to the first paragraph in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	sk	To set the options for importing HTML tags, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Load/Save - HTML Compatibility\</emph\>. A known META tag contains either "HTTP-EQUIV" or "NAME", and are imported as $[officename] comments. The only exception is <META NAME="GENERATOR"...>, which is ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	hd_id3163717				0	sk	Export Tips				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\about_meta_tags.xhp	0	help	par_id3159180				0	sk	Comments and script fields at the beginning of the first paragraph in a document are exported to the header of an HTML document. If the document begins with a table, the first paragraph in the first cell of the table is exported to the header of the HTML document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05020700.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Ázijská typografia				20200411 15:09:53
