helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02230300.xhp	0	help	par_id3148983				0	sk	\<variable id=\"kommentartext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\"HID_REDLINING_EDIT\"\>Enter a comment for the recorded change.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02230300.xhp	0	help	par_id3155391	3			0	sk	You can attach a comment when \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>the cursor is in a changed text passage \</caseinline\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>the changed cell is selected\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>, or in the \<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02230300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156426	5			0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>Comments are displayed as callouts in the sheet when you rest your mouse pointer over a cell with a recorded change. You can also view comments that are attached to a changed cell in the changes list in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02230400.xhp\" name=\"Accept or Reject Changes\"\>\<emph\>Accept or Reject Changes\</emph\>\</link\> dialog. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	List of Regular Expressions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146765				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>regular expressions; list of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>replacing;tab stops (regular expressions)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tab stops;regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>concatenation, see ampersand symbol\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>ampersand symbol, see also operators\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146765				0	sk	\<variable id=\"02100001\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\"\>Zoznam regulárnych výrazov\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149741				0	sk	Character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	sk	Result/Use				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6600543				0	sk	Any character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9824518.00000001				0	sk	Represents the given character unless otherwise specified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152427				0	sk	.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149031				0	sk	Represents any single character except for a line break or paragraph break. For example, the search term "sh.rt" returns both "shirt" and "short".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154682				0	sk	^				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155351				0	sk	Only finds the search term if the term is at the beginning of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames, at the beginning of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "^Peter".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194				0	sk	$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152542				0	sk	Only finds the search term if the term appears at the end of a paragraph. Special objects such as empty fields or character-anchored frames at the end of a paragraph are ignored. Example: "Peter$".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156414				0	sk	*				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155555				0	sk	Nájde nula alebo viac znakov pred "*". Napríklad "Ab*c" nájde "Ac", "Abc", "Abbc", "Abbbc" atď.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147399				0	sk	+				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958				0	sk	Finds one or more of the characters in front of the "+". For example, "AX.+4" finds "AXx4", but not "AX4".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145313				0	sk	The longest possible string that matches this search pattern in a paragraph is always found. If the paragraph contains the string "AX 4 AX4", the entire passage is highlighted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267				0	sk	?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153684				0	sk	Finds zero or one of the characters in front of the "?". For example, "Texts?" finds "Text" and "Texts" and "x(ab|c)?y" finds "xy", "xaby", or "xcy".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3166410				0	sk	\\				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209				0	sk	Zvláštny znak, ktorý nasleduje po "\\", sa interpretuje ako normálny znak a nie ako regulárny výraz (okrem kombinácií\\n, \\t, \\> a \\<). Napríklad "tree\\." nájde "tree.", ale nie "treed" alebo "trees".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152945				0	sk	\\n				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153700				0	sk	Represents a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination. To change a line break into a paragraph break, enter \<emph\>\\n\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> and \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> boxes, and then perform a search and replace.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9262672				0	sk	\\n in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box stands for a line break that was inserted with the Shift+Enter key combination.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2366100				0	sk	\\n in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> text box stands for a paragraph break that can be entered with the Enter or Return key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153258				0	sk	\\t				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3157809				0	sk	Represents a tab. You can also use this expression in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150670				0	sk	\\b				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666				0	sk	Match a word boundary. For example, "\\bbook" finds "bookmark" but not "checkbook" whereas "book\\b" finds "checkbook" but not "bookmark". The discrete word "book" is found by both search terms.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149576				0	sk	^$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	sk	Finds an empty paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148550				0	sk	^.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159413				0	sk	Finds the first character of a paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	sk	& or $0				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153961				0	sk	Adds the string that was found by the search criteria in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box to the term in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box when you make a replacement.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149650				0	sk	For example, if you enter "window" in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box and "&frame" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, the word "window" is replaced with "windowframe".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150543				0	sk	You can also enter an "&" in the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box to modify the \<emph\>Attributes\</emph\> or the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> of the string found by the search criteria.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419				0	sk	[abc123]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154630				0	sk	Represents one of the characters that are between the brackets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156293				0	sk	[a-e]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149167				0	sk	Represents any of the characters that are between a and e, including both start and end characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id100520090232005				0	sk	The characters are ordered by their code numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155994				0	sk	[a-eh-x]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148676				0	sk	Represents any of the characters that are between a-e and h-x.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145318				0	sk	[^a-s]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153351				0	sk	Represents everything that is not between a and s.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156543				0	sk	\\xXXXX				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sk	Represents a special character based on its four-digit hexadecimal code (XXXX).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3159252				0	sk	The code for the special character depends on the font used. You can view the codes by choosing \<emph\>Insert - Special Character\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	sk	|				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154985				0	sk	Finds the terms that occur before the "|" and also finds the terms that occur after the "|". For example, "this|that" finds "this" and "that".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147376				0	sk	{2}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103				0	sk	Defines the number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket occurs. For example, "tre{2}" finds and selects "tree".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3151289				0	sk	{1,2}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147317				0	sk	Defines the minimum and maximum number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{1,2}" finds and selects "tre" and "tree".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4870754				0	sk	{1,}				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id843836				0	sk	Defines the minimum number of times that the character in front of the opening bracket can occur. For example, "tre{2,}" finds "tree", "treee", and "treeeee".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	sk	( )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2701803				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	sk	Defines the characters inside the parentheses as a reference. You can then refer to the first reference in the current expression with "\\1", to the second reference with "\\2", and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3156061				0	sk	For example, if your text contains the number 13487889 and you search using the regular expression (8)7\\1\\1, "8788" is found.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	sk	You can also use () to group terms, for example, "a(bc)?d" finds "ad" or "abcd".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9200109				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5766472				0	sk	Use $ (dollar) instead of \\ (backslash) to replace references. Use $0 to replace the whole found string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3154790				0	sk	[:alpha:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3147397				0	sk	Represents an alphabetic character. Use [:alpha:]+ to find one or more of them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	sk	[:digit:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	Represents a decimal digit. Use [:digit:]+ to find one or more of them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153743				0	sk	[:alnum:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153281				0	sk	Represents an alphanumeric character ([:alpha:] and [:digit:]).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	sk	[:space:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	sk	Represents a space character (but not other whitespace characters).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150486				0	sk	[:print:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150872				0	sk	Represents a printable character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	sk	[:cntrl:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	sk	Represents a nonprinting character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	sk	[:lower:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3145730				0	sk	Represents a lowercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3148455				0	sk	[:upper:]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id3150092	231			0	sk	Represents an uppercase character if \<emph\>Match case\</emph\> is selected in \<emph\>Options.\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id5311441				0	sk	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id956834773				0	sk	e([:digit:])?    -- finds 'e' followed by zero or one digit. Note that currently all named character classes like [:digit:] must be enclosed in parentheses.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id952368773				0	sk	^([:digit:])$    -- finds lines or cells with exactly one digit.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id9568773				0	sk	You can combine the search terms to form complex searches.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	hd_id71413				0	sk	To find three-digit numbers alone in a paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id2924283				0	sk	^[:digit:]{3}$				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5781731				0	sk	^ means the match has to be at the start of a paragraph, 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id6942045				0	sk	[:digit:] matches any decimal digit, 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id4721823				0	sk	{3} means there must be exactly 3 copies of "digit", 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5806756				0	sk	$ means the match must end a paragraph. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id1751457				0	sk	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Regular_Expressions_in_Writer\"\>Wiki page about regular expressions in Writer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\02100001.xhp	0	help	par_id5483870				0	sk	\<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Regular_Expressions_in_Calc\"\>Wiki page about regular expressions in Calc\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
