helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3156027				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FORMAT_HEADER\"\>Adds a header to the current page style. A header is an area in the top page margin, where you can add text or graphics.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3150693				0	sk	If you want, you can also add borders or a background fill to a header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153821	32			0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WRITER\"\>To add a header to the current page style, select \<emph\>Header on\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3153827				0	sk	If you want to extend a header into the page margins, insert a frame into the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\05040300.xhp	0	help	par_id3154046				0	sk	To quickly move the text cursor from the document text to the header or footer, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down. Press the same key again to move the text cursor back into the document text.				20200411 15:09:53
