helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id102620090953596				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Allows to use the same field name for multiple fields in the generated PDF file. If disabled, field names will be exported using generated unique names.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3946958				0	sk	Export automatically inserted blank pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id8551896				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>If switched on, automatically inserted blank pages are being exported to pdf file. This is best if you are printing the pdf file double-sided. Example: In a book a chapter paragraph style is set to always start with an odd numbered page. The previous chapter ends on an odd page. %PRODUCTNAME inserts an even numbered blank page. This option controls whether to export that even numbered page or not.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id3954548				0	sk	Embed standard fonts				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id853434896				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Normally the 14 standard Postscript fonts are not embedded in a PDF file, because every PDF reader software already contains these fonts. Enable this option to embed the standard fonts that are installed on your system and that are used in the document.\</ahelp\> Use this option if you expect to have a better looking or more useful standard font than the font that is available in the recipients' PDF reader software.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	hd_id080420080355360				0	sk	Embed this document inside the PDF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\01\ref_pdf_export.xhp	0	help	par_id0804200803553767				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>The document being exported will be embedded inside the PDF file.\</ahelp\> Some PDF tools or %PRODUCTNAME extensions may allow to extract the file from the PDF and save it; in this way, the original %PRODUCTNAME document can be edited back without the need of a PDF editing application.				20200411 15:09:53
