helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154338				0	sk	Maticový zásobník				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3146941				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_MATRIX\"\>This icon inserts a matrix with four placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>matrix{<?>#<?>##<?>#<?>}\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The position of an element inside this diagram is indicated by two coordinates; the first specifies the line number and the second the column number. You can expand this matrix in any direction in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window by adding characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN103C9				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3150027\" src=\"starmath/res/co21903.png\" width=\"0.3335inch\" height=\"0.3335inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150027\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149358				0	sk	Voľný priestor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149370				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SMA_BLANK\"\>This icon inserts a gap or space between placeholders.\</ahelp\> You can also type \<emph\>~\</emph\> directly in the \<emph\>Commands\</emph\> window. The command must appear to the left or right of a symbol, variable, number or complete command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155394	48			0	sk	For alignment, the \<emph\>alignl, alignc\</emph\> and \<emph\>alignr\</emph\> commands are especially effective, if you are 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3151009				0	sk	aligning numerators and denominators, for example \<emph\>{alignl a}over{b+c}\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148812				0	sk	constructing binomials or stacks, for example \<emph\>binom{2*n}{alignr k}\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	sk	aligning the elements in a matrix, for example \<emph\>matrix{alignr a#b+2##c+1/3#alignl d}\</emph\> and				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155946				0	sk	beginning a new line, for example \<emph\>a+b-c newline alignr x/y\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154621				0	sk	Ak použijete príkazy na zoradenie, všimnite si, že				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3147382				0	sk	they can only placed at the beginning of expressions and can only occur once. Therefore you can type \<emph\>a+b alignr c\</emph\>, but not \<emph\>a+alignr b\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3154004				0	sk	they affect each other, which means that typing \<emph\>{alignl{alignr a}}over{b+c}\</emph\> aligns \<emph\>a\</emph\> on the right.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	hd_id8036133				0	sk	To align using the "matrix" command				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_idN10F70				0	sk	Zarovnať doľava				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149645				0	sk	If a line or an expression begins with text, it is aligned on the left by default. You can change this with any of the \<emph\>align\</emph\> commands. An example is \<emph\>stack{a+b-c*d#alignr "text"}\</emph\>, where "text" appears aligned to the right. Note that text must always be surrounded by quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3149966				0	sk	The standard centralized formulas can be aligned to the left without using the \<emph\>Format - Alignment\</emph\> menu. To do this, place an empty character string, that is, the inverted commas which surround any text "", before the section of formula that you want to align. For example, typing \<emph\>"" a+b newline "" c+d\</emph\> results in both equations being left-aligned instead of centered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3145654				0	sk	Ak napíšete informácie v príkazovom okne, všimnite si, že niektoré formáty vyžadujú medzery pre korektnú štruktúru. To je obzvlášť potrebné, ak zapisujete hodnoty (napríklad, a lsup{3}) namiesto zástupných znakov.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3148708				0	sk	Click \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091100.xhp\" name=\"Brackets and Grouping\"\>Brackets and Grouping\</link\> for more information about formatting in \<emph\>$[officename] Math\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\smath\01\03090700.xhp	0	help	par_id3155340				0	sk	Useful information about \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091200.xhp\" name=\"Indexes and Exponents\"\>Indexes and Exponents\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/smath/01/03091400.xhp\" name=\"Scaling\"\>Scaling\</link\>, helps you organize your document in the best possible way.				20200411 15:09:53
