helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9449446				0	sk	Legenda				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8122196				0	sk	Visible grid lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9909665				0	sk	For additional elements use the Insert menu of the chart in edit mode. There you can define the following elements:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id9141819				0	sk	Sekundárne osi				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6354869				0	sk	Vedľajšie mriežky				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2685323				0	sk	Data labels				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id6042664				0	sk	Statistics, for example mean values, y error bars and trend lines				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_column_line.xhp	0	help	par_id7889950				0	sk	To set different data labels for each data series, use the properties dialog of the data series.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Chart Type Line				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id2187566				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>line charts\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>chart types;line\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9422894				0	sk	\<variable id=\"type_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/schart/01/type_line.xhp\"\>Chart Type Line\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id389721				0	sk	On the first page of the \<link href=\"text/schart/01/wiz_chart_type.xhp\"\>Chart Wizard\</link\> you can choose a chart type. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id9826349				0	sk	Úsečka				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2334665				0	sk	A line chart shows values as points on the y axis. The x axis shows categories. The y values of each data series can be connected by a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8956572				0	sk	Points only - this subtype plots only points.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id500808				0	sk	Points and lines - this subtype plots points and connects points of the same data series by a line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id8366649				0	sk	Lines only - this subtype plots only lines.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id476393				0	sk	3D lines - this subtype connects points of the same data series by a 3D line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id2655720				0	sk	Mark \<emph\>Stack series\</emph\> to arrange the points' y values cumulative above each other. The y values no longer represent absolute values, except for the first column which is drawn at the bottom of the stacked points. If you select \<emph\>Percent\</emph\>, the y values are scaled as percentage of the category total.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\type_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3682058				0	sk	Mark \<emph\>Smooth lines\</emph\> to draw curves through the points instead of straight lines. Click \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> for a \<link href=\"text/schart/01/smooth_line_properties.xhp\"\>dialog\</link\> to change the curves' properties.				20200411 15:09:53
