helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/05040201.xhp\" name=\"Scale\"\>Scale\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	sk	Controls the scaling of the X or Y axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sk	The axes are automatically scaled by $[officename] so that all values are optimally displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	sk	To achieve specific results, you can manually change the axis scaling. For example, you can display only the top areas of the columns by shifting the zero line upwards.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154730				0	sk	Scale				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sk	You can enter values for subdividing axes in this area. You can automatically set the properties \<emph\>Minimum, Maximum, Major interval, Minor interval count\</emph\> and \<emph\>Reference value\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150751				0	sk	Minimum				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153713				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MIN\"\>Defines the minimum value for the beginning of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156385				0	sk	Maximum				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3159266				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_MAX\"\>Defines the maximum value for the end of the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155336				0	sk	Major interval				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3143218				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_MAIN\"\>Defines the interval for the main division of the axes.\</ahelp\> The main interval cannot be larger than the value area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154020				0	sk	Minor interval count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_STEP_HELP\"\>Defines the interval for the subdivision of the axes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150089				0	sk	Reference value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH_SPINFIELD_TP_SCALE_EDT_ORIGIN\"\>Specifies at which position to display the values along the axis.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3166432				0	sk	Automaticky				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145389				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_AUTO_ORIGIN\"\>You must first deselect the \<emph\>Automatic\</emph\> option in order to modify the values.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3149129				0	sk	Disable this feature if you are working with "fixed" values, as it does not permit automatic scaling.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159206				0	sk	Logaritmická mierka				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3145360				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:TP_SCALE:CBX_LOGARITHM\"\>Specifies that you want the axis to be subdivided logarithmically.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3153956				0	sk	Use this feature if you are working with values that differ sharply from each other. You can use logarithmic scaling to make the grid lines of the axis equidistant but have values that may increase or decrease.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id9941404				0	sk	Reverse direction				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id5581835				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Defines where the lower and where the higher values are displayed at the axis. The unchecked state is the mathematical direction.\</ahelp\> That means for Cartesian coordinate systems that the x-axis shows the lower values on the left and the y-axis shows the lower values at the bottom. For polar coordinate systems the mathematical angle axis direction is counterclockwise and the radial axis is from inner to outer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	hd_id922204				0	sk	Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id59225				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>For some types of axes, you can select to format an axis as text or date, or to detect the type automatically.\</ahelp\> For the axis type "Date" you can set the following options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id1159225				0	sk	Minimum and maximum value to be shown on the ends of the scale.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id2259225				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Resolution can be set to show days, months, or years as interval steps.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id3359225				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Major interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\05040201.xhp	0	help	par_id4459225				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Minor interval can be set to show a certain number of days, months, or years.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
