helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	sk	Secondary axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3166428				0	sk	Use this area to assign a second axis to your chart. If a data series is already assigned to this axis, $[officename] automatically displays the axis and the label. You can turn off these settings later on. If no data has been assigned to this axis and you activate this area, the values of the primary Y axis are applied to the secondary axis.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152988				0	sk	X axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3156445				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_X_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary X axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152896				0	sk	Y axis				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153818				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>Displays a secondary Y axis in the chart.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04040000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154762	41			0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:CHECKBOX:DLG_AXIS:CB_Y_SECONDARY\"\>The major axis and the secondary axis can have different scaling. For example, you can scale one axis to 2 in. and the other to 1.5 in. \</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Y chybové panely				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147428				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/schart/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Y Error Bars\"\>Y Error Bars\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149666				0	sk	\<variable id=\"statistik\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Use the \<emph\>Y Error Bars\</emph\> dialog to display error bars for 2D charts.\</ahelp\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3401287				0	sk	An error bar is an indicator line that spans over a range from y - NegativeErrorValue to y + PositiveErrorValue. In this term, y is the value of the data point. When "standard deviation" is selected, y is the mean value of the data series. NegativeErrorValue and PositiveErrorValue are the amounts calculated by the error bar function or given explicitly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	sk	The \<emph\>Insert - Y Error Bars\</emph\> menu command is only available for 2D charts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150344				0	sk	Chybová kategória				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Error category\</emph\> area, you can choose different ways to display the error category.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152989				0	sk	Žiadne				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"SCH:RADIOBUTTON:TP_STAT:RBT_NONE\"\>Does not show any error bars.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\schart\01\04050000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145117				0	sk	Konštantná hodnota				20200411 15:09:53
