helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	sk	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	sk	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	sk	Running a slide show from a file				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	sk	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	sk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	sk	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20200411 15:09:53
