helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	User-Defined Functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>functions; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Basic IDE for user-defined functions\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>IDE; Basic IDE\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>programming;functions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	sk	\<variable id=\"userdefined_function\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/userdefined_function.xhp\" name=\"Defining Functions Yourself\"\>User-Defined Functions\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153969				0	sk	You can apply user-defined functions in $[officename] Calc in the following ways:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145366				0	sk	You can define your own functions using the Basic-IDE. This method requires a basic knowledge of programming.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sk	You can program functions as \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060111.xhp\" name=\"add-ins\"\>add-ins\</link\>. This method requires an advanced knowledge of programming.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149260				0	sk	Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148456				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> button. You will now see the Basic IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150327				0	sk	Enter the function code. In this example, we define a \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> function that calculates the volume of a rectangular solid with side lengths \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\> and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\>:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	sk	Close the Basic-IDE window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150043				0	sk	Your function is automatically saved in the default module and is now available. If you apply the function in a Calc document that is to be used on another computer, you can copy the function to the Calc document as described in the next section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147340				0	sk	Copying a Function To a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145232	19			0	sk	In stage 2 of "Defining A Function Using %PRODUCTNAME Basic", in the \<emph\>Macro\</emph\> dialog you clicked on \<emph\>Edit \</emph\>. As the default, in the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field the \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> module is selected. The \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> library resides locally in your user directory.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	sk	If you want to copy the user-defined function to a Calc document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150086				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>My Macros - Standard - Module1\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3166430				0	sk	In the Basic-IDE, select the source of your user-defined function and copy it to the clipboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_idN1081D				0	sk	Close the Basic-IDE.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Macros - Organize Macros - %PRODUCTNAME Basic\</item\> .				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Macro from\</emph\> field select \<emph\>(Name of the Calc document) - Standard - Module1\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148699				0	sk	Paste the clipboard contents in the Basic-IDE of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153305				0	sk	Applying a User-defined Function in $[officename] Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148869				0	sk	Once you have defined the function \<item type=\"literal\"\>VOL(a; b; c)\</item\> in the Basic-IDE, you can apply it the same way as the built-in functions of $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	sk	Open a Calc document and enter numbers for the function parameters \<item type=\"literal\"\>a\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>b\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>c\</item\> in cells A1, B1, and C1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3156019				0	sk	Set the cursor in another cell and enter the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3155264				0	sk	=VOL(A1;B1;C1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\userdefined_function.xhp	0	help	par_id3146776				0	sk	The function is evaluated and you will see the result in the selected cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Importing and Exporting Text Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153726				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>csv files;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; importing/exporting as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>exporting;formulas as csv files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;csv files with formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153726				0	sk	\<variable id=\"csv_formula\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_formula.xhp\" name=\"Importing and Exporting Text Files\"\>Importing and Exporting CSV Text Files with Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149402				0	sk	Comma separated values (CSV) files are text files that contain the cell contents of a single sheet. Commas, semicolons, or other characters can be used as the field delimiters between the cells. Text strings are put in quotation marks, numbers are written without quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150715				0	sk	To Import a CSV File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155445				0	sk	In the \<emph\>File type\</emph\> field, select the format "Text CSV". Select the file and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>. When a file has the .csv extension, the file type is automatically recognized.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149565				0	sk	You will see the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3149255				0	sk	If the csv file contains formulas, but you want to import the results of those formulas, then choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022				0	sk	To Export Formulas and Values as CSV Files				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342				0	sk	Click the sheet to be written as a csv file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3166423				0	sk	If you want to export the formulas as formulas, for example, in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155111				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150200				0	sk	Under \<emph\>Display\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	sk	If you want to export the calculation results instead of the formulas, do not mark \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3148702				0	sk	Zvoľte \<emph\>Súbor - Uložiť ako\</emph\>. Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Uložiť ako\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153912				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> field select the format "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	sk	Enter a name and click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	sk	From the \<emph\>Export of text files\</emph\> dialog that appears, select the character set and the field and text delimiters for the data to be exported, and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3146781				0	sk	If the numbers use commas as decimal separators or thousands separators, do not select the comma as the field delimiter. If the text contains double quotation marks, you must select the single quotation mark as separator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3150050				0	sk	If necessary, after you have saved, clear the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> check box to see the calculated results in the table again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153487				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3153008				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000207.xhp\" name=\"Export text files\"\>Export text files\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_formula.xhp	0	help	par_id3155595				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000208.xhp\" name=\"Import text files\"\>Import text files\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Text Superscript / Subscript				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>superscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>subscript text in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text super/sub\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters;superscript/subscript\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151112				0	sk	\<variable id=\"super_subscript\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/super_subscript.xhp\" name=\"Text Superscript / Subscript\"\>Text Superscript / Subscript\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	sk	In the cell, select the character that you want to put in superscript or subscript.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	sk	If, for example, you want to write H20 with a subscript 2, select the 2 in the cell (not in the input line).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	sk	Otvorte kontextové menu a zvoľte \<emph\>Znak\</emph\>. Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Znak\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Font Position\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153954				0	sk	Select the \<emph\>Subscript\</emph\> option and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\super_subscript.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020500.xhp\" name=\"Context menu - Character - Font Position\"\>Context menu - Character - Font Position\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Automatically Calculating Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>series; calculating\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>calculating; series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>linear series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>growth series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date series\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>powers of 2 calculations\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; filling automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic cell filling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFill function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>filling;cells, automatically\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calc_series\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Calculating Series\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A8				0	sk	You can automatically fill cells with data with the AutoFill command or the Series command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D3				0	sk	Using AutoFill				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D7				0	sk	AutoFill automatically generates a data series based on a defined pattern.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sk	On a sheet, click in a cell, and type a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CB				0	sk	Click in another cell and then click back in the cell where you typed the number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	sk	Drag the fill handle in the bottom right corner of the cell across the cells that you want to fill, and release the mouse button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	sk	The cells are filled with ascending numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN106EE				0	sk	To quickly create a list of consecutive days, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Monday\</item\> in a cell, and drag the fill handle.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id9720145				0	sk	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	sk	If you select two or more adjacent cells that contain different numbers, and drag, the remaining cells are filled with the arithmetic pattern that is recognized in the numbers. The AutoFill function also recognizes customized lists that are defined under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10737				0	sk	You can double-click the fill handle to automatically fill all empty columns of the current data block. For example, first enter Jan into A1 and drag the fill handle down to A12 to get the twelve months in the first column. Now enter some values into B1 and C1. Select those two cells, and double-click the fill handle. This fills automatically the data block B1:C12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10713				0	sk	Using a Defined Series				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sk	Select the cell range in the sheet that you want to fill.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3154754				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Fill - Series\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10716				0	sk	Select the parameters for the series. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10731				0	sk	If you select a \<emph\>linear\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>added\</emph\> to each consecutive number in the series to create the next value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN1073C				0	sk	If you select a \<emph\>growth\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is \<emph\>multiplied\</emph\> by each consecutive number to create the next value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_idN10747				0	sk	If you select a \<emph\>date\</emph\> series, the increment that you enter is added to the time unit that you specify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_series.xhp	0	help	par_id3159173				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Creating Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148491				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; calling up and applying\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148491				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datapilot_createtable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_createtable.xhp\" name=\"Creating Pivot Tables\"\>Creating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156023				0	sk	Position the cursor within a range of cells containing values, row and column headings.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Create\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Select Source\</emph\> dialog appears. Choose \<emph\>Current selection\</emph\> and confirm with \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. The table headings are shown as buttons in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. Drag these buttons as required and drop them into the layout areas "Page Fields", "Column Fields", "Row Fields" and "Data Fields".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	sk	Drag the desired buttons into one of the four areas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id7599414				0	sk	Drag a button to the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area to create a button and a listbox on top of the generated pivot table. The listbox can be used to filter the pivot table by the contents of the selected item. You can use drag-and-drop within the generated pivot table to use another page field as a filter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	sk	If the button is dropped in the \<emph\>Data Fields\</emph\> area it will be given a caption that also shows the formula that will be used to calculate the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	sk	Dvojitým kliknutím na tlačidlo v časti \<emph\>Dátové pole\</emph\> vyvoláte dialógové okno \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Dátové pole\"\>\<emph\>Dátové pole\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	sk	Use the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data Field\</item\> dialog to select the calculations to be used for the data. To make a multiple selection, press the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key while clicking the desired calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	sk	The order of the buttons can be changed at any time by moving them to a different position in the area with the mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	sk	Remove a button by dragging it back to the area of the other buttons at the right of the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	sk	To open the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090105.xhp\" name=\"Data Field\"\>\<emph\>Data Field\</emph\>\</link\> dialog, double-click one of the buttons in the \<emph\>Row\</emph\> or \<emph\>Column\</emph\> area. Use the dialog to select if and to what extent \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> calculates display subtotals.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_createtable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	sk	Exit the Pivot Table dialog by pressing OK. A \<emph\>Filter\</emph\> button will now be inserted, or a page button for every data field that you dropped in the \<emph\>Page Fields\</emph\> area. The pivot table is inserted further down.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Printing Sheet Details				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>printing;sheet details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing details\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>grids; printing sheet grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; printing, instead of results\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>charts;printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet grids; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; printing grids\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>borders; printing cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>zero values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>null values; printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	sk	\<variable id=\"print_details\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_details.xhp\" name=\"Printing Sheet Details\"\>Printing Sheet Details\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	sk	When printing a sheet you can select which details are to be printed:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	Row and column headers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	sk	Sheet grid				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	sk	Comments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145801				0	sk	Objects and graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	sk	Grafy				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3154731				0	sk	Grafické objekty				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sk	Vzorce				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752				0	sk	To choose the details proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	sk	Select the sheet you want to print.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340	13			0	sk	The command is not visible if the sheet was opened with write protection on. In that case, click the \<emph\>Edit File \</emph\>icon on the \<emph\>Standard\</emph\> Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	14			0	sk	Select the \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> tab. In the \<emph\>Print \</emph\>area mark the details to be printed and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3145789				0	sk	Print the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_details.xhp	0	help	par_id3150345				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Calculating With Dates and Times				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146120				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>dates; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>times; in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;date and time formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>current date and time values\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146120				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calc_date\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_date.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Dates and Times\"\>Calculating With Dates and Times\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3154320				0	sk	In $[officename] Calc, you can perform calculations with current date and time values. As an example, to find out exactly how old you are in seconds or hours, follow the following steps:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150750				0	sk	In a spreadsheet, enter your birthday in cell A1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3145642	14			0	sk	Enter the following formula in cell A3: \<item type=\"literal\"\>=NOW()-A1\</item\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149020				0	sk	After pressing the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key you will see the result in date format. Since the result should show the difference between two dates as a number of days, you must format cell A3 as a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	sk	Place the cursor in cell A3, right-click to open a context menu and choose \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	sk	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog appears. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> tab, the "Number" category will appear already highlighted. The format is set to "General", which causes the result of a calculation containing date entries to be displayed as a date. To display the result as a number, set the number format to "-1,234" and close the dialog with the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	sk	The number of days between today's date and the specified date is displayed in cell A3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	sk	Experiment with some additional formulas: in A4 enter =A3*24 to calculate the hours, in A5 enter =A4*60 for the minutes, and in A6 enter =A5*60 for seconds. Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key after each formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_date.xhp	0	help	par_id3149207				0	sk	The time since your date of birth will be calculated and displayed in the various units. The values are calculated as of the exact moment when you entered the last formula and pressed the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Enter\</item\> key. This value is not automatically updated, although "Now" continuously changes. In the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> menu, the menu item \<emph\>Cell Contents - AutoCalculate\</emph\> is normally active; however, automatic calculation does not apply to the function NOW. This ensures that your computer is not solely occupied with updating the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Writing Multi-line Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154346				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>text in cells; multi-line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; text breaks\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>breaks in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>multi-line text in cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154346				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_wrap\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_wrap.xhp\" name=\"Writing Multi-line Text\"\>Writing Multi-line Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	sk	Pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter keys inserts a manual line break. This shortcut only works directly in the cell, not in the input line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153142				0	sk	If you want the text to automatically break at the right border of the cell, proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	sk	Select all the cells where you want the text to break at the right border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sk	In \<emph\>Format - Cells - Alignment\</emph\>, mark the \<emph\>Wrap text automatically\</emph\> option and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_wrap.xhp	0	help	par_id3145799				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cell\"\>Format - Cell\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Copying Formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151113				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying; formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151113				0	sk	\<variable id=\"formula_copy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_copy.xhp\" name=\"Copying Formulas\"\>Copying Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	sk	There are various ways to copy a formula. One suggested method is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	sk	Select the cell containing the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Copy\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3159155				0	sk	Select the cell into which you want the formula to be copied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V. The formula will be positioned in the new cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	sk	If you want to copy a formula into multiple cells, there is a quick and easy way to copy into adjacent cell areas:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sk	Select the cell containing the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	sk	Position the mouse on the bottom right of the highlighted border of the cell, and continue holding down the mouse button until the pointer changes to a cross-hair symbol.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sk	With the mouse button pressed, drag it down or to the right over all the cells into which you want to copy the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714				0	sk	When you release the mouse button, the formula will be copied into the cells and automatically adjusted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_copy.xhp	0	help	par_id3156385				0	sk	If you do not want values and texts to be automatically adjusted, then hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key when dragging. Formulas, however, are always adjusted accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying Filters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153896				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>filters; applying/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows;removing/redisplaying with filters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;filters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153896				0	sk	\<variable id=\"filters\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/filters.xhp\" name=\"Applying Filters\"\>Applying Filters\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	sk	Filters and advanced filters allow you to work on certain filtered rows (records) of a data range. In the spreadsheets in $[officename] there are various possibilities for applying filters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	sk	One use for the \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function is to quickly restrict the display to records with identical entries in a data field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Standard Filter\</emph\> dialog, you can also define ranges which contain the values in particular data fields. You can use the standard filter to connect the conditions with either a logical AND or a logical OR operator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	The \<emph\>Advanced filter\</emph\> allows up to a total of eight filter conditions. With advanced filters you enter the conditions directly into the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id9384746				0	sk	To remove a filter, so that you see all cells again, click inside the area where the filter was applied, then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Filter - Remove Filter\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_idN10663				0	sk	When you select multiple rows from an area where a filter was applied, then this selection can include rows that are visible and rows that are hidden by the filter. If you then apply formatting, or delete the selected rows, this action then applies only to the visible rows. The hidden rows are not affected. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\filters.xhp	0	help	par_id218817				0	sk	This is the opposite to rows that you have hidden manually by the \<emph\>Format - Rows - Hide Rows\</emph\> command. Manually hidden rows are deleted when you delete a selection that contains them.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Formatting Numbers as Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;entering as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; for numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell formats; text/numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers as text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/text_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers as Text\"\>Formatting Numbers as Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	sk	You can format numbers as text in $[officename] Calc. Open the context menu of a cell or range of cells and choose \<emph\>Format Cells - Numbers\</emph\>, then select "Text" from the \<emph\>Category\</emph\> list. Any numbers subsequently entered into the formatted range are interpreted as text. The display of these "numbers" is left-justified, just as with other text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	sk	If you have already entered normal numbers in cells and have afterwards changed the format of the cells to "Text", the numbers will remain normal numbers. They will not be converted. Only numbers entered afterwards, or numbers which are then edited, will become text numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3144765				0	sk	If you decide to enter a number directly as text, enter an apostrophe (') first. For example, for years in column headings, you can enter '1999, '2000 and '2001. The apostrophe is not visible in the cell, it only indicates that the entry is to be recognized as a text. This is useful if, for example, you enter a telephone number or postal code that begins with a zero (0), because a zero (0) at the start of a sequence of digits is removed in normal number formats.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\text_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3156284				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Entering Formulas 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>formula bar; input line\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>input line in formula bar\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; inputting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;formulas\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150868				0	sk	\<variable id=\"formula_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_enter.xhp\" name=\"Entering Formulas\"\>Entering Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6848353				0	sk	You can enter formulas in several ways: using the icons, or by typing on the keyboard, or by a mixture of both methods.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145364				0	sk	Click the cell in which you want to enter the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150012				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Function\</emph\> icon on the Formula Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	sk	You will now see an equals sign in the input line and you can begin to input the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	sk	After entering the required values, press Enter or click \<emph\>Accept\</emph\> to insert the result in the active cell. If you want to clear your entry in the input line, press Escape or click \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	sk	You can also enter the values and the formulas directly into the cells, even if you cannot see an input cursor. Formulas must always begin with an equals sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id4206976				0	sk	You can also press the + or - key on the numerical keyboard to start a formula. NumLock must be "on". For example, press the following keys in succession:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id1836909				0	sk	+ 5 0 - 8 Enter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8171330				0	sk	You see the result \<item type=\"literal\"\>42\</item\> in the cell. The cell contains the formula \<item type=\"literal\"\>=+50-8\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764				0	sk	If you are editing a formula with references, the references and the associated cells will be highlighted with the same color. You can now resize the reference border using the mouse, and the reference in the formula displayed in the input line also changes. \<emph\>Show references in color\</emph\> can be deactivated under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060300.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210	7			0	sk	\<variable id=\"tip\"\>If you would like to view the calculation of individual elements of a formula, select the respective elements and press F9. For example, in the formula =SUM(A1:B12)*SUM(C1:D12) select the section SUM(C1:D12) and press F9 to view the subtotal for this area. \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	sk	If an error occurs when creating the formula, an \<link href=\"text/scalc/05/02140000.xhp\" name=\"error message\"\>error message\</link\> appears in the active cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/main0206.xhp\" name=\"Formula bar\"\>Formula bar\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Rozpoznanie názvov ako adries				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148797				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>automatic addressing in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>natural language addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas; using row/column labels\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; as addressing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>addressing; automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>name recognition on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>row headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>column headers;using in formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows; finding labels automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>recognizing; column and row labels\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148797				0	sk	\<variable id=\"address_auto\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/address_auto.xhp\" name=\"Recognizing Names as Addressing\"\>Recognizing Names as Addressing\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3152597				0	sk	You can use cells with text to refer to the rows or to the columns that contain the cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3154942\" src=\"res/helpimg/names_as_addressing.png\" width=\"2.1291in\" height=\"0.8709in\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3154942\"\>Example spreadsheet\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3154512				0	sk	In the example spreadsheet, you can use the string \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column One'\</item\> in a formula to refer to the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>B5\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Column Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>C2\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>C5\</item\>. You can also use \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row One'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B3\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D3\</item\>, or \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Row Two'\</item\> for the cell range \<item type=\"literal\"\>B4\</item\> to \<item type=\"literal\"\>D4\</item\>. The result of a formula that uses a cell name, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>SUM('Column One')\</item\>, is 600.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	sk	This function is active by default. To turn this function off, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\> and clear the \<emph\>Automatically find column and row labels\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\address_auto.xhp	0	help	par_id3149210				0	sk	If you want a name to be automatically recognized by Calc, the name must start with a letter and be composed of alphanumeric characters. If you enter the name in the formula yourself, enclose the name in single quotation marks ('). If a single quotation mark appears in a name, you must enter a backslash in front of the quotation mark, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>'Harry\\'s Bar'.\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Cells in Currency Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156329				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>currency formats; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>international currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats; currency formats in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>currencies; default currencies\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defaults;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;currency formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329				0	sk	\<variable id=\"currency_format\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/currency_format.xhp\" name=\"Cells in Currency Format\"\>Cells in Currency Format\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	sk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can give numbers any currency format. When you click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Currency\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3150791\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_currencyfield.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3150791\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formatting\</item\> bar to format a number, the cell is given the default currency format set under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	Exchanging of \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc documents can lead to misunderstandings, if your \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc document is loaded by a user who uses a different default currency format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	sk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can define that a number that you have formatted as "1,234.50 €", still remains in euros in another country and does not become dollars.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3151075				0	sk	You can change the currency format in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format Cells\</item\> dialog (choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</item\> tab) by two country settings. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\> combo box select the basic setting for decimal and thousands separators. In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box you can select the currency symbol and its position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749				0	sk	For example, if the language is set to "Default" and you are using a german locale setting, the currency format will be "1.234,00 €". A point is used before the thousand digits and a comma before the decimal places. If you now select the subordinate currency format "$ English (US)" from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list box , you will get the following format: "$ 1.234,00". As you can see, the separators have remained the same. Only the currency symbol has been changed and converted, but the underlying format of the notation remains the same as in the locale setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	sk	If, under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Language\</item\>, you convert the cells to "English (US)", the English-language locale setting is also transferred and the default currency format is now "$ 1,234.00".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\currency_format.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Entering Values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150868				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>values; inserting in multiple cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell ranges;selecting for data entries\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>areas, see also cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3405255				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cell_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_enter.xhp\"\>Entering Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7147129				0	sk	Calc can simplify entering data and values into multiple cells. You can change some settings to conform to your preferences.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id5621509				0	sk	To Enter Values Into a Range of Cells Manually				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8200018				0	sk	There are two features that assist you when you enter a block of data manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id1867427				0	sk	Area Detection for New Rows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7908871				0	sk	In the row below a heading row, you can advance from one cell to the next with the Tab key. After you enter the value into the last cell in the current row, press Enter. Calc positions the cursor below the first cell of the current block.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id6196783				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id6473586\" src=\"res/helpimg/area1.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6473586\"\>area detection\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id8118839				0	sk	In row 3, press Tab to advance from cell B3 to C3, D3, and E3. Then press Enter to advance to B4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3583788				0	sk	Area Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id2011780				0	sk	Use drag-and-drop to select the area where you want to input values. But start dragging from the last cell of the area and release the mouse button when you have selected the first cell. Now you can start to input values. Always press the Tab key to advance to the next cell. You will not leave the selected area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id7044282				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id2811365\" src=\"res/helpimg/area2.png\" width=\"4.8335in\" height=\"1.5937in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id2811365\"\>area selection\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3232520				0	sk	Select the area from E7 to B3. Now B3 is waiting for your input. Press Tab to advance to the next cell within the selected area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id8950163				0	sk	To Enter Values to a Range of Cells Automatically				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id633869				0	sk	See \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_series.xhp\"\>Automatically Filling in Data Based on Adjacent Cells\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Calculating Time Differences				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;time differences\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>time differences\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calc_timevalues\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calc_timevalues.xhp\" name=\"Calculating Time Differences\"\>Calculating Time Differences\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3149263				0	sk	If you want to calculate time differences, for example, the time between 23:30 and 01:10 in the same night, use the following formula:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3159153				0	sk	=(B2<A2)+B2-A2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3152598				0	sk	The later time is B2 and the earlier time is A2. The result of the example is 01:40 or 1 hour and 40 minutes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calc_timevalues.xhp	0	help	par_id3145271				0	sk	In the formula, an entire 24-hour day has a value of 1 and one hour has a value of 1/24. The logical value in parentheses is 0 or 1, corresponding to 0 or 24 hours. The result returned by the formula is automatically issued in time format due to the sequence of the operands.				20200411 15:09:53
