helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	sk	With the help of the \<emph\>Web Page Query ($[officename] Calc)\</emph\> import filter, you can insert tables from HTML documents in a Calc spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sk	You can use the same method to insert ranges defined by name from a Calc or Microsoft Excel spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sk	The following insert methods are available:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146976				0	sk	Inserting by Dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154319				0	sk	Set the cell cursor at the cell where the new content will be inserted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	sk	Zvoľte \<emph\>Vložiť - Odkaz na externé dáta\</emph\>. Otvorí sa dialógové okno \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\"\>Externé dáta\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	sk	Enter the URL of the HTML document or the name of the spreadsheet. Press Enter when finished. Click the \<emph\>...\</emph\> button to open a file selection dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149400				0	sk	In the large list box of the dialog, select the named ranges or tables you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sk	You can also specify that the ranges or tables are updated every n seconds.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	sk	The import filter can create names for cell ranges on the fly. As much formatting as possible is retained, while the filter intentionally does not load any images.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149021				0	sk	Inserting by Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153965				0	sk	Open two documents: the $[officename] Calc spreadsheet in which the external data is to be inserted (target document) and the document from which the external data derives (source document).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	sk	In the target document open the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sk	In the lower combo box of the Navigator select the source document. The Navigator now shows the range names and database ranges or the tables contained in the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3148842	20			0	sk	In the Navigator select the \<emph\>Insert as link\</emph\> drag mode \<image id=\"img_id3152985\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20238.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3152985\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3157978				0	sk	Drag the desired external data from the Navigator into the target document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	sk	If you have loaded an HTML document with the \<emph\>Web Page Query\</emph\> filter as the source document, you will find the tables in the Navigator, named continuously from "HTML_table1" onwards, and also two range names that have been created:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3152873				0	sk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_all\</item\> - designates the entire document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149897				0	sk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>HTML_tables\</item\> - designates all HTML tables in the document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149126				0	sk	Editing the external data				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3159228				0	sk	Open \<emph\>Edit - Links\</emph\>. Here you can edit the link to the external data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\webquery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154650				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External data dialog\"\>External data dialog\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Importing and Exporting dBASE Files 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id1226844				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>exporting;spreadsheets to dBASE\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>importing;dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>dBASE import/export\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; importing from/exporting to dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables in databases;importing dBASE files\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10738				0	sk	\<variable id=\"dbase_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/dbase_files.xhp\"\>Importing and Exporting dBASE Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10756				0	sk	You can open and save data in the dBASE file format (*.dbf file extension) in $[officename] Base or a spreadsheet. In %PRODUCTNAME Base, a dBASE database is a folder that contains files with the .dbf file extension. Each file corresponds to a table in the database. Formulas and formatting are lost when you open and save a dBASE file from %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10759				0	sk	To Import a dBASE File Into a Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10760				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071F				0	sk	Locate the *.dbf file that you want to import. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10768				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10730				0	sk	Otvorí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Importovať súbor dBASE\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10774				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10777				0	sk	The dBASE file opens as a new Calc spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1074E				0	sk	If you want to save the spreadsheet as a dBASE file, do not alter or delete the first row in the imported file. This row contains information that is required by a dBASE database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077A				0	sk	To Import a dBASE File Into a Database Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1076C				0	sk	A %PRODUCTNAME Base database table is actually a link to an existing database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10796				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - New - Database\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10786				0	sk	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box of the \<emph\>Save As\</emph\> dialog, enter a name for the database.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10792				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1079A				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Database type \</emph\>box of the \<emph\>Database Properties\</emph\> dialog, select "dBASE".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107A6				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AE				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Browse\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107B6				0	sk	Locate the directory that contains the dBASE file, and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Create\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F1				0	sk	To Save a Spreadsheet as a dBASE File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F8				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10800				0	sk	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> box, select "dBASE file".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F9				0	sk	In the \<emph\>File name\</emph\> box, type a name for the dBASE file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10801				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\dbase_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10808				0	sk	Only the data on the current sheet is exported.				20200411 15:09:53
