helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Validity of Cell Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156442				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>values; limiting on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>limits; specifying value limits on input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>permitted cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; validity\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>error messages; defining for incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>actions in case of incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Help tips; defining text for cell input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comments;help text for cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; defining input help\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>macros; running when incorrect input\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; validity check\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	sk	\<variable id=\"validity\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/validity.xhp\" name=\"Validity of Cell Contents\"\>Validity of Cell Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156283				0	sk	For each cell, you can define entries to be valid. Invalid entries to a cell will be rejected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252				0	sk	The validity rule is activated when a new value is entered. If an invalid value has already been inserted into the cell, or if you insert a value in the cell either with drag-and-drop or by copying and pasting, the validity rule will not take effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id5174718				0	sk	You can choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective\</emph\> at any time and choose the command \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>\<emph\>Mark Invalid Data\</emph\>\</link\> to display which cells contain invalid values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155603				0	sk	Using Cell Contents Validity				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3155959				0	sk	Select the cells for which you want to define a new validity rule.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148837	8			0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Validity\</item\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156020	9			0	sk	On the \<emph\>Criteria\</emph\> tab page, enter the conditions for new values entered into cells. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159208				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Allow\</emph\> field, select an option.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3153011				0	sk	If you select "Whole Numbers", values such as "12.5" are not allowed. Choosing "Date" allows date information both in the local date format as well as in the form of a \<link href=\"text/sbasic/shared/03030101.xhp\" name=\"serial date\"\>serial date\</link\>. Similarly, the "Time" condition permits time values such as "12:00" or serial time numbers. "Text Length" stipulates that cells are allowed to contain text only.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id9224829				0	sk	Select "List" to enter a list of valid entries.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149317				0	sk	Select the next condition under \<emph\>Data\</emph\>. According to what you choose, additional options will be selectable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3151389				0	sk	After you have determined the conditions for cell validity, you can use the other two tab pages to create message boxes:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3159261				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Input Help\</emph\> tab page, enter the title and the text of the tip, which will then be displayed if the cell is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page, select the action to be carried out in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3147416				0	sk	If you select "Stop" as the action, invalid entries are not accepted, and the previous cell contents are retained.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3150033				0	sk	Select "Warning" or "Information" to display a dialog in which the entry can either be canceled or accepted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149947				0	sk	If you select "Macro", then by using the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button you can specify a macro to be run in the event of an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3149011	35			0	sk	To display the error message, select \<emph\>Show error message when invalid values are entered\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3148586				0	sk	After changing the action for a cell on the \<emph\>Error Alert\</emph\> tab page and closing the dialog with OK, you must first select another cell before the change takes effect.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\validity.xhp	0	help	par_id3154805				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"Data - Validity\"\>Data - Validity\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Finding and Replacing in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	bm_id3769341				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>searching, see also finding\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>finding;formulas/values/text/objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>replacing; cell contents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;multiple cell texts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149204				0	sk	\<variable id=\"finding\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/finding.xhp\"\>Finding and Replacing in Calc\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9363689				0	sk	In spreadsheet documents you can find words, formulas, and styles. You can navigate from one result to the next, or you can highlight all matching cells at once, then apply another format or replace the cell content by other content.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id3610644				0	sk	The Find & Replace dialog				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2224494				0	sk	Cells can contain text or numbers that were entered directly as in a text document. But cells can also contain text or numbers as the result of a calculation. For example, if a cell contains the formula =1+2 it displays the result 3. You must decide whether to search for the 1 respective 2, or to search the 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id2423780				0	sk	To find formulas or values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2569658				0	sk	You can specify in the Find & Replace dialog either to find the parts of a formula or the results of a calculation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6394238				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7214270				0	sk	Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2186346				0	sk	Select "Formulas" or "Values" in the \<emph\>Search in\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id1331217				0	sk	With "Formulas" you will find all parts of the formulas. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id393993				0	sk	With "Values" you will find the results of the calculations. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3163853				0	sk	Cell contents can be formatted in different ways. For example, a number can be formatted as a currency, to be displayed with a currency symbol. You see the currency symbol in the cell, but you cannot search for it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id7359233				0	sk	Finding text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6549272				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\> to open the Find & Replace dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id6529740				0	sk	Enter the text to find in the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> text box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9121982				0	sk	Either click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> or \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id3808404				0	sk	When you click \<emph\>Find\</emph\>, Calc will select the next cell that contains your text. You can watch and edit the text, then click \<emph\>Find\</emph\> again to advance to the next found cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id2394482				0	sk	If you closed the dialog, you can press a key combination (\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+F) to find the next cell without opening the dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id631733				0	sk	By default, Calc searches the current sheet. Click \<emph\>More Options\</emph\>, then enable \<emph\>Search in all sheets\</emph\> to search through all sheets of the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id7811822				0	sk	When you click \<emph\>Find All\</emph\>, Calc selects all cells that contain your entry. Now you can for example set all found cells to bold, or apply a Cell Style to all at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	hd_id8531449				0	sk	The Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9183935				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>View - Navigator\</emph\> to open the Navigator window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id946684				0	sk	The Navigator is the main tool for finding and selecting objects.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\finding.xhp	0	help	par_id9607226				0	sk	Use the Navigator for inserting objects and links within the same document or from other open documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151112				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>printing; sheets on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets; printing on multiple pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; repeating when printing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>repeating;columns/rows on printed pages\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; printing on all sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>footers; printing on sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>printing; rows/columns as table headings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headings;repeating rows/columns as\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153727				0	sk	\<variable id=\"print_title_row\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/print_title_row.xhp\" name=\"Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\"\>Printing Rows or Columns on Every Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014				0	sk	If you have a sheet that is so large that it will be printed multiple pages, you can set up rows or columns to repeat on each printed page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146975				0	sk	As an example, If you want to print the top two rows of the sheet as well as the first column (A)on all pages, do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3163710				0	sk	Zvoľte \<emph\>Formát - Oblasti tlače - Upraviť\</emph\>. Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Upraviť oblasti tlače\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	sk	Click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Rows to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3145800				0	sk	The dialog shrinks so that you can see more of the sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155602				0	sk	Select the first two rows and, for this example, click cell A1 and drag to A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154018				0	sk	In the shrunk dialog you will see $1:$2. Rows 1 and 2 are now rows to repeat.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sk	Kliknite opäť na ikonu vpravo od oblasti \<emph\>Opakovať riadky\</emph\>. dialógové okno sa znovu sa zobrazí.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155443				0	sk	If you also want column A as a column to repeat, click the icon at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	sk	Click column A (not in the column header).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	sk	Click the icon again at the far right of the \<emph\>Columns to repeat\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	sk	Rows to repeat are rows from the sheet. You can define headers and footers to be printed on each print page independently of this in \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3155380				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/03100000.xhp\" name=\"View - Page Break Preview\"\>View - Page Break Preview\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\print_title_row.xhp	0	help	par_id3146113				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05070000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\"\>Format - Page - (Header / Footer)\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Protecting Cells from Changes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146119				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>protecting;cells and sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell protection; enabling\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents; protecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; hiding for printing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; sheet protection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;hiding\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146119				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cell_protect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_protect.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Cells from Changes\"\>Protecting Cells from Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153368				0	sk	In \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc you can protect sheets and the document as a whole. You can choose whether the cells are protected against accidental changes, whether the formulas can be viewed from within Calc, whether the cells are visible or whether the cells can be printed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145261				0	sk	Protection can be provided by means of a password, but it does not have to be. If you have assigned a password, protection can only be removed once the correct password has been entered.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sk	Note that the cell protection for cells with the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute is only effective when you protect the whole sheet. In the default condition, every cell has the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> attribute. Therefore you must remove the attribute selectively for those cells where the user may make changes. You then protect the whole sheet and save the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id5974303				0	sk	These protection features are just switches to prevent accidental action. The features are not intended to provide any secure protection. For example, by exporting a sheet to another file format, a user may be able to surpass the protection features. There is only one secure protection: the password that you can apply when saving an OpenDocument file. A file that has been saved with a password can be opened only with the same password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	sk	Select the cells that you want to specify the cell protection options for.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149019				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Cells\</item\> and click the \<emph\>Cell Protection\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	sk	Select the protection options that you want. All options will be applied only after you protect the sheet from the Tools menu - see below.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id31529866655				0	sk	Uncheck \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to allow the user to change the currently selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152898	10			0	sk	Select \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> to prevent changes to the contents and the format of a cell. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069A				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Hide formula\</emph\> to hide and to protect formulas from changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A1				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Hide when printing\</emph\> to hide protected cells in the printed document. The cells are not hidden onscreen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3152872				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	sk	Apply the protection options.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C0				0	sk	To protect the cells from being changed / viewed / printed according to your settings in the \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> dialog, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C7				0	sk	To protect the structure of the document, for example the count, \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\"\>names\</link\>, and order of the sheets, from being changed, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Protect Document - Document\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106CF				0	sk	(Optional) Enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D2				0	sk	If you forget your password, you cannot deactivate the protection. If you only want to protect cells from accidental changes, set the sheet protection, but do not enter a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153810	13			0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_protect.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B8C				0	sk	            \<embedvar href=\"text/shared/guide/digital_signatures.xhp#digital_signatures\"/\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Ukotvenie riadkov alebo stĺpcov v podobe hlavičiek				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154684				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>tables; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>title rows; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns; freezing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>freezing rows or columns\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>headers; freezing during table split\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>scrolling prevention in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>windows; splitting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; splitting windows\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154684				0	sk	\<variable id=\"line_fix\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/line_fix.xhp\" name=\"Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\"\>Freezing Rows or Columns as Headers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sk	If you have long rows or columns of data that extend beyond the viewable area of the sheet, you can freeze some rows or columns, which allows you to see the frozen columns or rows as you scroll through the rest of the data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156441				0	sk	Vyberte riadok pod alebo stĺpec napravo od riadku alebo stĺpca, ktorý chcete mať ukotvený. Všetky riadky nad alebo stĺpce naľavo od vášho výberu budú ukotvené.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	sk	To freeze both horizontally and vertically, select the \<emph\>cell\</emph\> that is below the row and to the right of the column that you want to freeze.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3151073	5			0	sk	To deactivate, choose \<emph\>Window - Freeze \</emph\>again.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	sk	If the area defined is to be scrollable, apply the \<emph\>Window - Split\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345				0	sk	If you want to print a certain row on all pages of a document, choose \<emph\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3147004				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07090000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Freeze\"\>Window - Freeze\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/07080000.xhp\" name=\"Window - Split\"\>Window - Split\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\line_fix.xhp	0	help	par_id3150304				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05080300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Print ranges - Edit\"\>Format - Print ranges - Edit\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	19xx/20xx Years				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150439				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>years; 2-digits\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>dates; 19xx/20xx\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150439				0	sk	\<variable id=\"year2000\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/year2000.xhp\" name=\"19xx/20xx Years\"\>19xx/20xx Years\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	sk	The year in a date entry is often entered as two digits. Internally, the year is managed by $[officename] as four digits, so that in the calculation of the difference from 1/1/99 to 1/1/01, the result will correctly be two years.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3154011				0	sk	Under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\> you can define the century that is used when you enter a year with only two digits. The default is 1930 to 2029.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\year2000.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	This means that if you enter a date of 1/1/30 or higher, it will be treated internally as 1/1/1930 or higher. All lower two-digit years apply to the 20xx century. So, for example, 1/1/20 is converted into 1/1/2020.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Deaktivácia automatických oprav				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>deactivating; automatic changes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; deactivating automatic changes in\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoInput function on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; AutoInput function of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>input support in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing; input in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoCorrect function;cell contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cell input;AutoInput function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;AutoInput function (in cells)\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;avoiding conversion to\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion on/off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456				0	sk	\<variable id=\"auto_off\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/auto_off.xhp\" name=\"Deactivating Automatic Changes\"\>Deactivating Automatic Changes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3156442				0	sk	By default, $[officename] automatically corrects many common typing errors and applies formatting while you type. You can immediately undo any automatic changes with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Z.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	sk	Nasledujúce riadky ukazujú ako je možné opätovne aktivovať a deaktivovať automatické opravy v $[officename] Calc:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145748				0	sk	Automatic Text or Number Completion				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154730				0	sk	When making an entry in a cell, $[officename] Calc automatically suggests matching input found in the same column. This function is known as \<emph\>AutoInput\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	sk	To turn the AutoInput on and off, set or remove the check mark in front of \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146972				0	sk	Automatic Conversion to Date Format				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sk	$[officename] Calc automatically converts certain entries to dates. For example, the entry \<emph\>1.1\</emph\> may be interpreted as January 1 of the current year, according to the locale settings of your operating system, and then displayed according to the date format applied to the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3159267				0	sk	Pokiaľ chcete mať istotu, že hodnota bude intepretovaná ako text, vložte pred jej začiatok apostrof ('), ktorý sa v bunke zobrazuje.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150043				0	sk	Quotation Marks Replaced by Custom Quotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3155333				0	sk	Zvoľte \<emph\>Nástroje - Možnosti automatickej opravy\</emph\>. V otvorenom okne prejdite na záložku \<emph\>Lokalizované možnosti\</emph\> a zrušte zakliknutie \<emph\>Nahradiť\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149565				0	sk	Cell Content Always Begins With Uppercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab. Unmark \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Capitalize first letter of every sentence\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150345				0	sk	Replace Word With Another Word				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3166425				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>. Go to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab. Select the word pair and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Delete\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3152992				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06130000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\"\>Tools - Cell Contents - AutoInput\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\auto_off.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Nástroje - Možnosti automatickej opravy\"\>Nástroje - Možnosti automatickej opravy\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using Rounded Off Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153361				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>numbers; rounded off\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounded off numbers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exact numbers in $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places; showing\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;number of decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values;rounded in calculations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;rounded off values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbers; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>precision as shown\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding precision\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; values as shown\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156422				0	sk	\<variable id=\"rounding_numbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rounding_numbers.xhp\" name=\"Using Rounded Off Numbers\"\>Using Rounded Off Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	sk	In $[officename] Calc, all decimal numbers are displayed rounded off to two decimal places.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152596				0	sk	To change this for selected cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3154321				0	sk	Mark all the cells you want to modify.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147428				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> and go to the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	sk	V poli \<emph\>Kategórie\</emph\> vyberte \<emph\>Číslo\</emph\>. V časti \<emph\>Voľby\</emph\> zmeňte počet v poli \<emph\>Desatinné miesta\</emph\> a uzavrite dialógové okno kliknutím na OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155415				0	sk	To change this everywhere				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3153707				0	sk	Na strane \<emph\>Spočítať\</emph\> zmeňte počet v poli \<emph\>Desatinné miesta\</emph\> a uzavrite dialógové okno kliknutím na OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154755				0	sk	To calculate with the rounded off numbers instead of the internal exact values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3150045				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920				0	sk	Go to the \<emph\>Calculate\</emph\> page. Mark the \<emph\>Precision as shown\</emph\> field and exit the dialog with OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3145790				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Numbers\"\>Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rounding_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147005				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\" name=\"Calculate\"\>Calculate\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148663				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; preventing data overwriting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>output ranges of pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148663				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datapilot_tipps\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_tipps.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\"\>Selecting Pivot Table Output Ranges\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3154123				0	sk	Click the button \<emph\>More\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Pivot Table\</emph\> dialog. The dialog will be extended.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	sk	You can select a named range in which the pivot table is to be created, from the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. If the results range does not have a name, enter the coordinates of the upper left cell of the range into the field to the right of the \<emph\>Results to\</emph\> box. You can also click on the appropriate cell to have the coordinates entered accordingly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974				0	sk	If you mark the \<emph\>Ignore empty rows\</emph\> check box, they will not be taken into account when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_tipps.xhp	0	help	par_id3145273				0	sk	If the \<emph\>Identify categories\</emph\> check box is marked, the categories will be identified by their headings and assigned accordingly when the pivot table is created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	References to Other Sheets and Referencing URLs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150441				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>HTML; in sheet cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>references; URL in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; Internet references\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>URL; in Calc\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150441				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cellreferences_url\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences_url.xhp\" name=\"Referencing URLs\"\>Referencing URLs\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id1955626				0	sk	For example, if you found an Internet page containing current stock exchange information in spreadsheet cells, you can load this page in $[officename] Calc by using the following procedure:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152993				0	sk	In a $[officename] Calc document, position the cursor in the cell into which you want to insert the external data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3145384				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Link to External Data\</item\>. The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"External Data\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\>\</link\> dialog appears.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3152892				0	sk	Enter the URL of the document or Web page in the dialog. The URL must be in the format: http://www.my-bank.com/table.html. The URL for local or local area network files is the path seen in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153068				0	sk	$[officename] loads the Web page or file in the "background", that is, without displaying it. In the large list box of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>External Data\</item\> dialog, you can see the name of all the sheets or named ranges you can choose from.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3153914				0	sk	Select one or more sheets or named ranges. You can also activate the automatic update function every "n" seconds and click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3157979				0	sk	The contents will be inserted as a link in the $[officename] Calc document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3144768				0	sk	Save your spreadsheet. When you open it again later, $[officename] Calc will update the linked cells following an inquiry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences_url.xhp	0	help	par_id3159204				0	sk	Under \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040900.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - General\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - General\</item\>\</link\> you can choose to have the update, when opened, automatically carried out either always, upon request or never. The update can be started manually in the dialog under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Links\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Grouping Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	bm_id4195684				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function;grouping table entries\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>ungrouping entries in pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10643				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datapilot_grouping\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_grouping.xhp\"\>Grouping Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10661				0	sk	The resulting pivot table can contain many different entries. By grouping the entries, you can improve the visible result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10667				0	sk	Select a cell or range of cells in the pivot table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Group\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066E				0	sk	Depending on the format of the selected cells, either a new group field is added to the pivot table, or you see one of the two \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090400.xhp\"\>Grouping\</link\> dialogs, either for numeric values, or for date values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_id3328653				0	sk	The pivot table must be organized in a way that grouping can be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_grouping.xhp	0	help	par_idN10682				0	sk	To remove a grouping, click inside the group, then choose \<emph\>Data - Group and Outline - Ungroup\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting and Editing Comments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153968				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>comments; on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;comments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>remarks on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;comments on cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>displaying; comments\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153968				0	sk	\<variable id=\"note_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/note_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Comments\"\>Inserting and Editing Comments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150440				0	sk	You can assign a comment to each cell by choosing \<link href=\"text/shared/01/04050000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Comment\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Comment\</emph\>\</link\>. The comment is indicated by a small red square, the comment indicator, in the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	sk	The comment is visible whenever the mouse pointer is over the cell, provided you have activated \<emph\>Help - Tips\</emph\> or - \<emph\>Extended Tips\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148575				0	sk	When you select the cell, you can choose \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> from the context menu of the cell. Doing so keeps the comment visible until you deactivate the \<emph\>Show Comment\</emph\> command from the same context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149958				0	sk	To edit a permanently visible comment, just click in it. If you delete the entire text of the comment, the comment itself is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10699				0	sk	Move or resize each comment as you like.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN1069D				0	sk	Format each comment by specifying background color, transparency, border style, and text alignment. Choose the commands from the context menu of the comment.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	sk	To show or hide the comment indicator, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\> and mark or unmark the \<emph\>Comment indicator\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\note_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715				0	sk	To display a help tip for a selected cell, use \<emph\>Data - Validity - Input Help\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
