helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying Sort Lists				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150870				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>filling;customized lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sort lists;applying\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>geometric lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>arithmetic lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>series;sort lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists; user-defined\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>customized lists\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150870	3			0	sk	\<variable id=\"sorted_list\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/sorted_list.xhp\" name=\"Applying Sort Lists\"\>Applying Sort Lists\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3159154				0	sk	Sort lists allow you to type one piece of information in a cell, then drag it to fill in a consecutive list of items.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3148645				0	sk	For example, enter the text "Jan" or "January" in an empty cell. Select the cell and click the mouse on the lower right corner of the cell border. Then drag the selected cell a few cells to the right or downwards. When you release the mouse button, the highlighted cells will be filled with the names of the months.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id2367931				0	sk	Hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>if you do not want to fill the cells with different values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3152577				0	sk	The predefined series can be found under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Sort Lists\</emph\>. You can also create your own lists of text strings tailored to your needs, such as a list of your company's branch offices. When you use the information in these lists later (for example, as headings), just enter the first name in the list and expand the entry by dragging it with your mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\sorted_list.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060400.xhp\" name=\"Sort lists\"\>Sort lists\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Converting Text to Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>formats; text as numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>time format conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>date formats;conversion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id0908200901265171				0	sk	\<variable id=\"numbers_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/numbers_text.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text to Numbers\"\>Converting Text to Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265127				0	sk	Calc converts text inside cells to the respective numeric values if an unambiguous conversion is possible. If no conversion is possible, Calc returns a #VALUE! error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265196				0	sk	Only integer numbers including exponent are converted, and ISO 8601 dates and times in their extended formats with separators. Anything else, like fractional numbers with decimal separators or dates other than ISO 8601, is not converted, as the text string would be locale dependent. Leading and trailing blanks are ignored.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265220				0	sk	The following ISO 8601 formats are converted:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265288				0	sk	CCYY-MM-DD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265267				0	sk	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265248				0	sk	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265374				0	sk	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265327				0	sk	CCYY-MM-DDThh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265399				0	sk	hh:mm				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265347				0	sk	hh:mm:ss				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265349				0	sk	hh:mm:ss,s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265342				0	sk	hh:mm:ss.s				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265491				0	sk	The century code CC may not be omitted. Instead of the T date and time separator, exactly one space character may be used.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265467				0	sk	If a date is given, it must be a valid Gregorian calendar date. In this case the optional time must be in the range 00:00 to 23:59:59.99999...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265420				0	sk	If only a time string is given, it may have an hours value of more than 24, while minutes and seconds can have a maximum value of 59.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265448				0	sk	The conversion is done for single arguments only, as in =A1+A2, or ="1E2"+1. Cell range arguments are not affected, so SUM(A1:A2) differs from A1+A2 if at least one of the two cells contain a convertible string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id090820090126540				0	sk	Strings inside formulas are also converted, such as in ="1999-11-22"+42, which returns the date 42 days after November 22nd, 1999. Calculations involving localized dates as strings inside the formula return an error. For example, the localized date string "11/22/1999" or "22.11.1999" cannot be used for the automatic conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id1005200903485368				0	sk	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485359				0	sk	In A1 enter the text \<item type=\"literal\"\>'1e2\</item\> (which is converted to the number 100 internally).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id1005200903485341				0	sk	In A2 enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A1+1\</item\> (which correctly results in 101).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\numbers_text.xhp	0	help	par_id0908200901265544				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Numbers\"\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Zvýraznenie záporných čísel				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147434				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; highlighting negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>highlighting;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>colors;negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats;colors for negative numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147434				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cellstyle_minusvalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp\" name=\"Highlighting Negative Numbers\"\>Highlighting Negative Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3153878				0	sk	Pre bunky obsahujúce čísla môžete použiť formátovanie čísel, ktoré zvyrazňuje záporné čísla červenou farbou alebo si môžete definovať vlastné formátovanie čisel, ktoré bude zobrazovať záporné čísla vami zvolenou farbou.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600				0	sk	Select the cells and choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3146969				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab, select a number format and mark \<emph\>Negative numbers red\</emph\> check box. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellstyle_minusvalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145640				0	sk	The cell number format is defined in two parts. The format for positive numbers and zero is defined in front of the semicolon; after the semicolon the formula for negative numbers is defined. You can change the code (RED) under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format code\</item\>. For example, instead of RED, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>YELLOW\</item\>. If the new code appears in the list after clicking the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Add\</item\> icon, this is a valid entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Referencing a Cell in Another Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147436				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>sheet references\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>references; to cells in other sheets/documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; operating in another document\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>documents;references\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cellreferences\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellreferences.xhp\" name=\"Referencing Other Sheets\"\>Referencing Other Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9663075				0	sk	In a sheet cell you can show a reference to a cell in another sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id1879329				0	sk	In the same way, a reference can also be made to a cell from another document provided that this document has already been saved as a file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id7122409				0	sk	To Reference a Cell in the Same Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id2078005				0	sk	Open a new, empty spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id4943693				0	sk	By way of example, enter the following formula in cell A1 of Sheet1:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id9064302				0	sk	               \<item type=\"literal\"\>=Sheet2.A1\</item\>            				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7609790				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Sheet 2\</emph\> tab at the bottom of the spreadsheet. Set the cursor in cell A1 there and enter text or a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id809961				0	sk	If you switch back to Sheet1, you will see the same content in cell A1 there. If the contents of Sheet2.A1 change, then the contents of Sheet1.A1 also change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	hd_id9209570				0	sk	To Reference a Cell in Another Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5949278				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Open\</emph\>, to load an existing spreadsheet document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8001953				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - New\</emph\>, to open a new spreadsheet document. Set the cursor in the cell where you want to insert the external data and enter an equals sign to indicate that you want to begin a formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8571123				0	sk	Now switch to the document you have just loaded. Click the cell with the data that you want to insert in the new document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id8261665				0	sk	Switch back to the new spreadsheet. In the input line you will now see how $[officename] Calc has added the reference to the formula for you. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id5888241				0	sk	The reference to a cell of another document contains the name of the other document in single inverted commas, then a hash #, then the name of the sheet of the other document, followed by a point and the name of the cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7697683				0	sk	Confirm the formula by clicking the green check mark.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id7099826				0	sk	If you drag the box in the lower right corner of the active cell to select a range of cells, $[officename] automatically inserts the corresponding references in the adjacent cells. As a result, the sheet name is preceded with a "$" sign to designate it as an absolute reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellreferences.xhp	0	help	par_id674459				0	sk	If you examine the name of the other document in this formula, you will notice that it is written as a \<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000002.xhp#url\" name=\"URL\"\>URL\</link\>. This means that you can also enter a URL from the Internet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying Multiple Operations				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147559				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>multiple operations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>what if operations;two variables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data tables; multiple operations in\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cross-classified tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147559				0	sk	\<variable id=\"multioperation\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multioperation.xhp\" name=\"Applying Multiple Operations\"\>Applying Multiple Operations\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145171				0	sk	Multiple Operations in Columns or Rows				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id4123966				0	sk	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Data - Multiple Operations\</item\> command provides a planning tool for "what if" questions. In your spreadsheet, you enter a formula to calculate a result from values that are stored in other cells. Then, you set up a cell range where you enter some fixed values, and the Multiple Operations command will calculate the results depending on the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156424				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the formula that applies to the data range. In the \<emph\>Column input cell/Row input cell\</emph\> field, enter the cell reference to the corresponding cell that is part of the formula. This can be explained best by examples:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159153				0	sk	Príklady				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153189				0	sk	You produce toys which you sell for $10 each. Each toy costs $2 to make, in addition to which you have fixed costs of $10,000 per year. How much profit will you make in a year if you sell a particular number of toys?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id6478774				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id1621753\" src=\"res/helpimg/what-if.png\" width=\"0.2228in\" height=\"0.2228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1621753\"\>what-if sheet area\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145239				0	sk	Calculating With One Formula and One Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146888				0	sk	To calculate the profit, first enter any number as the quantity (items sold) - in this example 2000. The profit is found from the formula Profit=Quantity * (Selling price - Direct costs) - Fixed costs. Enter this formula in B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3157875				0	sk	In column D enter given annual sales, one below the other; for example, 500 to 5000, in steps of 500.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3159115				0	sk	Select the range D2:E11, and thus the values in column D and the empty cells alongside in column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149723				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149149	46			0	sk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas \</emph\>field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149355				0	sk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the variable in the formula, which is replaced by the selected column values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149009				0	sk	Kliknutím na \<emph\>OK\</emph\> zatvoríte dialógové okno. V stĺpci E sa zobrazia výnosy pre rôzne hodnoty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148725				0	sk	Calculating with Several Formulas Simultaneously				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3146880				0	sk	Delete column E.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154675				0	sk	Enter the following formula in C5: = B5 / B4. You are now calculating the annual profit per item sold.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148885				0	sk	Select the range D2:F11, thus three columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3147474				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154846				0	sk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, select cells B5 through C5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153931				0	sk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3150862				0	sk	Kliknutím na \<emph\>OK\</emph\> zatvoríte dialógové okno. V stĺpci E sa zobrazia výnosy a v stĺpci F ročný výnos na kus.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146139				0	sk	Multiple Operations Across Rows and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3148584				0	sk	\<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> allows you to carry out joint multiple operations for columns and rows in so-called cross-tables. The formula cell has to refer to both the data range arranged in rows and the one arranged in columns. Select the range defined by both data ranges and call the multiple operation dialog. Enter the reference to the formula in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field. The \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> and the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> fields are used to enter the reference to the corresponding cells of the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149949				0	sk	Calculating with Two Variables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154808				0	sk	Consider columns A and B of the sample table above. You now want to vary not just the quantity produced annually, but also the selling price, and you are interested in the profit in each case.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149731				0	sk	Expand the table shown above. D2 through D11 contain the numbers 500, 1000 and so on, up to 5000. In E1 through H1 enter the numbers 8, 10, 15 and 20.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3152810				0	sk	Select the range D1:H11.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3153620				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Multiple Operations\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149981				0	sk	With the cursor in the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> field, click cell B5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	sk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Row input cell\</emph\> field and click cell B1. This means that B1, the selling price, is the horizontally entered variable (with the values 8, 10, 15 and 20).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3154049				0	sk	Set the cursor in the \<emph\>Column input cell\</emph\> field and click in B4. This means that B4, the quantity, is the vertically entered variable.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149141				0	sk	Kliknutím na OK dialógové okno zatvoríte. V oblasti E2:H11 uvidíte vypočítané zisky pre rôzne predajné ceny.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multioperation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155104				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12060000.xhp\" name=\"Multiple operations\"\>Multiple operations\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	 Importing and Exporting CSV Files 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	bm_id892361				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>number series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data series import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>exporting; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>importing; tables as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>delimited values and files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>comma separated files and values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text file import and export\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>csv files;importing and exporting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; importing/exporting as text\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>text documents; importing to spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;text csv files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>saving;as text csv\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10862				0	sk	\<variable id=\"csv_files\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/csv_files.xhp\"\>Opening and Saving Text CSV Files\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10880				0	sk	Comma Separated Values (CSV) is a text file format that you can use to exchange data from a database or a spreadsheet between applications. Each line in a Text CSV file represents a record in the database, or a row in a spreadsheet. Each field in a database record or cell in a spreadsheet row is usually separated by a comma. However, you can use other characters to delimit a field, such as a tabulator character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10886				0	sk	If the field or cell contains a comma, the field or cell \<emph\>must\</emph\> be enclosed by single quotes (') or double quotes (").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10890				0	sk	To Open a Text CSV File in Calc				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10897				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089F				0	sk	Locate the CSV file that you want to open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	sk	If the file has a *.csv extension, select the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	sk	If the CSV file has another extension, select the file, and then select "Text CSV" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082D				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Open\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	sk	The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108B1				0	sk	Specify the options to divide the text in the file into columns.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BB				0	sk	You can preview the layout of the imported data at the bottom of the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Import\</item\> dialog. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_id8444166				0	sk	Right-click a column in the preview to set the format or to hide the column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108E2				0	sk	Check the text delimiter box that matches the character used as text delimiter in the file. In case of an unlisted delimiter, type the character into the input box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C5				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN108FA				0	sk	To Save a Sheet as a Text CSV File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FC				0	sk	When you export a spreadsheet to CSV format, only the data on the current sheet is saved. All other information, including formulas and formatting, is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10901				0	sk	Open the Calc sheet that you want to save as a Text CSV file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107AF				0	sk	Only the current sheet can be exported.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10905				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Save as\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN10915				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box, enter a name for the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1090D				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File type\</item\> box, select "Text CSV".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DD				0	sk	(Optional) Set the field options for the Text CSV file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN1091C				0	sk	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit filter settings\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Export of text files\</item\> dialog, select the options that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\csv_files.xhp	0	help	par_idN107FC				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Save\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
