helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150448				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; introduction\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>DataPilot, see pivot table function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150448				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datapilot\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot.xhp\" name=\"Pivot Table\"\>Pivot Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024				0	sk	The \<emph\>pivot table\</emph\> (formerly known as \<emph\>DataPilot\</emph\>) allows you to combine, compare, and analyze large amounts of data. You can view different summaries of the source data, you can display the details of areas of interest, and you can create reports.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot.xhp	0	help	par_id3145069				0	sk	A table that has been created as a \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12090000.xhp\" name=\"pivot table\"\>pivot table\</link\> is an interactive table. Data can be arranged, rearranged or summarized according to different points of view.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Navigating Through Sheets Tabs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150769				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>sheets; showing multiple\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;using\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>views;multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150769	4			0	sk	\<variable id=\"multi_tables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/multi_tables.xhp\" name=\"Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\"\>Navigating Through Sheet Tabs\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	sk	By default $[officename] displays three sheets "Sheet1" to "Sheet3", in each new spreadsheet. You can switch between sheets in a spreadsheet using the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_idN106AF				0	sk	 \<image id=\"img_id4829822\" src=\"res/helpimg/sheettabs.png\" width=\"3.3335inch\" height=\"0.7638inch\" localize=\"true\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id4829822\"\>Sheet Tabs\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153144				0	sk	 \<image id=\"img_id3156441\" src=\"res/helpimg/calcnav.png\" width=\"0.6563inch\" height=\"0.1457inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156441\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	sk	Use the navigation buttons to display all the sheets belonging to your document. Clicking the button on the far left or the far right displays, respectively, the first or last sheet tab. The middle buttons allow the user to scroll forward and backward through all sheet tabs. To display the sheet itself click on the sheet tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\multi_tables.xhp	0	help	par_id3149379				0	sk	If there is insufficient space to display all the sheet tabs, you can increase it by pointing to the separator between the scrollbar and the sheet tabs, pressing the mouse button and, keeping the mouse button pressed, dragging to the right. In doing so you will be sharing the available space between the sheet tabs and horizontal scrollbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Unprotecting Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153252				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>cell protection; unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting; unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153252	14			0	sk	\<variable id=\"cell_unprotect\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cell_unprotect.xhp\" name=\"Unprotecting Cells\"\>Unprotecting Cells\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3151112				0	sk	Click the sheet for which you want to cancel the protection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\>, then choose \<emph\>Sheet\</emph\> or \<emph\>Document\</emph\> to remove the check mark indicating the protected status.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	sk	If you have assigned a password, enter it in this dialog and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cell_unprotect.xhp	0	help	par_id3153771				0	sk	The cells can now be edited, the formulas can be viewed, and all cells can be printed until you reactivate the protection for the sheet or document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying AutoFilter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156423				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>filters, see also AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>AutoFilter function;applying\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheets; filter values\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; filter sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>drop-down menus in sheet columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>database ranges; AutoFilter function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156423				0	sk	\<variable id=\"autofilter\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/autofilter.xhp\" name=\"Applying AutoFilter\"\>Applying AutoFilter\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147427				0	sk	The \<emph\>AutoFilter\</emph\> function inserts a combo box on one or more data columns that lets you select the records (rows) to be displayed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152576				0	sk	Select the columns you want to use AutoFilter on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>. The combo box arrows are visible in the first row of the range selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510				0	sk	Run the filter by clicking the drop-down arrow in the column heading and choosing an item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sk	Only those rows whose contents meet the filter criteria are displayed. The other rows are filtered. You can see if rows have been filtered from the discontinuous row numbers. The column that has been used for the filter is identified by a different color for the arrow button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id9216589				0	sk	When you apply an additional AutoFilter on another column of a filtered data range, then the other combo boxes list only the filtered data.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153714	12			0	sk	To display all records again, select the "all\<emph\>"\</emph\> entry in the AutoFilter combo box. If you choose "Standard\<emph\>"\</emph\>, the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Standard Filter\</item\> dialog appears, allowing you to set up a standard filter. Choose "Top 10" to display the highest 10 values only. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	sk	To stop using AutoFilter, reselect all cells selected in step 1 and once again choose \<emph\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id4303415				0	sk	To assign different AutoFilters to different sheets, you must first define a database range on each sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3159236				0	sk	The arithmetic functions also take account of the cells that are not visible due to an applied filter. For example, a sum of an entire column will also total the values in the filtered cells. Apply the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\> function if only the cells visible after the application of a filter are to be taken into account.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12040100.xhp\" name=\"Data - Filter - AutoFilter\"\>Data - Filter - AutoFilter\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\autofilter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060106.xhp\" name=\"SUBTOTAL\"\>SUBTOTAL\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Calculating With Formulas				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155411				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>formulas;calculating with\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; with formulas\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;formula calculation\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155411				0	sk	\<variable id=\"formulas\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formulas.xhp\" name=\"Calculating With Formulas\"\>Calculating With Formulas\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156281				0	sk	All formulas begin with an equals sign. The formulas can contain numbers, text, arithmetic operators, logic operators, or functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145272				0	sk	Remember that the basic arithmetic operators (+, -, *, /) can be used in formulas using the "Multiplication and Division before Addition and Subtraction" rule. Instead of writing =SUM(A1:B1) you can write =A1+B1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	sk	Parentheses can also be used. The result of the formula =(1+2)*3 produces a different result than =1+2*3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3156285				0	sk	Here are a few examples of $[officename] Calc formulas:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154015				0	sk	=A1+10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146972				0	sk	Displays the contents of cell A1 plus 10.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	sk	=A1*16%				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sk	Displays 16% of the contents of A1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146917				0	sk	=A1 * A2				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146315				0	sk	Displays the result of the multiplication of A1 and A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154022				0	sk	=ROUND(A1;1)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150363				0	sk	Displays the contents of cell A1 rounded to one decimal place.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150209				0	sk	=EFFECTIVE(5%;12)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150883				0	sk	Calculates the effective interest for 5% annual nominal interest with 12 payments a year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3146114				0	sk	=B8-SUM(B10:B14)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3154486				0	sk	Calculates B8 minus the sum of the cells B10 to B14.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152890				0	sk	=SUM(B8;SUM(B10:B14))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3159171				0	sk	Calculates the sum of cells B10 to B14 and adds the value to B8.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150109				0	sk	It is also possible to nest functions in formulas, as shown in the example. You can also nest functions within functions. The Function Wizard assists you with nested functions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060100.xhp\" name=\"Functions list\"\>Functions list\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formulas.xhp	0	help	par_id3152869				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060000.xhp\" name=\"AutoPilot: Functions\"\>Function Wizard\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
