helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150440				0	sk	\<variable id=\"cellcopy\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/cellcopy.xhp\" name=\"Only Copy Visible Cells\"\>Only Copy Visible Cells\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3148577				0	sk	Assume you have hidden a few rows in a cell range. Now you want to copy, delete, or format only the remaining visible rows.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154729				0	sk	$[officename] behavior depends on how the cells were made invisible, by a filter or manually.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	sk	Method and Action				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150751				0	sk	Výsledok				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	sk	Cells were filtered by AutoFilters, standard filters or advanced filters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044				0	sk	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	sk	Only the visible cells of the selection are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3166427				0	sk	Cells were hidden using the \<emph\>Hide\</emph\> command in the context menu of the row or column headers, or through an \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080000.xhp\" name=\"outline\"\>outline\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sk	Copy, delete, move, or format a selection of currently visible cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\cellcopy.xhp	0	help	par_id3154371				0	sk	All cells of the selection, including the hidden cells, are copied, deleted, moved, or formatted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Selecting Themes for Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>theme selection for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>layout;spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cell styles; selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sheets;formatting themes\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formats;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formatting;themes for sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791	6			0	sk	\<variable id=\"design\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/design.xhp\" name=\"Selecting Themes for Sheets\"\>Selecting Themes for Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	sk	$[officename] Calc comes with a predefined set of formatting themes that you can apply to your spreadsheets.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490				0	sk	It is not possible to add themes to Calc, and they cannot be modified. However, you can modify their styles after you apply them to a spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	sk	Before you format a sheet with a theme, you have to apply at least one custom cell style to the cells on the sheet. You can then change the cell formatting by selecting and applying a theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382				0	sk	To apply a custom cell style to a cell, you can open the Styles and Formatting window and, in its lower list box, set the Custom Styles view. A list of the existing custom defined cell styles will be displayed. Double click a name from the Styles and Formatting window to apply this style to the selected cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3153963				0	sk	To apply a theme to a spreadsheet:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146920	15			0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Choose Themes\</emph\> icon in the \<emph\>Tools\</emph\> bar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	sk	Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Výber témy\</emph\>. V ňom vidíte zoznam dostupných tém pre celý zošit a v dialógovom okne Štýly a formátovanie zoznam vlastných štýlov pre jednotlivé bunky.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3155114	9			0	sk	In the \<emph\>Theme Selection \</emph\>dialog, select the theme that you want to apply to the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150090				0	sk	Click OK				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3150201				0	sk	As soon as you select another theme in the \<emph\>Theme Selection\</emph\> dialog, some of the properties of the custom style will be applied to the current spreadsheet. The modifications will be immediately visible in your spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\design.xhp	0	help	par_id3146979				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/02/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Theme selection\"\>Theme selection\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155686				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; moving cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cells; moving by drag and drop \</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;moving by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>moving;cells by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;cells, by drag and drop\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	hd_id986358				0	sk	\<variable id=\"move_dragdrop\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/move_dragdrop.xhp\"\>Moving Cells by Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2760093				0	sk	When you drag-and-drop a selection of cells on a Calc sheet, the cells normally overwrite the existing cells in the area where you drop. This is the normal \<emph\>overwrite mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9527268				0	sk	When you hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key while releasing the mouse button, you enter the \<emph\>insert mode\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id79653				0	sk	In insert mode, the existing cells where you drop will be shifted to the right or to the bottom, and the dropped cells are inserted into the now empty positions without overwriting. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8676717				0	sk	The surrounding box of the moved cells looks different in insert mode. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id3968932				0	sk	In overwrite mode you see all four borders around the selected area. In insert mode you see only the left border when target cells will be shifted to the right. You see only the upper border when target cells will be shifted down. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id7399517				0	sk	Whether the target area will be shifted to the right or to the bottom depends on the distance between source and target cells, if you move within the same sheet. It depends on the number of horizontal or vertical cells in the moved area, if you move to a different sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id8040406				0	sk	If you move cells in insert mode within the same row (only horizontally), then after insertion of the cells, all cells will be shifted to the left to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2586748				0	sk	In both modes, you can hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key, or \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys while you release the mouse button to insert a copy or a link, respectively.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5814081				0	sk	Keys pressed while releasing the mouse button				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6581316				0	sk	Výsledok				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9906613				0	sk	No key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2815637				0	sk	Cells are moved and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells are emptied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id6161687				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4278389				0	sk	Cells are copied and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2805566				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5369121				0	sk	Links to the source cells are inserted and overwrite the cells in the target area. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id9518723				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2926419				0	sk	Cells are moved and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells are emptied, except if you move within the same rows on the same sheet. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id4021423				0	sk	If you move within the same rows on the same sheet, the cells in the target area shift to the right, and then the whole row shifts to fill the source area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2783898				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id2785119				0	sk	Cells are copied and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id584124				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option+Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt+Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift keys				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\move_dragdrop.xhp	0	help	par_id5590990				0	sk	Links to the source cells are inserted and shift the cells in the target area to the right or to the bottom. Source cells stay as they are.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Entering a Number with Leading Zeros				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147560				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>zero values; entering leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers; with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>integers with leading zeros\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; changing text/number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; changing text/number\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text in cells; changing to numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>converting;text with leading zeros, into numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147560				0	sk	\<variable id=\"integer_leading_zero\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/integer_leading_zero.xhp\" name=\"Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\"\>Entering a Number with Leading Zeros\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153194				0	sk	There are various ways to enter integers starting with a zero:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146119				0	sk	Enter the number as text. The easiest way is to enter the number starting with an apostrophe (for example, \<item type=\"input\"\>'0987\</item\>). The apostrophe will not appear in the cell, and the number will be formatted as text. Because it is in text format, however, you cannot calculate with this number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154013				0	sk	Naformátujte bunku s formátom čísla ako je \<item type=\"input\"\>\\0000\</item\>. Tento formát môže byť priradený poľu \<emph\>Formátovací­ kód\</emph\> na záložke \<emph\>Formát - Bunky - Čísla\</emph\> a definuje zobrazenie bunky ako " vždy zobraz prvú nuly a potom celé číslo s minimálne troma miestami respektíve vyplniť s nulami doľava v prípade že má menej ako tri číslice".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3153158				0	sk	If you want to apply a numerical format to a column of numbers in text format (for example, text "000123" becomes number "123"), do the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149377				0	sk	Select the column in which the digits are found in text format. Set the cell format in that column as "Number".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154944	60			0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Find & Replace\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3154510	61			0	sk	In the \<emph\>Search for\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>^[0-9]\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3155068	62			0	sk	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, enter \<item type=\"input\"\>&\</item\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018	63			0	sk	Check \<emph\>Regular expressions\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3156382	64			0	sk	Check \<emph\>Current selection only\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\integer_leading_zero.xhp	0	help	par_id3146916	65			0	sk	Click \<emph\>Replace All\</emph\>               				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	User-defined Number Formats				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	bm_id3143268				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;user-defined formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; user-defined numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; millions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>format codes; user-defined number formats\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143268				0	sk	\<variable id=\"format_value_userdef\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value_userdef.xhp\" name=\"User-defined Number Formats\"\>User-defined Number Formats\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150400				0	sk	You can define your own number formats to display numbers in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	sk	As an example, to display the number 10,200,000 as 10.2 Million:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	sk	Select the cells to which you want to apply a new, user-defined format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells - Numbers\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list box select "User-defined".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3148646				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Format code\</emph\> text box enter the following code:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	sk	0.0,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	sk	Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3155417				0	sk	The following table shows the effects of rounding, thousands delimiters (,), decimal delimiters (.) and the placeholders # and 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3146971				0	sk	Číslo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3154757				0	sk	.#,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value_userdef.xhp	0	help	par_id3147338				0	sk	0.0,, "Million"				20200411 15:09:53
