helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using Scenarios				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149664				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>scenarios; creating/editing/deleting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>opening;scenarios\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>selecting;scenarios in Navigator\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3125863				0	sk	\<variable id=\"scenario\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/scenario.xhp\" name=\"Using Scenarios\"\>Using Scenarios\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	sk	A $[officename] Calc scenario is a set of cell values that can be used within your calculations. You assign a name to every scenario on your sheet. Define several scenarios on the same sheet, each with some different values in the cells. Then you can easily switch the sets of cell values by their name and immediately observe the results. Scenarios are a tool to test out "what-if" questions.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149255				0	sk	Creating Your Own Scenarios				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704	16			0	sk	To create a scenario, select all the cells that provide the data for the scenario. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154020				0	sk	Select the cells that contain the values that will change between scenarios. To select multiple cells, hold down the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>\</item\>key as you click each cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150364				0	sk	Zvoľte \<emph\>Nástroje - Scenáre\</emph\>. Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Vytvoriť scenár\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	sk	Zadajte názov scenára a nechajte ostatné polia nezmenené. Zatvorte dialógové okno kliknutím na OK. Váš nový scenár je automaticky aktivovaný.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149664				0	sk	Using Scenarios				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415				0	sk	Scenarios can be selected in the Navigator:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3150752	12			0	sk	Open the Navigator with the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id1593676\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_navigator.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id1593676\"\>Navigator icon\</alt\>\</image\> on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	13			0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Scenarios\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id7617114\" src=\"sc/res/imglst/navipi/na07.png\" width=\"0.222inch\" height=\"0.222inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id7617114\"\>Scenarios icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154256				0	sk	In the Navigator, you see the defined scenarios with the comments that were entered when the scenarios were created.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id1243629				0	sk	Double-click a scenario name in the Navigator to apply that scenario to the current sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id9044770				0	sk	To delete a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3674123				0	sk	To edit a scenario, right-click the name in the Navigator and choose \<emph\>Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3424481				0	sk	Ak chcete skryť ohraničenie buniek, ktoré sú súčasťou scenára, otvorte dialógové okno \<emph\>Vlastnosti\</emph\> každého scenára, ktorý bunky ovplyvňuje, a zrušte zaškrtnutie poľa Zobraziť ohraničenie. Pri skrytí ohraničenia sa tiež odstráni zoznam, z ktorého môžete vyberať scenáre.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368				0	sk	If you want to know which values in the scenario affect other values, choose \<emph\>Tools - Detective - Trace Dependents\</emph\>. You see arrows to the cells that are directly dependent on the current cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\scenario.xhp	0	help	par_id3154484				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Creating Scenarios\"\>Creating Scenarios\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Updating Pivot Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>pivot table import\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pivot table function; refreshing tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>recalculating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>updating;pivot tables\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datapilot_updatetable\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/datapilot_updatetable.xhp\" name=\"Updating Pivot Tables\"\>Updating Pivot Tables\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\datapilot_updatetable.xhp	0	help	par_id3154684				0	sk	If the data of the source sheet has been changed, $[officename] recalculates the pivot table. To recalculate the table, choose \<emph\>Data - Pivot Table - Refresh\</emph\>. Do the same after you have imported an Excel pivot table into $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying Goal Seek				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145068				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>goal seeking;example\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>equations in goal seek\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating;variables in equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>variables;calculating equations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>examples;goal seek\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145068				0	sk	\<variable id=\"goalseek\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/goalseek.xhp\" name=\"Applying Goal Seek\"\>Applying Goal Seek\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3145171				0	sk	With the help of Goal Seek you can calculate a value that, as part of a formula, leads to the result you specify for the formula. You thus define the formula with several fixed values and one variable value and the result of the formula.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153966				0	sk	Goal Seek Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150871				0	sk	To calculate annual interest (I), create a table with the values for the capital (C), number of years (n), and interest rate (i). The formula is:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3152596				0	sk	I = C * n* i				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	sk	Let us assume that the interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> of 7.5% and the number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\> (1) will remain constant. However, you want to know how much the investment capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would have to be modified in order to attain a particular return \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\>. For this example, calculate how much capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> would be required if you want an annual return of $15,000.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960				0	sk	Enter each of the values for Capital \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\> (an arbitrary value like \<item type=\"literal\"\>$100,000\</item\>), number of years \<item type=\"literal\"\>n \</item\>(\<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>), and interest rate \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> (\<item type=\"literal\"\>7.5%\</item\>) in one cell each. Enter the formula to calculate the interest \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> in another cell. Instead of \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>, \<item type=\"literal\"\>n\</item\>, and \<item type=\"literal\"\>i\</item\> use the \<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/relativ_absolut_ref.xhp\"\>reference to the cell\</link\> with the corresponding value.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3147001				0	sk	Kurzor nastavte do bunky s úrokovou mierou \<item type=\"literal\"\>I\</item\> a zvoľte \<emph\>Nástroje - Hľadať riešenie\</emph\>. Zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Vyhľadanie cieľa\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150088				0	sk	The correct cell is already entered in the field \<emph\>Formula Cell\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3166426				0	sk	Place the cursor in the field \<emph\>Variable Cell\</emph\>. In the sheet, click in the cell that contains the value to be changed, in this example it is the cell with the capital value \<item type=\"literal\"\>C\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3150369				0	sk	Enter the expected result of the formula in the \<emph\>Target Value\</emph\> text box. In this example, the value is 15,000. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3146978				0	sk	Zobrazí sa dialógové okno s informáciou, že funkcia Hľadať riešenie bola úspešná. Kliknutím na \<emph\>Áno\</emph\> vložíte výsledok do bunky s premennou.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\goalseek.xhp	0	help	par_id3149409				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06040000.xhp\" name=\"Goal Seek\"\>Goal Seek\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Copying to Multiple Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149456				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>copying;values, to multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;values in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data;inserting in multiple sheets\</bookmark_value\> \<bookmark_value\>sheets; simultaneous multiple filling\</bookmark_value\> 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149456	3			0	sk	\<variable id=\"edit_multitables\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/edit_multitables.xhp\" name=\"Copying to Multiple Sheets\"\>Copying to Multiple Sheets\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3150868				0	sk	In $[officename] Calc, you can insert values, text or formulas that are simultaneously copied to other selected sheets of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3153768				0	sk	Select all desired sheets by holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl \</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>key and clicking the corresponding register tabs that are still gray at the bottom margin of the workspace. All selected register tabs are now white.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	sk	You can use Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Page Up or Page Down to select multiple sheets using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\edit_multitables.xhp	0	help	par_id3147435				0	sk	Now when you insert values, text or formulas into the active sheet, they will also appear in the identical positions in the other selected sheets. For example, data entered in cell A1 of the active sheet is automatically entered into cell A1 of any other seleted sheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Formatting Numbers With Decimals				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145367				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>numbers;formatting decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; numbers in tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; number formats\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defaults; number formats in spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places;formatting numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;numbers with decimals\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;adding/deleting decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>number formats; adding/deleting decimal places in cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting; decimal places\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>decimal places; adding/deleting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145367				0	sk	\<variable id=\"format_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_value.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Numbers With Decimals\"\>Formatting Numbers With Decimals\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3148576				0	sk	Enter a number into the sheet, for example, 1234.5678. This number will be displayed in the default number format, with two decimal places. You will see 1234.57 when you confirm the entry. Only the display in the document will be rounded off; internally, the number retains all four decimal places after the decimal point.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012				0	sk	To format numbers with decimals:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147394				0	sk	Nastavte kurzor do bunky s číslom a vyberte \<emph\>Formát - Bunky\</emph\>, zobrazí sa dialógové okno \<emph\>Formátovať bunky\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Numbers\</emph\> tab you will see a selection of predefined number formats. In the bottom right in the dialog you will see a preview of how your current number would look if you were to give it a particular format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3155766				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3149021\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_numberformatincdecimals.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149021\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\format_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3149256				0	sk	If you only want to modify the number of the decimal places displayed, the easiest method is to use the \<emph\>Number Format: Add Decimal Place\</emph\> or \<emph\>Number Format: Delete Decimal Place\</emph\> icons on the Formatting Bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Displaying Formulas or Values				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153195				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>formulas; displaying in cells\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>values; displaying in tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables; displaying formulas/values\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>results display vs. formulas display\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>displaying; formulas instead of results\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153195				0	sk	\<variable id=\"formula_value\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/formula_value.xhp\" name=\"Displaying Formulas or Values\"\>Displaying Formulas or Values\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3150010				0	sk	If you want to display the formulas in the cells, for example in the form =SUM(A1:B5), proceed as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Display\</emph\> area mark the \<emph\>Formulas\</emph\> box. Click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3147396				0	sk	If you want to view the calculation results instead of the formula, do not mark the Formulas box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\formula_value.xhp	0	help	par_id3153157				0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060100.xhp\" name=\"Spreadsheet - View\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - View\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149346				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds;cell ranges\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells; backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>rows, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns, see also cells\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149346				0	sk	\<variable id=\"background\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/background.xhp\" name=\"Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\"\>Defining Background Colors or Background Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id9520249				0	sk	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for cell ranges in $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144760				0	sk	Applying a Background Color to a $[officename] Calc Spreadsheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155429				0	sk	Select the cells.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Cells\</emph\> (or \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> from the context menu).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3152938				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146974				0	sk	Graphics in the Background of Cells				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155414				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sk	Select the graphic and click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153575				0	sk	The graphic is inserted anchored to the current cell. You can move and scale the graphic as you want. In your context menu you can use the \<emph\>Arrange - To Background\</emph\> command to place this in the background. To select a graphic that has been placed in the background, use the \<switchinline select=\"appl\"\>\<caseinline select=\"CALC\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Navigator\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id51576				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/background.xhp\"\>Watermarks\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156180				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030600.xhp\" name=\"Background tab page\"\>\<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7601245				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/format_table.xhp\"\>Formatting Spreadsheets\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Renaming Sheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150398				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>renaming;sheets\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sheet tabs;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;renaming\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; sheets\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150398				0	sk	\<variable id=\"rename_table\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/rename_table.xhp\" name=\"Renaming Sheets\"\>Renaming Sheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155131				0	sk	Click the name of the sheet that you want to change.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3146976				0	sk	Open the context menu and choose the \<emph\>Rename Sheet\</emph\> command. A dialog box appears where you can enter a new name.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149260				0	sk	Enter a new name for the sheet and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149667				0	sk	Alternatively, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option key\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt key\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and click on any sheet name and enter the new name directly.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502833				0	sk	Sheet names can contain almost any character. Some naming restrictions apply when you want to save the spreadsheet to Microsoft Excel format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050283				0	sk	When saving to Microsoft Excel format, the following characters are not allowed in sheet names:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050281				0	sk	colon :				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502897				0	sk	back slash \\				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050299				0	sk	forward slash /				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502913				0	sk	question mark ?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050298				0	sk	asterisk *				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502969				0	sk	left square bracket [				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502910				0	sk	right square bracket ]				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810502971				0	sk	single quote ' as the first or last character of the name				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id090920081050307				0	sk	In cell references, a sheet name has to be enclosed in single quotes ' if the name contains other characters than alphanumeric or underscore. A single quote contained within a name has to be escaped by doubling it (two single quotes). For example, you want to reference the cell A1 on a sheet with the following name:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503071				0	sk	This year's sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503054				0	sk	The reference must be enclosed in single quotes, and the one single quote inside the name must be doubled:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id0909200810503069				0	sk	'This year''s sheet'.A1				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\rename_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155444				0	sk	The name of a sheet is independent of the name of the spreadsheet. You enter the spreadsheet name when you save it for the first time as a file. The document can contain up to 256 individual sheets, which can have different names.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Calculating in Spreadsheets				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150791				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets; calculating\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>calculating; spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>formulas; calculating\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150791				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calculate\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/guide/calculate.xhp\" name=\"Calculating in Spreadsheets\"\>Calculating in Spreadsheets\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3146120				0	sk	The following is an example of a calculation in $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951				0	sk	Click in a cell, and type a number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10656				0	sk	Press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065D				0	sk	The cursor moves down to the next cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155064				0	sk	Enter another number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066F				0	sk	Press the Tab key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	sk	The cursor moves to the right into the next cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3154253				0	sk	Type in a formula, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=A3 * A4 / 100.\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_idN1068B				0	sk	 Press Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	sk	The result of the formula appears in the cell. If you want, you can edit the formula in the input line of the Formula bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\guide\calculate.xhp	0	help	par_id3155378				0	sk	When you edit a formula, the new result is calculated automatically.				20200411 15:09:53
