helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3154703				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060116.xhp\"\>Analysis Functions Part Two\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149566				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>ISLEAPYEAR function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>leap year determination\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149566				0	sk	ISLEAPYEAR				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150297				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".\"\>Determines whether a year is a leap year.\</ahelp\> If yes, the function will return the value 1 (TRUE); if not, it will return 0 (FALSE).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148487				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150205				0	sk	ISLEAPYEAR("Date")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3159239				0	sk	\<emph\>Date\</emph\> specifies whether a given date falls within a leap year. The Date parameter must be a valid date according to the locale settings of %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149817				0	sk	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_id3150786				0	sk	=ISLEAPYEAR(A1) returns 1, if A1 contains 1968-02-29, the valid date 29th of February 1968 in your locale setting.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107E7				0	sk	You may also use =ISLEAPYEAR("1968-02-29") or =ISLEAPYEAR("2/29/68").				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060111.xhp	0	help	par_idN107EA				0	sk	Never use =ISLEAPYEAR(2/29/68), because this would first evaluate 2 divided by 29 divided by 68, and then calculate the ISLEAPYEAR function from this small number as a serial date number.				20200411 15:09:53
