helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	WEEKDAY 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154925				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>WEEKDAY function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154925				0	sk	\<variable id=\"weekday\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_weekday.xhp\"\>WEEKDAY\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154228				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WOCHENTAG\"\>Returns the day of the week for the given date value.\</ahelp\> The day is returned as an integer between 1 (Sunday) and 7 (Saturday) if no type or type=1 is specified. If type=2, numbering begins at Monday=1; and if type=3 numbering begins at Monday=0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147217				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149033				0	sk	WEEKDAY(Number; Type)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3149046				0	sk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\>, as a date value, is a decimal for which the weekday is to be returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3154394				0	sk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> determines the type of calculation. For Type=1, the weekdays are counted starting from Sunday (this is the default even when the Type parameter is missing). For Type=2, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=1. For Type=3, the weekdays are counted starting from Monday=0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3156188				0	sk	These values apply only to the standard date format that you select under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153836				0	sk	Príklady				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150317				0	sk	=WEEKDAY("2000-06-14") returns 4 (the Type parameter is missing, therefore the standard count is used. The standard count starts with Sunday as day number 1. June 14, 2000 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	sk	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";2) returns 3 (the Type parameter is 2, therefore Monday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 3).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3153525				0	sk	=WEEKDAY("1996-07-24";1) returns 4 (the Type parameter is 1, therefore Sunday is day number 1. July 24, 1996 was a Wednesday and therefore day number 4).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150575				0	sk	=WEEKDAY(NOW()) returns the number of the current day.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_weekday.xhp	0	help	par_id3150588	171			0	sk	To obtain a function indicating whether a day in A1 is a business day, use the IF and WEEKDAY functions as follows: \<br/\>IF(WEEKDAY(A1;2)<6;"Business day";"Weekend")				20200411 15:09:53
