helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149979				0	sk	The formula in E2 is as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155849	82			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SYD($A$2;$B$2;$C$2;D2)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3156124				0	sk	This formula is duplicated in column E down to E11 (select E2, then drag down the lower right corner with the mouse).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3147270				0	sk	Cell E13 contains the formula used to check the total of the depreciation amounts. It uses the SUMIF function as the negative values in E8:E11 must not be considered. The condition >0 is contained in cell A13. The formula in E13 is as follows:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	85			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=SUMIF(E2:E11;A13)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155998				0	sk	Now view the depreciation for a 10 year period, or at a salvage value of 1 currency unit, or enter a different initial cost, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
