helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148834				0	sk	A security is purchased on 2001-01-01; the maturity date is 2006-01-01. The Coupon rate of interest is 8%. The yield is 9.0%. Interest is paid half-yearly (frequency is 2). Using daily balance interest calculation (basis 3) how long is the duration?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154902	413			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=DURATION_ADD("2001-01-01";"2006-01-01";0.08;0.09;2;3)\</item\>         				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159147				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>calculating; annual net interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>net annual interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECTIVE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159147				0	sk	EFFECTIVE				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154204				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_EFFEKTIV\"\>Returns the net annual interest rate for a nominal interest rate.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3145417				0	sk	Nominal interest refers to the amount of interest due at the end of a calculation period. Effective interest increases with the number of payments made. In other words, interest is often paid in installments (for example, monthly or quarterly) before the end of the calculation period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150510				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3148805				0	sk	EFFECTIVE(Nom; P)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149768	93			0	sk	            \<emph\>Nom\</emph\> is the nominal interest.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149334	94			0	sk	            \<emph\>P\</emph\> is the number of interest payment periods per year.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154223				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3144499				0	sk	If the annual nominal interest rate is 9.75% and four interest calculation periods are defined, what is the actual interest rate (effective rate)?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	97			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=EFFECTIVE(9.75%;4)\</item\> = 10.11% The annual effective rate is therefore 10.11%.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060103.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147241				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>effective interest rates\</bookmark_value\>         \<bookmark_value\>EFFECT_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
