helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156396	31			0	sk	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019	32			0	sk	Following you will find a description of those functions, which are called at the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>external DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150038	33			0	sk	For all \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> functions, the following applies:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157876				0	sk	void CALLTYPE fn(out, in1, in2, ...)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147616				0	sk	Output: Resulting value				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159119				0	sk	Input: Any number of types (double&, char*, double*, char**, Cell area), where the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"Cell area\"\>Cell area\</link\> is an array of types double array, string array, or cell array.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653				0	sk	GetFunctionCount()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3152981				0	sk	Returns the number of functions without the management functions of the reference parameter. Each function has a unique number between 0 and nCount-1. This number will be needed for the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetFunctionData\"\>GetFunctionData\</link\> and \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/04060112.xhp\" name=\"GetParameterDescription\"\>GetParameterDescription\</link\> functions later.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150742				0	sk	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148728				0	sk	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionCount(USHORT& nCount)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154677				0	sk	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3146940				0	sk	USHORT &nCount:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149893				0	sk	Output: Reference to a variable, which is supposed to contain the number of Add-In functions. For example: If the Add-In provides 5 functions for $[officename] Calc, then nCount=5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147476				0	sk	GetFunctionData()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154841				0	sk	Determines all the important information about an Add-In function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148888				0	sk	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148434				0	sk	void CALLTYPE GetFunctionData(USHORT& nNo, char* pFuncName, USHORT& nParamCount, Paramtype* peType, char* pInternalName)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149253				0	sk	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149686				0	sk	USHORT& nNo:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149949				0	sk	Input: Function number between 0 and nCount-1, inclusively.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149546				0	sk	char* pFuncName:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148579	52			0	sk	Output: Function name as seen by the programmer, as it is named in the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"UNIX\"\>Shared Library \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>DLL\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>. This name does not determine the name used in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153935				0	sk	USHORT& nParamCount:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3150142				0	sk	Output: Number of parameters in AddIn function. This number must be greater than 0, because there is always a result value; the maximum value is 16.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145143				0	sk	Paramtype* peType:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148750				0	sk	Output: Pointer to an array of exactly 16 variables of type Paramtype. The first nParamCount entries are filled with the suitable type of parameter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153078				0	sk	char* pInternalName:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155261				0	sk	Output: Function name as seen by the user, as it appears in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>. May contain umlauts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153327				0	sk	The pFuncName and pInternalName parameters are char arrays, which are implemented with size 256 in $[officename] Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148567				0	sk	GetParameterDescription()				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153000				0	sk	Provides a brief description of the Add-In function and its parameters. As an option, this function can be used to show a function and parameter description in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154501				0	sk	\<emph\>Syntax\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3153564				0	sk	void CALLTYPE GetParameterDescription(USHORT& nNo, USHORT& nParam, char* pName, char* pDesc)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3157995				0	sk	\<emph\>Parameter\</emph\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3155925				0	sk	USHORT& nNo:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3149883				0	sk	Input: Number of the function in the library; between 0 and nCount-1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3154326				0	sk	USHORT& nParam:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3159139				0	sk	Input: Indicates, for which parameter the description is provided; parameters start at 1. If nParam is 0, the description itself is supposed to be provided in pDesc; in this case, pName does not have any meaning.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3147374				0	sk	char* pName:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145245				0	sk	Output: Takes up the parameter name or type, for example, the word "Number" or "String" or "Date", and so on. Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3151020				0	sk	char* pDesc:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3148389				0	sk	Output: Takes up the description of the parameter, for example, "Value, at which the universe is to be calculated." Implemented in $[officename] Calc as char[256].				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060112.xhp	0	help	par_id3145303				0	sk	pName and pDesc are char arrays; implemented in $[officename] Calc with size 256. Please note that the space available in the \<emph\>Function Wizard\</emph\> is limited and that the 256 characters cannot be fully used.				20200411 15:09:53
