helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154511				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>MAX function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154511				0	sk	MAX				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153709				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MAX\"\>Returns the maximum value in a list of arguments.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id9282509				0	sk	Returns 0 if no numeric value and no error was encountered in the cell range(s) passed as cell reference(s). Text cells are ignored by MIN() and MAX(). The functions MINA() and MAXA() return 0 if no value (numeric or text) and no error was encountered. Passing a literal string argument to MIN() or MAX(), e.g. MIN("string"), still results in an error.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147340				0	sk	MAX(Number1; Number2; ...Number30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149568	6			0	sk	\<emph\>Number1; Number2;...Number30\</emph\> are numerical values or ranges. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153963				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147343				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1;A2;A3;50;100;200)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MAX(A1:B100)\</item\> returns the largest value from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166426				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>MAXA function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
