helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3151339	217			0	sk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the positive integer to be converted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3159262	218			0	sk	            \<emph\>Radix\</emph\> indicates the base of the number system. It may be any positive integer between 2 and 36.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060110.xhp	0	help	par_id3148746	219			0	sk	            \<emph\>MinimumLength\</emph\> (optional) determines the minimum length of the character sequence that has been created. If the text is shorter than the indicated minimum length, zeros are added to the left of the string.				20200411 15:09:53
