helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3147363				0	sk	The cells for the 1st and 2nd quarters each contain a sum formula for the three cells to their left. If you apply the \<emph\>AutoOutline\</emph\> command, the table is grouped into two quarters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\12080500.xhp	0	help	par_id3146918				0	sk	To remove the outline, select the table, and then choose \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12080600.xhp\" name=\"Data - Group and Outline - Remove\"\>Data - Group and Outline - Remove\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	DATEVALUE 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145621				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>DATEVALUE function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145621				0	sk	\<variable id=\"datevalue\"\>\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/func_datevalue.xhp\"\>DATEVALUE\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3145087				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_DATWERT\"\>Returns the internal date number for text in quotes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	sk	The internal date number is returned as a number. The number is determined by the date system that is used by $[officename] to calculate dates.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id0119200903491982				0	sk	If the text string also includes a time value, DATEVALUE only returns the integer part of the conversion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156294				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3149268				0	sk	DATEVALUE("Text")				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3154819	23			0	sk	         \<emph\>Text\</emph\> is a valid date expression and must be entered with quotation marks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156309				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_datevalue.xhp	0	help	par_id3155841	25			0	sk	         \<emph\>=DATEVALUE("1954-07-20")\</emph\> yields 19925.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153087				0	sk	Protecting Sheet				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	sk	\<variable id=\"tabelletext\"\>\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Protects the cells in the current sheet from being modified.\</ahelp\>\</variable\> Choose \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Protect Sheet\</emph\> dialog in which you then specify sheet protection with or without a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149664				0	sk	To protect cells from further editing, the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> check box must be checked on the \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/05020600.xhp\" name=\"Format - Cells - Cell Protection\"\>\<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>\</link\> tab page or on the \<emph\>Format Cells\</emph\> context menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	8			0	sk	Unprotected cells or cell ranges can be set up on a protected sheet by using the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> and \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> menus: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149123				0	sk	Select the cells that will be unprotected				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150329				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\>. Unmark the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156384				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> menu, activate protection for the sheet. Effective immediately, only the cell range you selected in step 1 can be edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149566	9			0	sk	To later change an unprotected area to a protected area, select the range. Next, on the \<emph\>Format - Cells - Cell Protection\</emph\> tab page, check the \<emph\>Protected\</emph\> box. Finally, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet \</emph\>menu. The previously editable range is now protected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3153964				0	sk	Sheet protection also affects the context menu of the sheet tabs at the bottom of the screen. The \<emph\>Delete\</emph\> and \<emph\>Rename\</emph\> commands cannot be selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150301				0	sk	If a sheet is protected, you will not be able to modify or delete any Cell Styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	sk	A protected sheet or cell range can no longer be modified until this protection is disabled. To disable the protection, choose the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document - Sheet\</emph\> command. If no password was set, the sheet protection is immediately disabled. If the sheet was password protected, the \<emph\>Remove Protection\</emph\> dialog opens, where you must enter the password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149815				0	sk	Once saved, protected sheets can only be saved again by using the \<emph\>File - Save As\</emph\> command.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150206				0	sk	Password (optional)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152990				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:Protect\"\>Allows you to enter a password to protect the sheet from unauthorized changes.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06060100.xhp	0	help	par_id3148700				0	sk	Complete protection of your work can be achieved by combining both options on the \<emph\>Tools - Protect Document\</emph\> menu, including password protection. To prohibit opening the document altogether, in the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> dialog mark the \<emph\>Save with password\</emph\> box before you click the \<emph\>Save\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Označiť neplatné dáta				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153821				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>cells; invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>data; showing invalid data\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>invalid data;marking\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153821				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/scalc/01/06030800.xhp\" name=\"Mark Invalid Data\"\>Mark Invalid Data\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3147264				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:ShowInvalid\" visibility=\"visible\"\>Marks all cells in the sheet that contain values outside the validation rules.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\06030800.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211				0	sk	The \<link href=\"text/scalc/01/12120000.xhp\" name=\"validity rules\"\>validity rules\</link\> restrict the input of numbers, dates, time values and text to certain values. However, it is possible to enter invalid values or copy invalid values into the cells if the \<emph\>Stop\</emph\> option is not selected. When you assign a validity rule, existing values in a cell will not be modified.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\func_eastersunday.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	EASTERSUNDAY				20200411 15:09:53
