helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154573	168			0	sk	            \<emph\>Data\</emph\> is the array or range of data in the sample.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3156334	169			0	sk	            \<emph\>Probability\</emph\> is the array or range of the corresponding probabilities.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151107	170			0	sk	            \<emph\>Start\</emph\> is the start value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153694	171			0	sk	            \<emph\>End\</emph\> (optional) is the end value of the interval whose probabilities are to be summed. If this parameter is missing, the probability for the \<emph\>Start \</emph\>value is calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147574				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3153666	173			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=PROB(A1:A50;B1:B50;50;60)\</item\> returns the probability with which a value within the range of A1:A50 is also within the limits between 50 and 60. Every value within the range of A1:A50 has a probability within the range of B1:B50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150941				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>WEIBULL function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150941				0	sk	WEIBULL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154916				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_WEIBULL\"\>Returns the values of the Weibull distribution.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372767				0	sk	The Weibull distribution is a continuous probability distribution, with parameters Alpha > 0 (shape) and Beta > 0 (scale). 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372777				0	sk	If C is 0, WEIBULL calculates the probability density function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372743				0	sk	If C is 1, WEIBULL calculates the cumulative distribution function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159393				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154478				0	sk	WEIBULL(Number; Alpha; Beta; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3151317	179			0	sk	            \<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value at which to calculate the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3158436	180			0	sk	            \<emph\>Alpha \</emph\>is the shape parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154668	181			0	sk	            \<emph\>Beta\</emph\> is the scale parameter of the Weibull distribution.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3154825	182			0	sk	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> indicates the type of function.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153794				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id3146077	184			0	sk	            \<item type=\"input\"\>=WEIBULL(2;1;1;1)\</item\> returns 0.86.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060185.xhp	0	help	par_id0305200911372899				0	sk	See also the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/How_Tos/Calc:_WEIBULL_function\"\>Wiki page\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
