helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154914				0	sk	If you enter the numbers \<item type=\"input\"\>512\</item\>;\<item type=\"input\"\>1024\</item\> and \<item type=\"input\"\>2000\</item\> in the Integer 1;2 and 3 text boxes, 128000 will be returned as the result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154230				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>LCM_ADD function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154230				0	sk	LCM_ADD				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3149036				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AAI_FUNC_LCM\"\> The result is the lowest common multiple of a list of numbers.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153132				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154395				0	sk	LCM_ADD(Number(s))				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3147377				0	sk	\<emph\>Number(s)\</emph\> is a list of up to 30 numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145122				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145135				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LCM_ADD(5;15;25)\</item\> returns 75.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155802				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>COMBIN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155802				0	sk	COMBIN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3156172				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN\"\>Returns the number of combinations for elements without repetition.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223				0	sk	COMBIN(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150313				0	sk	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153830				0	sk	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id6807458				0	sk	COMBIN returns the number of ordered ways to choose these items. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 3 different ways, namely AB, AC and BC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7414471				0	sk	COMBIN implements the formula: Count1!/(Count2!*(Count1-Count2)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153171				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153517				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBIN(3;2)\</item\> returns 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150284				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>COMBINA function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>number of combinations with repetitions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150284				0	sk	COMBINA				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157894				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KOMBINATIONEN2\"\>Returns the number of combinations of a subset of items including repetitions.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145752				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145765				0	sk	COMBINA(Count1; Count2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153372				0	sk	\<emph\>Count1\</emph\> is the number of items in the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155544				0	sk	\<emph\>Count2\</emph\> is the number of items to choose from the set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id1997131				0	sk	COMBINA returns the number of unique ways to choose these items, where the order of choosing is irrelevant, and repetition of items is allowed. For example if there are 3 items A, B and C in a set, you can choose 2 items in 6 different ways, namely AA, AB, AC, BB, BC and CC.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2052064				0	sk	COMBINA implements the formula: (Count1+Count2-1)! / (Count2!(Count1-1)!)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154584				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152904				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=COMBINA(3;2)\</item\> returns 6.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156086				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>TRUNC function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>decimal places;cutting off\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156086				0	sk	TRUNC				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157866				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_KUERZEN\"\>Truncates a number by removing decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148499				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148511				0	sk	TRUNC(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150796				0	sk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> with at most \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. Excess decimal places are simply removed, irrespective of sign.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3150816				0	sk	\<item type=\"literal\"\>TRUNC(Number; 0)\</item\> behaves as \<item type=\"literal\"\>INT(Number)\</item\> for positive numbers, but effectively rounds towards zero for negative numbers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3148548				0	sk	The \<emph\>visible\</emph\> decimal places of the result are specified in \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01060500.xhp\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Calc - Calculate\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152555				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152569				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(1.239;2)\</item\> returns 1.23. The 9 is lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id7050080				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=TRUNC(-1.234999;3)\</item\> returns -1.234. All the 9s are lost.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153601				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>LN function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>natural logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153601				0	sk	LN				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154974				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LN\"\>Returns the natural logarithm based on the constant e of a number.\</ahelp\> The constant e has a value of approximately 2.71828182845904.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154993				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155284				0	sk	LN(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155297				0	sk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose natural logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153852				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153866				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(3)\</item\> returns the natural logarithm of 3 (approximately 1.0986).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5747245				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LN(EXP(321))\</item\> returns 321.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109813				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>LOG function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>logarithms\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109813				0	sk	LOG				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3109841				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG\"\>Returns the logarithm of a number to the specified base.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3144719				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144732				0	sk	LOG(Number; Base)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3144746				0	sk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the value whose logarithm is to be calculated.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3152840				0	sk	\<emph\>Base\</emph\> (optional) is the base for the logarithm calculation. If omitted, Base 10 is assumed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152860				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3154429				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(10;3)\</item\> returns the logarithm to base 3 of 10 (approximately 2.0959).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id5577562				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG(7^4;7)\</item\> returns 4.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154187				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>LOG10 function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>base-10 logarithm\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154187				0	sk	LOG10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155476				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_LOG10\"\>Returns the base-10 logarithm of a number.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155494				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159294				0	sk	LOG10(Number)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3159308				0	sk	Returns the logarithm to base 10 of \<emph\>Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159328				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157916				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=LOG10(5)\</item\> returns the base-10 logarithm of 5 (approximately 0.69897).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152518				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>CEILING function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rounding;up to multiples of significance\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152518				0	sk	CEILING				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153422				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_OBERGRENZE\"\>Rounds a number up to the nearest multiple of Significance.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153440				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153454				0	sk	CEILING(Number; Significance; Mode)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3153467				0	sk	\<emph\>Number\</emph\> is the number that is to be rounded up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155000				0	sk	\<emph\>Significance\</emph\> is the number to whose multiple the value is to be rounded up.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3155020				0	sk	\<emph\>Mode\</emph\> is an optional value. If the Mode value is given and not equal to zero, and if Number and Significance are negative, then rounding is done based on the absolute value of Number. This parameter is ignored when exporting to MS Excel as Excel does not know any third parameter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3163792				0	sk	If both parameters Number and Significance are negative and the Mode value is equal to zero or is not given, the results in $[officename] and Excel will differ after the import has been completed. If you export the spreadsheet to Excel, use Mode=1 to see the same results in Excel as in Calc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145697				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145710				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2)\</item\> returns -10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145725				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;0)\</item\> returns -10				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3145740				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=CEILING(-11;-2;1)\</item\> returns -12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3157762				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>PI function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3157762				0	sk	PI				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3157790				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PI\"\>Returns 3.14159265358979, the value of the mathematical constant PI to 14 decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
