helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	bm_id3158121				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>ROUND function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158121				0	sk	ROUND				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158150				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_RUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number to a certain number of decimal places.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3158169				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158182				0	sk	ROUND(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3158196				0	sk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds to the nearest integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds to the nearest 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id599688				0	sk	This function rounds to the nearest number. See ROUNDDOWN and ROUNDUP for alternatives.				20200411 15:09:53
