helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146020				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_ABRUNDEN\"\>Rounds a number down, toward zero, to a certain precision.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146037				0	sk	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146051				0	sk	ROUNDDOWN(Number; Count)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id3146064				0	sk	Returns \<emph\>Number\</emph\> rounded down (towards zero) to \<emph\>Count\</emph\> decimal places. If Count is omitted or zero, the function rounds down to an integer. If Count is negative, the function rounds down to the next 10, 100, 1000, etc.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060106.xhp	0	help	par_id2188787				0	sk	This function rounds towards zero. See ROUNDUP and ROUND for alternatives.				20200411 15:09:53
