helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154800				0	sk	What is the net present value of periodic payments of 10, 20 and 30 currency units with a discount rate of 8.75%. At time zero the costs were paid as -40 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3143270				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=NPV(8.75%;10;20;30)\</item\> = 49.43 currency units. The net present value is the returned value minus the initial costs of 40 currency units, therefore 9.43 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
