helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156360				0	sk	\<emph\>PV\</emph\> is the present value (cash value) in a sequence of payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154920				0	sk	\<emph\>FV\</emph\> (optional) is the desired value (future value) to be reached at the end of the periodic payments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3156434				0	sk	\<emph\>Type\</emph\> (optional) is the due date for the periodic payments. Type=1 is payment at the beginning and Type=0 is payment at the end of each period.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_idN11645				0	sk	\<embedvar href=\"text/scalc/00/00000004.xhp#optional\"/\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152358				0	sk	Príklad				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3154222				0	sk	What are the periodic payments at a yearly interest rate of 1.99% if the payment time is 3 years and the cash value is 25,000 currency units. There are 36 months as 36 payment periods, and the interest rate per payment period is 1.99%/12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	par_id3155943				0	sk	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PMT(1.99%/12;36;25000)\</item\> = -715.96 currency units. The periodic monthly payment is therefore 715.96 currency units.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060119.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155799				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>TBILLEQ function\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>treasury bills;annual return\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>annual return on treasury bills\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
