helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436				0	sk	\<variable id=\"eyedropper\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/eyedropper.xhp\" name=\"Replacing Colors\"\>Replacing Colors\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3156286				0	sk	You can replace colors in bitmaps with the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> tool.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154704				0	sk	Up to four colors can be replaced at once.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3147344				0	sk	You can also use the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> option to replace the transparent areas of an image with a color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	sk	Similarly, you can use the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> to make a color on your image transparent.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205				0	sk	To replace colors with the Color Replacer tool				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3154656				0	sk	Ensure that the image you are using is a bitmap (for example, BMP, GIF, JPG, or PNG) or a metafile (for example, WMF).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3150202				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Color Replacer\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531				0	sk	Click the Color Replacer icon and position the mouse pointer over the color you want to replace in the image. The color appears in the box next to the icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3152985				0	sk	Click the color in the image. The color appears in the first \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> box and the check box next to the color is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3148866				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Replace with\</emph\> box, select the new color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3145362				0	sk	This replaces all occurrences of the \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the image.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3151191				0	sk	If you want to replace another color while the dialog is open, select the check box in front of \<emph\>Source color\</emph\> in the next row and repeat steps 3 to 5.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3149876				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Replace\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3157871				0	sk	If you want to expand or contract the color selection area, increase or decrease the tolerance of the \<emph\>Color Replacer\</emph\> tool and repeat your selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\eyedropper.xhp	0	help	par_id3146878				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06030000.xhp\" name=\"Color Replacer\"\>Color Replacer\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
