helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156442				0	sk	\<variable id=\"join_objects3d\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/join_objects3d.xhp\" name=\"Assembling 3D Objects\"\>Assembling 3D Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3145251				0	sk	3D objects that each form a 3D scene can be combined into a single 3D scene.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150042				0	sk	To combine 3D objects:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154702				0	sk	Insert a 3D object from the \<emph\>3D Objects\</emph\> toolbar (for example, a cube).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155335				0	sk	Insert a second slightly larger 3D object (for example, a sphere).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148488				0	sk	Select the second 3D object (sphere) and choose \<emph\>Edit - Cut\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3149211				0	sk	Double-click the first object (cube) to enter its group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3154652				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Edit - Paste\</emph\>. Both objects are now part of the same group. If you want, you can edit the individual objects or change their position within the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3155376				0	sk	Double-click outside the group to exit the group.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\join_objects3d.xhp	0	help	par_id3148606				0	sk	You cannot intersect or subtract 3D objects.				20200411 15:09:53
