helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145086				0	sk	\<variable id=\"load_styles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/load_styles.xhp\" name=\"Using Styles From Another Document or Template\"\>Using Styles From Another Document or Template\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491				0	sk	You can import styles from another document or template into the current document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3155910				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> to open the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN10703				0	sk	Click the arrow next to the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon to open the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_idN1070B				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Load styles\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3149632				0	sk	Use the check boxes at the bottom of the dialog to select the style types that you want to import. To replace styles in the current document that have the same name as the ones you are importing, select \<emph\>Overwrite\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145098				0	sk	Vykonajte jednu z nasledujúcich možností:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	sk	Click an entry in the \<emph\>Categories\</emph\> list, then click the template containing the styles that you want to use in the \<emph\>Templates\</emph\> list, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\load_styles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153377				0	sk	Click \<emph\>From File\</emph\>, locate the file containing the styles that you want to use, and then click name, and then click \<emph\>Open\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using Wildcards in Text Searches				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150099				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>wildcards, see regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>searching; with wildcards\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>regular expressions;searching\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>examples for regular expressions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>characters;finding all\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>invisible characters;finding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraph marks;searching\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150099				0	sk	\<variable id=\"search_regexp\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/search_regexp.xhp\"\>Using Wildcards in Text Searches\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345516				0	sk	Wildcards or placeholders can be used to search for some unspecified or even invisible characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155182				0	sk	You can use wildcards when you find and replace text in a document. For example, "s.n" finds "sun" and "son".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Find & Replace\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id2142399				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More Options\</item\> to expand the dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3155861				0	sk	Select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Regular expressions\</item\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Search for\</item\> box, type the search term and the wildcard(s) that you want to use in your search.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3156113				0	sk	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Find All\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153401				0	sk	Regular Expression Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641				0	sk	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136				0	sk	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609				0	sk	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854				0	sk	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id0509200916345545				0	sk	The wildcard for a tab character is \\t.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	sk	A search using a regular expression will work only within one paragraph. To search using a regular expression in more than one paragraph, do a separate search in each paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149875				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02100001.xhp\" name=\"List of Wildcards\"\>List of Wildcards\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149832				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>multi-column text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; multi-column\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; on text pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections; columns in/use of\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	sk	\<variable id=\"sections\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/sections.xhp\" name=\"Using Sections\"\>Using Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	sk	Sections are named blocks of text, including graphics or objects, that you can use in a number of ways:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149284				0	sk	To prevent text from being edited.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149630				0	sk	To show or hide text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149647				0	sk	To reuse text and graphics from other $[officename] documents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	sk	To insert sections of text that uses a different column layout than the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149855				0	sk	A section contains at least one paragraph. When you select a text and create a section, a paragraph break is automatically inserted at the end of the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3149872				0	sk	You can insert sections from a text document, or an entire text document as a section into another text document. You can also insert sections from a text document as links in another text document, or in the same document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3153367	39			0	sk	To insert a new paragraph immediately before or after a section, click in front or behind the section, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Enter.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	sk	Sections and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sk	You can insert sections into an existing section. For example, you can insert a section containing two columns into a section that contains one column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3154845				0	sk	A section layout, for example on the number of columns, has priority over the page layout defined in a page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\sections.xhp	0	help	par_id3155883				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/00/00000005.xhp#dde\" name=\"DDE\"\>DDE\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147407				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>numbering; lists, while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;creating while typing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lists;automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbers;lists\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic bullets/numbers; AutoCorrect function\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>bullets; using automatically\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs; automatic numbering\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147407				0	sk	\<variable id=\"auto_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\"\>Creating Numbered or Bulleted Lists as You Type\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155525				0	sk	$[officename] can automatically apply numbering or bullets as you type.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154243				0	sk	To Enable Automatic Numbering and Bulleting				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152830	29			0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Options\</item\> tab, and then select “Apply numbering – symbol”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3152867				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - AutoCorrect\</emph\>, and ensure that \<emph\>While Typing\</emph\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id2357860				0	sk	The automatic numbering option is only applied to paragraphs that are formatted with the "Default", "Text body", or "Text body indent" paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152897				0	sk	To Create a Numbered or Bulleted List While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147773				0	sk	Type 1., i., or I. to start a numbered list. Type * or - to start a bulleted list. You can also type a right parenthesis after the number instead of a period , for example, 1) or i).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147794				0	sk	Enter a space, type your text, and then press Enter. The new paragraph automatically receives the next number or bullet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147814				0	sk	Press Enter again to finish the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147287				0	sk	You can start a numbered list with any number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154083				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06050000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Numbering/Bullets\"\>Format - Bullets and Numbering\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
