helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145083				0	sk	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\"\>Inserting Graphics From the Gallery With Drag-and-Drop\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907				0	sk	You can drag-and-drop an object from the gallery into a text document, spreadsheet, drawing, or presentation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155923				0	sk	To replace a gallery object that you inserted in a document, hold down Shift+Ctrl, and then drag a different gallery object onto the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145084				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; styles, by fill format mode\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>brush for copying styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles; transferring\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text formats; copying and pasting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145084				0	sk	\<variable id=\"stylist_fillformat\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/stylist_fillformat.xhp\" name=\"Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\"\>Applying Styles in Fill Format Mode\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	sk	You can quickly apply styles, such as paragraph and character styles, in your document by using the Fill Format Mode in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3156114				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153128				0	sk	Click the icon of the style category that you want to apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3145090	17			0	sk	Click the style, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Fill Format Mode\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149644\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_fillstyle.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149644\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371				0	sk	Move the mouse pointer to where you want to apply the style in the document, and click. To apply the style to more than one item, drag to select the items, and then release.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	sk	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> when finished.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\stylist_fillformat.xhp	0	help	par_id3159259				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05140000.xhp\" name=\"Styles and Formatting\"\>Styles and Formatting\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920				0	sk	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263				0	sk	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105				0	sk	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	sk	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929				0	sk	Open a new text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510				0	sk	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750				0	sk	Select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\> box, select "Left Page".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
