helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149687				0	sk	\<variable id=\"indices_literature\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_literature.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Bibliography\"\>Creating a Bibliography\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155864				0	sk	A bibliography is a list of works that you reference in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153402				0	sk	Storing Bibliographic Information				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	sk	$[officename] stores bibliographic information in a bibliography database, or in an individual document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244				0	sk	To Store Information in the Bibliography Database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	sk	Choose \<link href=\"text/shared/01/02250000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Bibliography Database\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Bibliography Database\</emph\>\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3155900				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Record\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147123				0	sk	Type a name for the bibliography entry in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\> box, and then add additional information to the record in the remaining boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219	66			0	sk	Close the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bibliography Database\</item\> window. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150242				0	sk	To Store Bibliographic Information in an Individual Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150945				0	sk	Click in your document where you want to add the bibliography entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964				0	sk	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120300.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3150525				0	sk	Select \<emph\>From document content\</emph\> and click \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153738				0	sk	Type a name for the bibliography entry in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153763				0	sk	Select the publication source for the record in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box, and then add additional information in the remaining boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3146873				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3146897				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert Bibliography Entry\</item\> dialog, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150741				0	sk	Inserting Bibliography Entries From the Bibliography Database				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3148402				0	sk	Click in your document where you want to add the bibliography entry.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3148421				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Bibliography Entry\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3153231				0	sk	Select \<emph\>From bibliography database\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147059				0	sk	Select the name of the bibliography entry that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Short name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3147085				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id3156060				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120300.xhp\" name=\"Bibliography Database\"\>Bibliography Database\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_literature.xhp	0	help	par_id6367076				0	sk	Some external tools exist that can interact with %PRODUCTNAME. One example is called \<link href=\"http://bibus-biblio.sourceforge.net/wiki/index.php/Main_Page\"\>Bibus\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	bm_id7693411				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>selecting;tables\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>tables;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>columns;selecting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rows;selecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN105F0				0	sk	\<variable id=\"table_select\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_select.xhp\"\>Selecting Tables, Rows, and Columns\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN1060E				0	sk	You can select a table in a text document with a keyboard or with a mouse.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10614				0	sk	To select a table with the keyboard, move the cursor into the table, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+A until all the cells are selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10633				0	sk	To select a table with the mouse, move the mouse pointer to a position just above and left of the table. The mouse pointer becomes a diagonal arrow. Click to select the table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_select.xhp	0	help	par_idN10637				0	sk	To select a row or column with the mouse, point to a position just left of the row or above the column. The mouse pointer becomes an arrow. Click to select the row or column.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>indexes; editing/updating/deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents; editing and deleting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;indexes/tables of contents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	sk	\<variable id=\"indices_edit\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_edit.xhp\" name=\"Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\"\>Updating, Editing and Deleting Indexes and Tables of Contents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155856				0	sk	Place the cursor in the index or table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155871				0	sk	If you cannot place your cursor in the index or table of contents, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</item\>, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Enable\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Cursor in protected areas\</item\> section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3154248				0	sk	Right-click and choose an editing option from the menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3155872				0	sk	You can also make changes directly to an index or table of contents. Right-click in the index or table of contents, choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>, click \<emph\>Index/Table\</emph\> tab, and then clear the \<emph\>Protected from manual changes\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting Sections				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>sections; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents;inserting linked sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;linked sections, manually\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting sections\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	sk	\<variable id=\"section_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/section_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Sections\"\>Inserting Sections\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155917				0	sk	You can insert new sections, or links to sections in other documents into the current document. If you insert a section as a link, the content of the link changes when you modify the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	sk	To Insert a New Section				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149843				0	sk	Click in your document where you want to insert a new section, or select the text that you want to convert to a section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156103				0	sk	If you select a text that occurs within a paragraph, the text is automatically converted into a new paragraph.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149281				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	sk	Set the options for the section, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149635				0	sk	To Insert a Section as a Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149648				0	sk	Before you can insert a section as link, you must first create sections in the source document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	sk	When you open a document that contains linked sections, $[officename] prompts you to update the contents of the sections. To manually update a link, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Links\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149860				0	sk	You can also insert linked sections in HTML documents. When you view the page in a web browser, the content of the sections corresponds to the content of the sections at the time the HTML document was last saved.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145104				0	sk	Click in your document where you want to insert the linked section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3156241				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>New Section\</item\> box, type a name for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153387				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> area, select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link\</item\> check box. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>Under Windows, you can also select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>DDE\</item\> check box to automatically update the contents of the section when the section in the source document is changed.\</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154852				0	sk	Click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File name\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155882				0	sk	Locate the document containing the section that you want to link to, and then click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3149978				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Section\</item\> box, select the section that you want to insert.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\section_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150003				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using the Direct Cursor				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155178				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>text; cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>entering text with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>direct cursor; settings\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>writing with direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>cursor;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>settings;direct cursor\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155178				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_direct_cursor\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_direct_cursor.xhp\" name=\"Using the Direct Cursor\"\>Using the Direct Cursor\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155908				0	sk	The direct cursor allows you to enter text anywhere on a page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_id3155921				0	sk	To set the behavior of the direct cursor, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106A3				0	sk	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools\</item\> bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Direct Cursor\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3149846\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_shadowcursor.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3149846\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	sk	Click in a free space in the text document. The mouse pointer changes to reflect the alignment that will be applied to the text that you type:				20200411 15:09:53
