helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN10700				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id6953622\" src=\"res/helpimg/dircursright.png\" width=\"0.1563in\" height=\"0.3228in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id6953622\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> Align right				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_direct_cursor.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	sk	Type your text. %PRODUCTNAME automatically inserts the required number of blank lines, and, if the options are enabled, tabs and spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Delenie slov				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;manual/automatic\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>separation, see hyphenation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>automatic hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>manual hyphenation in text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695				0	sk	\<variable id=\"using_hyphen\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\" name=\"Hyphenation\"\>Hyphenation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155918	31			0	sk	By default, $[officename] moves words that do not fit on a line to the next line. If you want, you can use automatic or manual hyphenation to avoid this behavior: 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155864				0	sk	Automatic Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3147414				0	sk	Automatic hyphenation inserts hyphens where they are needed in a paragraph. This option is only available for paragraph styles and individual paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149832				0	sk	To Automatically Hyphenate Text in a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3148850				0	sk	Right-click in a paragraph, and choose \<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156104				0	sk	Click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>\<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3150101				0	sk	In the Hyphenation area, select the Automatically check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153121				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149629				0	sk	To Automatically Hyphenate Text in Multiple Paragraphs				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149644				0	sk	If you want to automatically hyphenate more than one paragraph, use a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	sk	For example, enable the automatic hyphenation option for the "Default" paragraph style, and then apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149611				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149867				0	sk	Right-click the paragraph style that you want to hyphenate, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145106				0	sk	Click the Text Flow tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3149582				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Hyphenation\</emph\> area, select the \<emph\>Automatically\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3156250				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3145400				0	sk	Apply the style to the paragraphs that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145417				0	sk	Manual Hyphenation				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154400				0	sk	You can insert a hyphen where you want on a line, or let $[officename] search for the words to hyphenate, and then offer a suggested hyphenation.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help					0	sk	To Manually Hyphenate Single Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3153363				0	sk	To quickly insert a hyphen, click in the word where you want to add the hyphen, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Hyphen(-).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154244				0	sk	If you insert a manual hyphen in a word, the word is only hyphenated at the manual hyphen. No additional automatic hyphenation is applied for this word. A word with a manual hyphen will be hyphenated without regard to the settings on the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154847				0	sk	To Manually Hyphenate Text in a Selection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3154869				0	sk	Select the text that you want to hyphenate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\using_hyphen.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Language - Hyphenation\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
