helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Using Rulers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	bm_id8186284				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>rulers;using rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>horizontal rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vertical rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>indents; setting on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>page margins on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table cells;adjusting the width on rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>showing;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>hiding;rulers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>adjusting page margins and cell widths\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1065F				0	sk	\<variable id=\"ruler\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/ruler.xhp\"\>Using Rulers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_idN1067D				0	sk	To show or hide rulers, choose \<emph\>View - Ruler\</emph\>. To show the vertical ruler, choose \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01040200.xhp\" name=\"Writer - View\"\>\<emph\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer - View\</emph\>\</link\>, and then select \<emph\>Vertical ruler\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Ruler\</emph\> area.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149686				0	sk	Adjusting Page Margins				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3155175				0	sk	The margins of a page are indicated by the filled areas at the ends of the rulers.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149038				0	sk	Changing Indents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3153631				0	sk	Indents are adjusted with the three small triangles on the horizontal ruler.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3152776	26			0	sk	To change the left or the right paragraph indent, select the paragraph(s) that you want change the indent for, drag the bottom left or the bottom right triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3145769				0	sk	To change the first line indent of a selected paragraph, drag the top left triangle on the horizontal ruler to a new location.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\ruler.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164				0	sk	You can also double-click anywhere on the horizontal ruler, and adjust the indents in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030000.xhp\" name=\"Paragraph\"\>\<emph\>Paragraph\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150620				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>indexes;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables of contents;unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables;protecting/unprotecting cells\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>unprotecting tables of contents and indexes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>protecting;tables and sections\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cells;protecting/unprotecting\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id6007263				0	sk	\<variable id=\"protection\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/protection.xhp\" name=\"Protecting Content in %PRODUCTNAME Writer\"\>Protecting Content in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME Writer\</item\>\</link\> \</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id1924802				0	sk	The following is an overview of the different ways of protecting contents in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer from being modified, deleted or viewed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150114				0	sk	Protecting Sections in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150592				0	sk	Any section of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text document can be protected against changes with a password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id4545426				0	sk	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the section against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3166413				0	sk	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3144764				0	sk	Select the text. Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section - Section\</emph\>, then under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> mark the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> and \<emph\>With password\</emph\> check boxes. (If the section already exists: \<emph\>Format - Sections\</emph\>.) Enter and confirm a password of at least 5 characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147497				0	sk	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147173				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Sections - Section\</emph\> and under \<emph\>Write protection\</emph\> clear the \<emph\>Protect\</emph\> check box. Enter the correct password.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146081				0	sk	Protecting Cells in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154480				0	sk	You can protect the contents of individual cells of a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text table from changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id363170				0	sk	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the cells against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154360				0	sk	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145643				0	sk	Place the cursor in a cell or select cells. Right-click to open the context menu, then choose \<emph\>Cell - Protect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3150042				0	sk	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	sk	Place the cursor in the cell or select the cells. First, if necessary, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids\</emph\> and mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>. Then right-click the cell to open the context menu, choose \<emph\>Cell - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3151189				0	sk	Select the table in the Navigator, open the context menu and select \<emph\>Table - Unprotect\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3147322				0	sk	Use Shift+Ctrl+T to remove protection for the entire current table or all selected tables.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149259				0	sk	Automatic Protection of Indexes and Tables				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153966				0	sk	Tables of contents and indexes created automatically in a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer text are automatically protected against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id814539				0	sk	This protection is not intended to be a secure protection. It is just a switch to protect the contents against accidental changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3145767				0	sk	Turning on protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3153786				0	sk	Place the cursor in the index/table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3159088				0	sk	V kontextovom menu zvoľte \<emph\>Upraviť Index/Tabuľku\</emph\>. Na záložke Index/Tabuľka označte \<emph\>Zamknuté proti ručným zmenám\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3154118				0	sk	Turning off protection				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3148463	49			0	sk	Place the cursor in the index. First of all, if necessary, under \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Formatting Aids \</emph\>, mark \<emph\>Cursor in protected areas - Enable\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152968				0	sk	From the context menu choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>. On the Index/Table tab page, unmark \<emph\>Protected against manual changes\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\protection.xhp	0	help	par_id3152774				0	sk	In the Navigator, select the index, then open the context menu in the Navigator and select \<emph\>Index - Read-only\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
