helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150229	47			0	sk	Click an index level in the \<emph\>Levels \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150934	48			0	sk	Click the style that you want to apply in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style \</emph\>list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150960				0	sk	Click the assign button \<emph\><\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150516				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146878				0	sk	To Assign Hyperlinks to Entries in a Table of Contents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3146890				0	sk	You can assign a cross-reference as a hyperlink to entries in a table of contents.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150712				0	sk	Right-click in the table of contents, and then choose \<emph\>Edit Index/Table\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3150738				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Entries\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148399				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list click the heading level that you want to assign hyperlinks to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3148424	53			0	sk	In the \<emph\>Structure \</emph\>area, click in the box in front of \<emph\>E#\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3153171				0	sk	Click in the box behind the \<emph\>E\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Hyperlink\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_form.xhp	0	help	par_id3147060				0	sk	Repeat for each heading level that you want to create hyperlinks for, or click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>All\</item\> button to apply the formatting to all levels.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145078				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>tab stops; inserting in lists\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>numbering; changing the level of\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>levels;changing outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bullet lists;changing levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>lowering outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>rising outline levels\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>changing;outline levels\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145078				0	sk	\<variable id=\"insert_tab_innumbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_tab_innumbering.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\"\>Changing the Outline Level of Numbered and Bulleted Lists\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155909				0	sk	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph down one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155859				0	sk	To move a numbered or bulleted paragraph up one outline level, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press Shift+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_tab_innumbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3153403	8			0	sk	To insert a tab between the number or bullet and the paragraph text, click at the beginning of the paragraph, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152999				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>charts;copying from Calc into Writer\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>copying; charts from $[officename] Calc\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;inserting Calc charts\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152999				0	sk	\<variable id=\"insert_graphic_fromchart\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\"\>Inserting a Calc Chart into a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155890				0	sk	You can insert a copy of a chart that is not updated when you modify the chart data in the spreadsheet.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3149054				0	sk	Open the text document that you want to copy the chart to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	sk	Open the spreadsheet containing the chart that you want to copy.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	sk	In the spreadsheet, click the chart. Eight handles appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414				0	sk	Drag the chart from the spreadsheet to the text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\insert_graphic_fromchart.xhp	0	help	par_id3145102				0	sk	You can resize and move the chart in the text document as you would any object. To edit the chart data, double-click the chart.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Creating a Form Letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159257				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>serial letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>form letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mail merge\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>letters; creating form letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>wizards;form letters\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159257				0	sk	\<variable id=\"form_letters\"\>\<variable id=\"form_letters_main\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/form_letters_main.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Form Letter\"\>Creating a Form Letter\</link\>\</variable\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id3150502				0	sk	To create a form letter, you need a text document that contains fields for address data, and an address database. Then you combine or merge the address data and the text document to either print the letters or send them by e-mail.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id0805200801132382				0	sk	If the document is in HTML format, any embedded or linked images will not be sent with the e-mail.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10653				0	sk	The \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/mailmerge00.xhp\"\>Mail Merge Wizard\</link\> helps you to create form letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10664				0	sk	To create a form letter				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN1066B				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Mail Merge Wizard\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10672				0	sk	You see the Mail Merge Wizard dialog. The following is an example of one of many possible ways to navigate the wizard's pages:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10676				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Start from a template\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Browse\</emph\> button.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10681				0	sk	You see the \<emph\>New\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN10685				0	sk	Select \<item type=\"literal\"\>Business Correspondence\</item\> in the left list, and then \<item type=\"literal\"\>Modern letter\</item\> in the right list. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\> to close the Templates dialog, and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> in the wizard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_id2669759				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Letter\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106BD				0	sk	On the next step of the wizard, click the \<emph\>Select Address List\</emph\> button to check that you are using the correct address list. Select an address block type, match the data fields if necessary, and click \<emph\>Next\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106C5				0	sk	Next follows the \<emph\>Create a salutation\</emph\> step. Deselect the \<emph\>Insert personalized salutation\</emph\> box. Under \<emph\>General salutation\</emph\>, select the salutation that you want on top of all letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\form_letters_main.xhp	0	help	par_idN106D5				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Next\</emph\> and finally \<emph\>Finish\</emph\> to create the mail merge.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Animating Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	bm_id3151182				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>effects; text animation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>animations;text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151182				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_animation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_animation.xhp\" name=\"Animating Text\"\>Animating Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	sk	You can only animate text that is contained in a drawing object, such as rectangles, lines, or text objects. For example, draw a rectangle, then double-click the rectangle and enter your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149811				0	sk	Select the drawing object containing the text that you want to animate.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3155178				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Object - Text Attributes\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Animation\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3149819				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Effect\</item\> box, select the animation that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_animation.xhp	0	help	par_id3145786				0	sk	Set the properties of the effect, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145246				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>Navigator;master documents\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>master documents;creating/editing/exporting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>subdocuments;creating/editing/removing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>removing;subdocuments\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>indexes; master documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145246				0	sk	\<variable id=\"globaldoc_howtos\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/globaldoc_howtos.xhp\"\>Working with Master Documents and Subdocuments\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id1522873				0	sk	A master document lets you manage large documents, such as a book with many chapters. The master document can be seen as a container for individual \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Writer files. The individual files are called subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153127				0	sk	To Create a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149634				0	sk	Vykonajte jednu z nasledujúcich možností:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149956				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - New - Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	sk	Open an existing document and choose \<emph\>File - Send - Create Master Document\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149873				0	sk	If you are creating a new master document, the first entry in the Navigator should be a \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text\</item\> entry. Type an introduction or enter some text. This ensures that after having edited an existing style in the master document, you see the changed style when viewing the subdocuments.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145114				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Navigator\</item\> for master documents (should open automatically, else press F5 to open), click and hold the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> icon, and do one of the following:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3156240				0	sk	To insert an existing file as a subdocument, choose \<emph\>File\</emph\>, locate the file that you want to include, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145405				0	sk	To create a new subdocument, choose \<emph\>New Document\</emph\>, type a name for the file, and then click \<emph\>Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8550981				0	sk	To insert some text between subdocuments, choose \<emph\>Text\</emph\>. Then type the text. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153382				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Save\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154242				0	sk	To Edit a Master Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sk	Use the Navigator for rearranging and editing the subdocuments in a master document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	sk	To open a subdocument for editing, double-click the name of the subdocument in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3155931				0	sk	To remove a subdocument from the master document, right-click the subdocument in the Navigator list and choose \<emph\>Delete\</emph\>. The subdocument file is not deleted, only the entry in the Navigator is removed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148677				0	sk	To add text to a master document, right-click an item in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Text\</emph\>. A text section is inserted before the selected item in the master document where you can type the text that you want. You cannot insert text next to an existing text entry in the Navigator.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149982				0	sk	To reorder the subdocuments in a master document, drag a subdocument to a new location in the Navigator list. You can also select a subdocument in the list, and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move down\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Move up\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153022				0	sk	To add an index, such as a table of contents, right-click in the Navigator list, and then choose \<emph\>Insert - Index\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148949				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3148959\" src=\"sw/imglst/sc20246.png\" width=\"0.1862in\" height=\"0.1862in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148959\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153632				0	sk	To update an index in a master document, select the index in the Navigator, and then click the \<emph\>Update\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_idN10C40				0	sk	When you insert an object like a frame or a picture into a master document, do not anchor the object "to page". Instead, set the anchor "to paragraph" on the \<emph\>Format - (Object type) - Type\</emph\> tab page, and then set the object's position relative to "Entire Page" in the \<emph\>Horizontal\</emph\> and \<emph\>Vertical\</emph\> list boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153656				0	sk	To Start Each Subdocument on a New Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3152760				0	sk	Ensure that each subdocument starts with a heading that uses the same paragraph style, for example "Heading 1".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153876				0	sk	In the master document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3153907				0	sk	Right-click "Heading 1" and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124				0	sk	Click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Text Flow\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3149770				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Breaks\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>, and then select “Page” in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224				0	sk	If you want each subdocument to start on an odd page, select \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>, and select "Right page" in the box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3145205				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145228				0	sk	To Export a Master Document as a \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3150315				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File - Export\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3148580				0	sk	In the \<emph\>File format\</emph\> list, select a text document file format and click \<emph\>Export\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id8371227				0	sk	The subdocuments will be exported as sections. Use \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Sections\</item\> to unprotect and remove sections, if you prefer a plain text document without sections.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\globaldoc_howtos.xhp	0	help	par_id3154382				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator in master mode\"\>Navigator in master mode\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
