helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155886				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	sk	Place the cursor in the footer and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147134				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Fields\</emph\> dialog, click the \<emph\>Document\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150955				0	sk	Click 'Page' in the \<emph\>Type\</emph\> list and 'Next page' in the \<emph\>Select\</emph\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150517				0	sk	Click a numbering style in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537				0	sk	If you select 'Text' in the \<emph\>Format\</emph\> list, only the text that you enter in the \<emph\>Value\</emph\> box is displayed in the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_nextpage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150727				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> to insert the field with the page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting Page Numbers in Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155624				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>footers; with page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages; numbers and count of\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page numbers; footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;pages\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155624				0	sk	\<variable id=\"footer_pagenumber\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footer_pagenumber.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\"\>Inserting Page Numbers in Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id8230842				0	sk	You can easily insert a page number field in the footer of your document. You can also add a page count to the footer, for example, in the form "Page 9 of 12"				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id7867366				0	sk	To Insert a Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\> and select the page style that you want to add the footer to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3150534				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3153155				0	sk	If you want, you can align the page number field as you would text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	hd_id2988677				0	sk	To Additionally Add a Page Count				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	sk	Click in front of the page number field, type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> and enter a space; click after the field, enter a space and then type \<item type=\"literal\"\>of\</item\> and enter another space.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footer_pagenumber.xhp	0	help	par_id3155554				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Page Numbers 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	bm_id5918759				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>page numbers;inserting/defining/formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles;page numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;starting page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>styles;page numbers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id413830				0	sk	\<variable id=\"pagenumbers\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagenumbers.xhp\" name=\"Page Numbers\"\>Page Numbers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1617175				0	sk	In Writer, a page number is a field that you can insert into your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id6091494				0	sk	To Insert Page Numbers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id8611102				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Page Number\</emph\> to insert a page number at the current cursor position.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6604510				0	sk	If you see the text "Page number" instead of the number, choose \<emph\>View - Field names\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2678914				0	sk	However, these fields will change position when you add or remove text. So it is best to insert the page number field into a header or footer that has the same position and that is repeated on every page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id614642				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header - (name of page style)\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer - (name of page style)\</item\> to add a header or footer to all pages with the current page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id2551652				0	sk	To Start With a Defined Page Number				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6111941				0	sk	Now you want some more control on page numbers. You are writing a text document that should start with page number 12.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5757621				0	sk	Click into the first paragraph of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2632831				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph - Text flow\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4395275				0	sk	In the Breaks area, enable \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>. Enable \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\> just to be able to set the new \<emph\>Page number\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1654408				0	sk	The new page number is an attribute of the first paragraph of the page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id7519150				0	sk	To Format the Page Number Style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9029206				0	sk	You want roman page numbers running i, ii, iii, iv, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3032319				0	sk	Double-click directly before the page number field. You see the \<emph\>Edit Fields\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id9139378				0	sk	Select a number format and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5051728				0	sk	Using Different Page Number Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1558885				0	sk	You need some pages with the roman numbering style, followed by the remaining pages in another style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1541184				0	sk	In Writer, you will need different page styles. The first page style has a footer with a page number field formatted for roman numbers. The following page style has a footer with a page number field formatted in another look.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id18616				0	sk	Both page styles must be separated by a page break. In Writer, you can have automatic page breaks and manually inserted page breaks.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id6138492				0	sk	An \<emph\>automatic page break\</emph\> appears at the end of a page when the page style has a different "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4569231				0	sk	For example, the "First Page" page style has "Default" as the next style. To see this, you may press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Styles and Formatting\</item\> window, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> icon, right-click the First Page entry. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Modify\</item\> from the context menu. On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab, you can see the "next style".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id291451				0	sk	A \<emph\>manually inserted page break\</emph\> can be applied without or with a change of page styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3341776				0	sk	If you just press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\>, you apply a page break without a change of styles.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id5947141				0	sk	If you choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual break\</emph\>, you can insert a page break without or with a change of style or with a change of page number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id1911679				0	sk	It depends on your document what is best: to use a manually inserted page break between page styles, or to use an automatic change. If you just need one title page with a different style than the other pages, you can use the automatic method:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id9364909				0	sk	To Apply a Different Page Style to the First Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4473403				0	sk	Click into the first page of your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4313791				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4331797				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id4191717				0	sk	Double-click the "First Page" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id2318796				0	sk	Now your title page has the style "First Page", and the next pages automatically have the "Default" style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id399182				0	sk	You can now for example insert a footer for the "Default" page atyle only, or insert footers in both page styles, but with differently formatted page number fields.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	hd_id5298318				0	sk	To Apply a Manually Inserted Page Style Change				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7588732				0	sk	Click at the start of the first paragraph on the page where a different page style will be applied.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id95828				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>. You see the \<emph\>Insert Break\</emph\> dialog.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3496200				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list box, select a page style. You may set a new page number, too. Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagenumbers.xhp	0	help	par_id7599108				0	sk	The selected page style will be used from the current paragraph to the next page break with style. You may need to create the new page style first.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Changing Page Backgrounds				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	bm_id8431653				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>backgrounds; different pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;page backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;backgrounds\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	sk	\<variable id=\"pagebackground\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp\"\>Changing Page Background\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10812				0	sk	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the background of the pages in a document. For example, to change the page background of one or more pages in a document to a watermark, you need to create a page style that uses the watermark background, and then apply the page style to the pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10820				0	sk	To Change the Page Background				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10827				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082F				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10837				0	sk	In the list of page styles, right-click an item, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1083F				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1084B				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10855				0	sk	To only apply the new page style to a single page, select "Default".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10859				0	sk	To apply the new page style to all subsequent pages, select the name of the new page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1085F				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10867				0	sk	In the list box at the top, select whether you want a solid color or a graphic. Then select your options from the tab page. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1086B				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087A				0	sk	To Change the Page Background of All Pages in a Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1087E				0	sk	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN10892				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN1089A				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A2				0	sk	Double-click the page style that uses the page background that you want to apply.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A5				0	sk	To Use Different Page Backgrounds in the Same Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A9				0	sk	Before you begin, ensure that you have created a page style that uses a page background. See \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pagebackground.xhp#define\"\>To Change the Page Background\</link\> for details.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108BD				0	sk	Click in front of the first character of the paragraph where you want to change the page background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C1				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108C9				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Page break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108D1				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box, select a page style that uses the page background.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pagebackground.xhp	0	help	par_idN108DB				0	sk	To change the background of the current page only, select a page style where the Next Style option is set to "Default".				20200411 15:09:53
