helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149487				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>text frames; inserting/editing/linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>resizing;text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scaling; text frames, by mouse\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;text frames\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text flow; from frame to frame\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>frames; linking\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;hiding text frames from printing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149487				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_frame\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_frame.xhp\" name=\"Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\"\>Inserting, Editing, and Linking Text Frames\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149842				0	sk	A text frame is a container for text and graphics that you can place anywhere on a page. You can also use a frame to apply a column layout to text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156104				0	sk	To Insert a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149961				0	sk	Select the text that you want to include in the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149602				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Frame\</emph\>, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145115				0	sk	To Edit a Text Frame				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578				0	sk	To edit the contents of a text frame, click in the frame, and make the changes that you want.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156239				0	sk	To edit a frame, select the frame, right-click, and then choose a formatting option. You can also right-click the selected frame, and choose \<emph\>Frame\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3156261				0	sk	To resize a text frame, click an edge of the frame, and drag one of the edges or corners of the frame. Hold down Shift while you drag to maintain the proportion of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153386				0	sk	To Hide Text From Printing				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154262				0	sk	Any Writer text frame can be set to a mode which allows viewing the text on screen, but hides the text from printing.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154858				0	sk	Select the text frame (you see the eight handles).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155875				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Frame/Object - Options\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3155899				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Properties\</emph\> area, unmark the \<emph\>Print\</emph\> check box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148701				0	sk	To Link Text Frames				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3149986				0	sk	You can link Writer text frames so that their contents automatically flow from one frame to another.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3153025				0	sk	Click the edge of a frame that you want to link. Selection handles appear on the edges of the frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150223	87			0	sk	On the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Frame\</item\> Bar, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Link Frames\</item\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3148968\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_chainframes.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148968\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150930				0	sk	Click the frame that you want to link to.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150947				0	sk	You can only link frames if:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3150969				0	sk	The target frame is empty.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365				0	sk	The target frame is not linked to another frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3154383				0	sk	The source and the target frames are in the same section. For example, you cannot link a header frame to a footer frame.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145559				0	sk	The source frame does not have a next link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3145577				0	sk	The target or the source frame are not contained in each other.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id3151083				0	sk	When you select a linked frame, a line is displayed that connects the linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_frame.xhp	0	help	par_id5853144				0	sk	The AutoSize feature is available only for the last frame in a chain of linked frames.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Formatting Headers or Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;lines under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866				0	sk	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243				0	sk	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\> and select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109				0	sk	Set the spacing options that you want to use.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128				0	sk	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More\</item\>. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Border/Background\</item\> dialog opens.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520				0	sk	To add a separator line between the header or the footer and the content of the page, click the bottom edge of the square in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area. Click a line style in the \<emph\>Style\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3153742	25			0	sk	To adjust the spacing between the content of the header or footer and the line, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> box, and then enter a value in the\<emph\> Bottom\</emph\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\subscript.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Making Text Superscript or Subscript				20200411 15:09:53
