helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154265				0	sk	\<variable id=\"auto_spellcheck\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/auto_spellcheck.xhp\" name=\"Automatically Check Spelling\"\>Automatically Check Spelling\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3154664				0	sk	You can have $[officename] automatically check spelling while you type and underline possible misspelt words with a red wavy line.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154678				0	sk	To Check Spelling Automatically While You Type				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155531	42			0	sk	Activate the \<emph\>AutoSpellcheck \</emph\>icon on the Standard bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3155569	33			0	sk	Right-click a word with a red wavy underline, and then choose a suggested replacement word from the list, or from the \<emph\>AutoCorrect \</emph\>submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	6			0	sk	If you choose a word from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>AutoCorrect\</item\> submenu, the underlined word and the replacement word are automatically added to the AutoCorrect list for the current language. To view the AutoCorrect list, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Replace\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147819				0	sk	You can also add the underlined word to your custom dictionary by choosing \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147220				0	sk	To Exclude Words From the Spellcheck				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147263				0	sk	Select the words that you want to exclude.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3147282				0	sk	Click the Language control on the Status bar to open a menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145602				0	sk	Choose “None (Do not check spelling)”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\auto_spellcheck.xhp	0	help	par_id3145648				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01010401.xhp\" name=\"Creating a new dictionary.\"\>Creating a new dictionary.\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Changing Page Orientation (Landscape or Portrait)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	bm_id9683828				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>page styles;orientation/scope\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page formats; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formatting; changing individual pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>portrait and landscape\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>landscape and portrait\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing;portrait/landscape format\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paper orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>pages;orientation\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sideways orientation of pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>scope of page styles\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN106FF				0	sk	\<variable id=\"pageorientation\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/pageorientation.xhp\"\>Changing Page Orientation\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6418042				0	sk	All page properties for Writer text documents, like for example the page orientation, are defined by page styles. By default, a new text document uses the “Default” page style for all pages. If you open an existing text document, different page styles may have been applied to the different pages. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id8324533				0	sk	It is important to know that changes that you apply to a page property will only affect the pages that use the current page style. The current page style is listed in the Status Bar at the lower window border.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7524033				0	sk	To Change the Page Orientation for All Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6307260				0	sk	If your text document consists only of pages with the same page style, you can change the page properties directly:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5256508				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9681997				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7994323				0	sk	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id7069002				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id4202398				0	sk	To Change the Page Orientation Only for Some Pages				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1071D				0	sk	$[officename] uses page styles to specify the orientation of the pages in a document. Page styles define more page properties, as for example header and footer or page margins. You can either change the “Default” page style for the current document, or you can define own page styles and apply those page styles to any parts of your text. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1449324				0	sk	At the end of this help page, we'll discuss the scope of page styles in detail. If you are unsure about the page style concept, please read the section at the end of this page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1480758				0	sk	Unlike character styles or paragraph styles, the page styles don't know a hierarchy. You can create a new page style based on the properties of an existing page style, but when you later change the source style, the new page style does not automatically inherit the changes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2962126				0	sk	To change the page orientation for all pages that share the same page style, you first need a page style, then apply that style:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10727				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10741				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10749				0	sk	Right-click a page style and choose \<emph\>New\</emph\>. The new page style initially gets all properties of the selected page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10751				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Organizer\</emph\> tab page, type a name for the page style in the \<emph\>Name\</emph\> box, for example "My Landscape".				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1075D				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Next Style\</emph\> box, select the page style that you want to apply to the next page that follows a page with the new style. See the section about the scope of page styles at the end of this help page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN10775				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Page\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN1077D				0	sk	Under \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paper format\</item\>, select “Portrait” or “Landscape”.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AE				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1658375				0	sk	Now you have defined a proper page style with the name "My Landscape". To apply the new style, double-click the "My Landscape" page style in the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window. All pages in the current scope of page styles will be changed. If you defined the "next style" to be a different style, only the first page of the current scope of page styles will be changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id6082949				0	sk	The Scope of Page Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2858668				0	sk	You should be aware of the scope of page styles in %PRODUCTNAME. Which pages of your text document get affected by editing a page style?				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id3278603				0	sk	One Page Long Styles				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id5169225				0	sk	A page style can be defined to span one page only. The “First Page” style is an example. You set this property by defining another page style to be the "next style", on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6670125				0	sk	A one page long style starts from the lower border of the current page style range up to the next page break. The next page break appears automatically when the text flows to the next page, which is sometimes called a "soft page break". Alternatively, you can insert a manual page break.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id2118594				0	sk	To insert a manual page break at the cursor position, press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Ctrl+Enter\</item\> or choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\> and just click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	hd_id166020				0	sk	Manually Defined Range of a Page style				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6386913				0	sk	The “Default” page style does not set a different "next style" on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page - Organizer\</item\> tab page. Instead, the "next style" is set also to be “Default”. All page styles that are followed by the same page style can span multiple pages. The lower and upper borders of the page style range are defined by "page breaks with style". All the pages between any two "page breaks with style" use the same page style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6062196				0	sk	You can insert a "page break with style" directly at the cursor position. Alternatively, you can apply the "page break with style" property to a paragraph or to a paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id6054261				0	sk	Perform any one of the following commands:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id1811578				0	sk	To insert a "page break with style" at the cursor position, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Manual Break\</item\>, select a \<emph\>Style\</emph\> name from the listbox, and click OK.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id9935911				0	sk	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Paragraph - Text Flow\</item\>. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4753868				0	sk	To apply the "page break with style" property to the current paragraph style, right-click the current paragraph. Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit Paragraph Style\</item\> from the context menu. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\pageorientation.xhp	0	help	par_id4744407				0	sk	To apply the "page break with style" property to an arbitrary paragraph style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</item\>. Click the \<emph\>Paragraph Styles\</emph\> icon. Right-click the name of the paragraph style you want to modify and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>. Click the \<emph\>Text Flow\</emph\> tab. In the Breaks area, activate \<emph\>Enable\</emph\> and \<emph\>With Page Style\</emph\>. Select a page style name from the listbox.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875				0	sk	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584				0	sk	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245				0	sk	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503				0	sk	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153				0	sk	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	sk	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572				0	sk	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Manual Break\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	sk	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845				0	sk	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858				0	sk	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833				0	sk	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846				0	sk	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	sk	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\> is selected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396				0	sk	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416				0	sk	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133				0	sk	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635				0	sk	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				20200411 15:09:53
