helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155182				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>characters; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; uppercase or lowercase\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lowercase letters; text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>uppercase; formatting text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>capital letters;changing to small letters\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;cases of text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>initial capitals in titles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>small capitals (guide)\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155182				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_capital\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_capital.xhp\" name=\"Changing the Case of Text\"\>Changing the Case of Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3155916				0	sk	You can change the case of text, format text with small capitals, or capitalize the first letter of each word in a selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_idN10728				0	sk	When you apply a formatting to your text by \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, the text stays the same, it is only displayed in another way. On the other hand, when you choose \<emph\>Format - Change Case\</emph\>, the text is permanently changed.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155861				0	sk	To Capitalize Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3147420				0	sk	Select the text that you want to capitalize.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149841				0	sk	Vykonajte jednu z nasledujúcich možností:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485778				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Uppercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910485775				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select the type of capitalization in the Effects box. "Capitals" capitalizes all letters. "Title" capitalizes the first letter of each word. "Small capitals" capitalizes all letters, but in a reduced font size.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149644				0	sk	To Change Text to Lowercase				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149964				0	sk	Select the text that you want to change to lowercase.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id3149606				0	sk	Vykonajte jednu z nasledujúcich možností:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id112020091049000				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Change Case - Lowercase\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_capital.xhp	0	help	par_id1120200910490034				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Character\</item\>, click the Font Effects tab, then select "Lowercase" in the Effects box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	About Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145576				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>fields;updating/viewing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>updating;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Help tips;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>properties;fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>disabling;field highlighting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>changing;field shadings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>viewing;fields\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145576				0	sk	\<variable id=\"fields\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/fields.xhp\" name=\"About Fields\"\>About Fields\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3154246				0	sk	Fields are used for data that changes in a document, such as the current date or the total number of pages in a document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154262				0	sk	Viewing Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150509				0	sk	Fields consist of a field name and the field content. To switch the field display between the field name or the field content, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/03090000.xhp\" name=\"View - Fields\"\>\<emph\>View - Field Names\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536				0	sk	To display or hide field highlighting in a document, choose \<emph\>View - Field Shadings\</emph\>. To permanently disable this feature, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - Appearance\</emph\>, and clear the check box in front of \<emph\>Field shadings\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3152885				0	sk	To change the color of field shadings, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - \<link href=\"text/shared/optionen/01012000.xhp\" name=\"$[officename] - Appearance\"\>\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>$[officename] - Appearance\</item\>\</link\>\</emph\>, locate the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Field shadings\</item\> option, and then select a different color in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color setting\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153166				0	sk	Vlastnosti poľa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3153180				0	sk	Most field types in a document, including database fields, store and display variable values.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155533				0	sk	The following field types execute an action when you click the field:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582				0	sk	Typ poľa				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147760				0	sk	Vlastnosť				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147789				0	sk	Zástupný znak				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147812				0	sk	Opens a dialog to insert the object for which the placeholder was set.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147216				0	sk	Vložiť referenciu				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147239				0	sk	Moves the mouse pointer to the reference.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147267				0	sk	Spustiť makro				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3147290				0	sk	Runs a macro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145614				0	sk	Vstupné pole				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3145637				0	sk	Opens a dialog to edit the contents of the field.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3151244				0	sk	Placeholder, hidden text, insert reference, variable, database, and user-defined fields display a help tip when you rest the mouse pointer over the field in a document. To enable this feature, ensure that the Extended Tips option (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>What's This?\</item\>) is selected in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Help\</item\> menu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155937				0	sk	Updating Fields				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155963				0	sk	To update all of the fields in a document, press F9, or choose \<emph\>Edit - Select All\</emph\>, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\fields.xhp	0	help	par_id3155984				0	sk	To update a field that was inserted from a database, select the field, and then press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	About Headers and Footers				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863				0	sk	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255				0	sk	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511				0	sk	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896				0	sk	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119				0	sk	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726				0	sk	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\> tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876				0	sk	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704				0	sk	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	sk	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153899				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>calculating;in text tables\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; performing calculations in\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153899				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calculate_intext2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_intext2.xhp\" name=\"Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\"\>Displaying the Result of a Table Calculation in a Different Table\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	sk	You can perform a calculation on cells in one table and display the result in a different table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	sk	Open a text document, insert a table with multiple columns and rows, and then insert another table consisting of one cell.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150528				0	sk	Enter numbers into some of the cells of the large table.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155532				0	sk	Place the cursor in the table with the single cell, and then press F2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155551				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Formula Bar\</item\>, enter the function that you want to perform, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>=SUM\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155577				0	sk	Click in a cell in the larger table that contains a number, press the plus sign (+), and then click in a different cell containing a number.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155598				0	sk	Press \<emph\>Enter\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_intext2.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	sk	If you want, you can format the table to behave as normal text. Insert the table into a frame, and then anchor the frame as a character. The frame remains anchored to the adjacent text when you insert or delete text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting an Entire Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155185				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>sections;inserting external content\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;merging\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>links;inserting text documents as\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155185				0	sk	\<variable id=\"textdoc_inframe\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/textdoc_inframe.xhp\" name=\"Inserting an Entire Text Document\"\>Inserting an Entire Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id1812799				0	sk	To Insert a Text File				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3155855				0	sk	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - File\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149839				0	sk	Locate the text document that you want to insert, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3148858				0	sk	The contents of the text document are embedded into the current document and are not updated if the source file is changed. If you want the contents to automatically update when you change the source document, insert the file as a link.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156105				0	sk	To Insert an Entire Text Document as a Link				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3150096				0	sk	Place the cursor in the document where you want to insert the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153404				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Section\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3153127				0	sk	Type a name in the \<emph\>New Section\</emph\> box, and then select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149642				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>File Name\</item\> box, type the name of the file that you want to insert, or click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and locate the file.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149968				0	sk	If the target text document contains sections, you can select the section that you want to insert in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Sections\</item\> box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149619				0	sk	If you want, set the formatting options for the section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3149862				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\textdoc_inframe.xhp	0	help	par_id3145099				0	sk	$[officename] automatically updates the contents of the inserted section whenever the source document is changed. To manually update the contents of the section, choose \<emph\>Tools - Update - Update All\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Printing in Reverse Order				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149688				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>ordering;printing in reverse order\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>printing; reverse order\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149688				0	sk	\<variable id=\"printing_order\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/printing_order.xhp\" name=\"Printing in Reverse Order\"\>Printing in Reverse Order\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3155854				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>File - Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149836				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Options\</emph\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3156106				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Print in reverse page order\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Print\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\printing_order.xhp	0	help	par_id3149616				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/01130000.xhp\" name=\"Printing\"\>Printing\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619				0	sk	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879				0	sk	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895				0	sk	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175				0	sk	To Define a Conditional Variable				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	sk	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759				0	sk	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784				0	sk	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810				0	sk	Click "Text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	sk	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645				0	sk	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659				0	sk	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193				0	sk	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212				0	sk	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250				0	sk	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936				0	sk	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969				0	sk	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446				0	sk	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473				0	sk	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073				0	sk	To Display the Conditional Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086				0	sk	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110				0	sk	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136				0	sk	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box with 3, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168				0	sk	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Emphasizing Text				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149820				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>text; emphasizing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>emphasizing text\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149820				0	sk	\<variable id=\"text_emphasize\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/text_emphasize.xhp\" name=\"Emphasizing Text\"\>Emphasizing Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155922				0	sk	Here are a few examples of how to emphasize text in a document:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	sk	Select the text and apply a different font style or effect, such as \<emph\>bold\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149840	68			0	sk	Right-click in a paragraph, choose \<emph\>Paragraph, \</emph\>set the options that you want, for example, the background color, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id3150084				0	sk	Select the text, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Frame\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_id6924649				0	sk	Use the Text tool on the Drawing toolbar. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\text_emphasize.xhp	0	help	par_idN106E7				0	sk	Use Fontwork. To open the Fontwork window, click the Fontwork Gallery icon on the Drawing bar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147692				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>pasting;results of formulas\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>clipboard;calculating in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>formulas;pasting results in text documents\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147692				0	sk	\<variable id=\"calculate_clipboard\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/calculate_clipboard.xhp\" name=\" Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\"\> Calculating and Pasting the Result of a Formula in a Text Document\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3156366				0	sk	If your text already contains a formula, for example "12+24*2", $[officename] can calculate, and then paste the result of the formula in your document, without using the \<emph\>Formula Bar\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3154250				0	sk	Select the formula in the text. The formula can only contain numbers and operators and cannot contain spaces.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3155496	38			0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Calculate\</emph\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Plus Sign (+).				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\calculate_clipboard.xhp	0	help	par_id5172582				0	sk	Place the cursor where you want to insert the result of the formula, and then choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Edit - Paste\</item\>, or press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+V.\<br/\>The selected formula is replaced by the result.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145819				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>endnotes;inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>editing;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>organizing;footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; inserting and editing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145819				0	sk	\<variable id=\"footnote_usage\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_usage.xhp\" name=\"Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\"\>Inserting and Editing Footnotes or Endnotes\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258				0	sk	Footnotes reference more information about a topic at the bottom of a page and endnotes reference information at the end of the document. $[officename] automatically numbers the footnotes and endnotes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155881				0	sk	To Insert a Footnote or Endnote				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155903				0	sk	Click in your document where you want to place the anchor of the note.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147120				0	sk	Choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04030000.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Insert - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150937				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\> area, select the format that you want to use. If you select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Character\</item\>, click the browse button (\<item type=\"menuitem\"\>...\</item\>) and select the character that you want to use for the footnote.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150508				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footnote\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Endnote\</item\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150704				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150729				0	sk	Type the note.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3148843				0	sk	\<image id=\"img_id3148857\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_insertfootnote.png\" width=\"0.222in\" height=\"0.222in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3148857\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3153176				0	sk	You can also insert footnotes by clicking the \<emph\>Insert Footnote Directly\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155543				0	sk	To Edit a Footnote or Endnote				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3150167				0	sk	The mouse pointer changes to a hand when you rest it over a footnote or endnote anchor in your document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3155563				0	sk	To edit the text of a footnote or endnote, click in the note, or click the anchor for the note in the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145029				0	sk	To change the format of a footnote, click in the footnote, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command+T\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>F11\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> to open the Styles and Formatting window, right-click "Footnote" in the list, and then choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145062				0	sk	To jump from the footnote or endnote text to the note anchor in the text, press PageUp.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3145081				0	sk	To edit the numbering properties of a footnote or endnote anchor, click in front of the anchor, and choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02150000.xhp\" name=\"Edit - Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Edit - Footnote/Endnote\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147776				0	sk	To change the formatting that $[officename] applies to footnotes and endnotes, choose \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/06080000.xhp\" name=\"Tools - Footnotes\"\>\<emph\>Tools - Footnotes/Endnotes\</emph\>\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147813				0	sk	To edit the properties of the text area for footnotes or endnotes, choose \<emph\>Format - Page\</emph\>, and then click the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05040600.xhp\" name=\"Footnote\"\>\<emph\>Footnote\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_usage.xhp	0	help	par_id3147232				0	sk	To remove a footnote, delete the footnote anchor in the text.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148882				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>settings;word completion\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>word completion;settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text documents;word completion settings\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>weekdays; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>months; automatically completing\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	hd_id4745017				0	sk	\<variable id=\"word_completion_adjust\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion_adjust.xhp\"\>Fine-Tuning the Word Completion for Text Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id4814294				0	sk	If you like it that $[officename] automatically completes the words that you frequently use, you can make further adjustments to refine that behavior. If you want, you can also save the current list of collected words so that it can be used in the next session.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2593462				0	sk	To fine-tune the word completion choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools – AutoCorrect Options - Word Completion\</item\> and select any of the following options:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107C6				0	sk	To Insert an Additional Space Character				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B03				0	sk	Select \<emph\>Append space\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B0E				0	sk	The space character is appended after you type the first character of the next word after the auto-completed word. The space character is suppressed if the next character is a delimiter, such as a full stop or a new line character.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CC				0	sk	To Define the Accept Key				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B20				0	sk	Choose the key to accept the suggested word using the \<emph\>Accept with\</emph\> list box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D2				0	sk	To Select the Minimum Number of Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B36				0	sk	Use the \<emph\>Min. word length\</emph\> box to set the minimum number of characters a word must have to be collected into the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D8				0	sk	To Select the Scope of Collected Words				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B4C				0	sk	Disable the option \<emph\>When closing a document, remove the words collected from it from the list\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B53				0	sk	Now the list is also valid for other documents that you open. When you close the last %PRODUCTNAME document, the word list is deleted.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B56				0	sk	If you enable the checkbox, the list is only valid as long as the current document is open.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id2634968				0	sk	If you want the word list to exist longer than the current %PRODUCTNAME session, save it as a document, as described in the following section.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107DE				0	sk	To Use the Word List for Further Sessions				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10B94				0	sk	If the automatic spellcheck option is enabled, only the words that are recognized by the spellcheck are collected.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA1				0	sk	Use the word list to always start with a defined set of technical terms for the word completion feature.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BA7				0	sk	Open the text document that contains the terms that you want to use for word completion.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BAB				0	sk	The word completion feature collects the words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107ED				0	sk	Select all or some of the words in the list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN107F4				0	sk	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+C to copy all selected words into the clipboard. Paste the clipboard into a new document and save it to get a reference list of collected words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10BC6				0	sk	Later you can open the reference list and automatically collect the words, so that the word completion feature starts with a defined set of words.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_idN10809				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/06040600.xhp\"\>Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\word_completion_adjust.xhp	0	help	par_id5458845				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/word_completion.xhp\"\>Using Word Completion\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156377				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>rows; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>columns; inserting/deleting in tables by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>tables; editing by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>keyboard;adding or deleting rows/columns\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>splitting cells;by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>merging;cells, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting;rows/columns, by keyboard\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156377				0	sk	\<variable id=\"table_cells\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/table_cells.xhp\" name=\"Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\"\>Adding or Deleting a Row or Column to a Table Using the Keyboard\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149487				0	sk	You can add or delete rows or columns in tables as well as split or merge table cells using the keyboard.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3155906				0	sk	To insert a new row in a table, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the up or down arrow key. You can also move the cursor to the last cell in the table, and then press Tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3147412				0	sk	To insert a new column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then press the left or right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3156096				0	sk	To split a table cell instead of adding a column, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Insert, and then hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while you press the left or right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3153408				0	sk	To delete a row, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the up or down arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149626				0	sk	To delete a column, place the cursor in a table cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\table_cells.xhp	0	help	par_id3149612				0	sk	To merge a table into an adjacent cell, place the cursor in the cell, press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Delete, hold down \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, and then press the left or the right arrow key.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	sk	Spacing Between Footnotes				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147683				0	sk	\<bookmark_value\>spacing; endnotes/footnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>endnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footnotes; spacing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines;footnotes/endnotes\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147683				0	sk	\<variable id=\"footnote_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/footnote_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Rozostupy medzi poznámkami pod čiarou\"\>Rozostupy medzi poznámkami pod čiarou>\</link\>\</variable\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3145808				0	sk	If you want to increase the spacing between footnote or endnote texts, you can add a top and bottom border to the corresponding paragraph style.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155603				0	sk	Click in a footnote or endnote.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155620				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154251				0	sk	Right-click the Paragraph Style that you want to modify, for example, "Footnote", and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155884				0	sk	Click the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05030500.xhp\" name=\"Borders\"\>\<emph\>Borders\</emph\>\</link\> tab.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147110				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Default\</item\> area, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Set Top and Bottom Borders Only\</item\> icon.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931				0	sk	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Line\</item\> area, click a line in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\> list.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150961				0	sk	Select "White" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Color\</item\> box. If the background of the page is not white, select the color that best matches the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150519				0	sk	In the \<emph\>Spacing to contents\</emph\> area, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> check box.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150709				0	sk	Enter a value in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Top\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Bottom\</item\> boxes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\footnote_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150740				0	sk	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
