helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id7355265				0	sk	You can define a background color or use a graphic as a background for various objects in $[officename] Writer.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147653				0	sk	To Apply a Background To Text Characters				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150669				0	sk	Select the characters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3155390				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665				0	sk	Click the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab, select the background color.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153541				0	sk	To Apply a Background To a Paragraph				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3145119				0	sk	Place the cursor in the paragraph or select several paragraphs.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3158430				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Format - Paragraph\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3151245				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id0104201010554939				0	sk	To select an object in the background, hold down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key and click the object. Alternatively, use the Navigator to select the object.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149294				0	sk	To Apply a Background To All or Part of a Table				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154346				0	sk	Place the cursor in the table in your text document.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3148664				0	sk	Choose \<emph\>Table - Table Properties\</emph\>.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938				0	sk	On the \<emph\>Background\</emph\> tab page, select the background color or a background graphic.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3156280				0	sk	In the \<emph\>For\</emph\> box, choose whether the color or graphic should apply to the current cell, the current row or the whole table. If you select several cells or rows before opening the dialog, the change applies to the selection.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151041				0	sk	You may also use an icon to apply a background to table parts.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3150767				0	sk	To apply a background color to cells, select the cells and click the color on the \<emph\>Background Color\</emph\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_id3147084				0	sk	To apply a background color to a text paragraph within a cell, place the cursor into the text paragraph, then click the color on the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Background Color\</item\> toolbar.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\background.xhp	0	help	par_idN10A56				0	sk	\<link href=\"text/shared/02/02160000.xhp\"\>Highlighting icon\</link\>				20200411 15:09:53
