helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3083450				0	sk	\<ahelp hid=\".uno:UnsetCellsReadOnly\"\>Removes the cell protection for all selected cells in the current table.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3154558	3			0	sk	To remove the protection from several tables at once, select the tables, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T. To remove the protection from all of the tables in a document, click anywhere in the document, and then press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command \</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Shift+T.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\05100400.xhp	0	help	par_id3150765				0	sk	You can also remove cell protection from a table in the \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/02110000.xhp\" name=\"Navigator\"\>Navigator\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
